Kandal Provincial Authority Suspends Excavation Business After Finding Offenses of Mining and Overweight Transportation
(Kandal): Kandal provincial authorities have temporarily suspended a mining business owned by Ratha after being found guilty of illegal mining and overweight transportation. This location is in Ancheng Krom village, Puk Russey commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province.
When leading the joint force to suspend the above business on January 19, 2022, Mr. Nop Dara, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province, requested Mr. Ratha to collect the relevant documents and present to the joint working group, and the offending vehicle must be kept at the inspector. Khsach Kandal District Police Station.
At the same time, the deputy governor asked the pit business owners and truck drivers to respect the road traffic law, road law and other legal standards. Transportation must be properly covered with tents to avoid falling on the road that could cause accidents.
He also requested the relevant departments, especially the Department of Areas and Energy and the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kandal Province to cooperate with the owners of the Moharatha Trading Pit to implement the procedure and requested the owners of the mines to cooperate with the joint provincial working group. Relevant documents shall be presented to the working group within 15 days from the date of this inspection.
After a thorough inspection, the joint team found that four vehicles transported out of the Maharajah trading pit were overloaded, causing some road damage, and the driver acknowledged that Its car is really overweight.
In that, the representative of Moha Ratha Trading Pit showed insufficient license related to the actual excavation of land with a size of about 15 hectares at the reservoir to collect tigers in Anchreng Krom village, Pok Russey commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province.
After a thorough inspection, the joint provincial working group decided to temporarily suspend the excavation and transport of the land, storing two machines and four vehicles that violated the mining business and four vehicles that were overweight.
In a telephone conversation with Indonesian President Joko Widodo on Friday morning, January 21, 2022, the Prime Minister sent a message to the Indonesian Foreign Minister requesting the Indonesian Foreign Minister to send his message to the Minister of Foreign Affairs. Foreigner Malaysia. This is according to Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, told Fresh News after the meeting.
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn emphasized that "Samdech Techo Prime Minister emphasized that although the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Malaysia has worked in the framework of the opposition in the past, but he should not be a Minister of Foreign Affairs and a diplomat. "One of them used arrogant words with the ASEAN chair as well as the head of the ASEAN government, who did not use diplomatic language at all."
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn quoted Samdech Techo, who spoke with the President of Indonesia, stated that "Samdech Techo Prime Minister's visit to Myanmar on January 7-8 was to plant trees, not to cut down trees. . "And planting this tree is not a one-day planting and expects to bear fruit immediately, because it takes time. A long-term political solution is to take time and work hard."
According to Kao Kim Hourn, during the meeting, Samdech Techo told the Indonesian president that the Malaysian foreign minister did not understand the art of diplomacy.
According to Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, during the bilateral meeting, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also mentioned that the visit to Myanmar was an immediate trip and also got some results. The outcome of the visit is an agreement to end violence and shootings by the end of 2022 and to provide humanitarian assistance to the people of Myanmar in need.
During the meeting, the Prime Minister and the President of Indonesia discussed the establishment of an "ASEAN-Triad" mechanism to address Myanmar and Indonesia's initiative to establish an observer mission using ASEAN embassy officials in Yangon. .
Regarding this mechanism, the Prime Minister requested the ASEAN Foreign Ministers to meet in the future to discuss and find ways to promote this work.
The President of Indonesia considers that what he has done and is pushing for a solution to the crisis in Myanmar is beneficial, but must continue to implement the five principles of unanimity decided by the ASEAN Heads of Government to urge the Myanmar side to implement the five plans.
Joko Widodo also said that all solutions must be attended by all parties, as the prince has said, that national unity to find a solution must involve all parties.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to Myanmar on January 7-8, 2022, despite being seen as a strong Cambodian effort to solve the problems of Myanmar and ASEAN. The visit drew a small amount of criticism from commentators, including Malaysian Foreign Minister Saifuddin Abdullah.
Responding to the criticism, Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong, one of Cambodia's most talented former diplomats, explained that there was nothing wrong with Hun Sen's visit to Myanmar. The Deputy Prime Minister called the visit a step towards resolving Myanmar's problems based on the five principles of consensus.
Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong also attacked critics of Samdech Techo's visit for not understanding and not reading these five unanimous principles.
The Deputy Prime Minister said, "I understand that the criticism of Samdech in the past through the media in the units of ASEAN politicians seems to have forgotten the meaning of these five points. "They seem to have forgotten the connection from point one to point five. They do not seem to understand the logic of these five points."
The former Cambodian diplomat continued, "I think this visit is the right one to help Myanmar, which is an ASEAN issue. Since Cambodia is the chair of ASEAN in 2022, Cambodia must take the first step to resolve this issue on the basis of five points of consensus." "
The Deputy Prime Minister also praised Samdech Techo Hun Sen's initiative to establish a tripartite mechanism (Troika) consisting of Cambodia, Brunei and Indonesia to solve Myanmar's problems. The Deputy Prime Minister said that the Myanmar issue is an issue that cannot be resolved in the short term, so this tripartite mechanism is a long-term mechanism for resolving the Myanmar issue towards success.
"Creating a triad is the best initiative to come together. The problem of Myanmar is not the problem of Cambodia, it is the problem of ASEAN, so Samdech Techo, the chair of ASEAN, took the first step to solve these five points. There is nothing wrong. This was confirmed by Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong.
The crisis has dragged on for about a year, until Myanmar did not attend ASEAN meetings in 2021. Myanmar's absence from ASEAN was considered by Samdech Techo Hun Sen as a split of ASEAN.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, expressed his strong intention to solve Myanmar's problems, especially to bring Myanmar to the ASEAN Forum. At the beginning of January 2022, just became the chair of ASEAN, Samdech Techo Hun Sen traveled to Myanmar.
In response to Cambodia's request, Myanmar's military leader Ong Minglang agreed to postpone the shooting with stakeholders in the country. The military leader agreed to facilitate the special envoy of the ASEAN chair to hold talks with the parties to the conflict in Myanmar and to facilitate the provision of assistance to the people of Myanmar on all sides.
The results of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit are seen as a step and a light in resolving the crisis in Myanmar. Many countries have supported this result.
