China-US flights may face total shutdown in February
The Civil Aviation Administration of China (CAAC), the Chinese civil aviation regulator, announced the suspension of eight more domestic flights from three US airlines this week.
The latest flight cancellation has led to a total of 84 flights being canceled this year, Reuters reported.
The three US airlines have already faced frequent flight cancellations within four to six weeks due to the discovery of Kovid-19 disease on passengers. It is also possible that these airlines are more likely to face a nationwide flight suspension in February.
A new type of virus, Omikrong, is putting increasing pressure on flights into China.
Since January 1, the CAAC has canceled more than 100 international flights to China due to the import of Kovid-19, bringing the total number of flights canceled to more than 200.
