Mr. Theng Sothol, Governor of Chamkar Mon District, said that Chamkar Mon District covers an area of 7.15 square kilometers, has 5 communes, 38 villages, a total population of 47,53 people, about 9442 families and a density of 6,606. People per square meter.
For the construction management, a monitoring mechanism was set up for the garbage collection agency, including the signing of a contract between the five district governors. And strengthen garbage collection services during various festivals. In addition, a total of 152 bins were installed in the parks and 3 7-ton garbage bins were installed in the markets.
Mr. Theng Sothol added that in the field of education and outreach, he cooperated with the Phnom Penh Capital Administration and relevant ministries in conducting outreach campaigns with the participation of monks, students and youths of the CPP and youth scouts to clean up garbage in the parks. And the streets after the Water Festival.
For the implementation of the fine mechanism, the district administration has put up billboards on education, fines, as defined by law, such as along sewer 105 in the two markets in the district and the main public parks, and has also set up fine agencies in the five communes. .
