South Korea suspects North Korea is preparing for a military parade
SEOUL (Reuters) - The South Korean military on Thursday said it had signaled that North Korea was preparing for a military parade ahead of two major political events in the country. This was released by Yonhap News Agency on Thursday evening, January 20, 2022.
According to Yonhap, North Korea plans to celebrate the birthdays of two former North Korean leaders, Kim Jong Un's biological father, Kim Jong Il, on February 16 and his biological grandfather. Mr. Kim Il Sung on April 15, 2022.
Also on Thursday, North Korea's KCNA reported that Pyongyang would resume all activities that had been suspended in the past. The announcement is likely to refer to the re-testing of nuclear weapons and intercontinental ballistic missiles (ICBMs) after being suspended since late 2017.
