At the same time, he would like to express his condolences to the families of the victims and support the three young children who are living with their grandmothers until their parents recover. "Techo" New Business Training Center and Cambodian Investors Network Sign Memorandum of Understanding to Promote New Business Ecosystem in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Digital Economy and Society Policy Framework 2021-2035 sets out a long-term vision for building a vibrant digital economy and society by laying the foundations for promoting change and digital capture in all areas.
The new business ecosystem also plays an important role in promoting the application of these principles in living with Kovid-19 in the new normal trajectory.
On January 18, 2022, Dr. Taing Nguon Ly, Executive Director of the “Techo” New Business Training Center and Mr. Heang Raksmey, Program Manager of the Cambodian Investors Network, signed a Memorandum of Understanding for the purpose of promoting new business and participating in development. Ecosystems of New Business and Entrepreneurship in Cambodia by Connecting New Businesses to Investors in Cambodia's New Digital Business Nursery.
The new Cambodia Digital Business Nursery was officially launched on December 8, 2021 with the main aim of supporting the new business ecosystem in Cambodia.
In addition, new businesses can even use the new business ecosystem to capture various benefits. New Digital Business Nursery Cambodia also allows new businesses, business orienters, investors, growers and business accelerators, academia and other stakeholders to register on this digital platform to expand opportunities for business growth and communication with others in This one ecosystem.
The new "Techo" Business Training Center (CEC) is a public administrative institution under the auspices of the Ministry of Economy and Finance of Cambodia. The SEC has an obligation to accelerate new business ventures by increasing entrepreneurial capacity and innovation through the Center's programs and services. The Cambodia Investor Network is an investor development program that allows investors to participate in investor education and gateways.
The program is sponsored by the Cambodian Investors Club Association (CiC) and has a five-month course with a rigorous schedule and activities, including joint study tours, investment pitching and pitching. New business, business evaluation and communication with local and foreign investors.
Both sides have a mission that goes hand in hand and will also be useful if there is a new and improved business ecosystem. Therefore, the signing of this Memorandum of Understanding demonstrates the bilateral commitment to support all aspects of the new business ecosystem, as well as other stakeholders, in line with the Cambodian Digital Economic and Social Policy Framework. 2021-2035.
