Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Border Peace is Necessary for Citizens along the Cambodia-Vietnam Border (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, said that maintaining border peace, relations and cooperation Good relations between Cambodia and Vietnam are a necessary element for the people and the two countries to benefit economically.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's remarks came as he allowed Vietnamese Foreign Minister Bui Thanh Son to pay a courtesy call and discuss some issues in the morning of Thursday, January 20, 2022. Is visiting Cambodia.
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, affirmed that in front of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Mr. Bouy Thanh Son expressed his deep appreciation and admiration for Samdech Techo for Cambodia's rapid progress. For Bouy Thanh Son, Cambodia's progress is due to the skillful leadership of Samdech Techo.
This year 2022 is the 55th anniversary of the relationship between Cambodia and Vietnam, which is a fenced country and has a common history in the cause of saving the lives of the people of the two countries. During the meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Bouy Thanh Son, they also discussed the strengthening and expansion of relations and cooperation to make it even better.
According to Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, during the meeting, Mr. Bouy Thanh Son expressed his satisfaction with the excellent relations between Cambodia and Vietnam and also expressed satisfaction with the trade volume between the two countries, which increased to nearly 10,000. Million US dollars.
Bui Thanh Son expects Cambodia and Vietnam to continue to strengthen economic and trade ties, which are important elements for both countries. The Vietnamese Foreign Minister also expects Cambodia to continue to enhance cooperation in agriculture, industry and other areas such as banking and finance.
Mr. Bouy Thanh Son also thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for allowing the resumption of direct flights between Cambodia and Vietnam and for recognizing cross-border travel with a vaccination card.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the relations between Cambodia and Vietnam have improved and that what he did with the former Prime Minister of Vietnam, Nguyen Suon Phuc, has pushed the trade volume to a higher level than planned. Samdech Techo considered this trade growth as the success of the relationship and cooperation between Cambodia and Vietnam because Cambodia has the capacity to produce and Vietnam has a basis for processing.
The Prime Minister also stressed that the people as well as Vietnam benefit from each other because of a peaceful border, cooperation and friendship. Therefore, maintaining a border of peace, cooperation and friendship is necessary for people to be able to do business and do business together.
The Prime Minister also expressed his belief that the trade volume between Cambodia and Vietnam will increase further by more than 10 billion dollars.
Samdech Techo also expressed his pleasure to see direct flights between Cambodia and Vietnam to facilitate travel between the people of the two countries. In this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mentioned the railway connection between Cambodia and Vietnam, Samdech wants to see new principles on the railway connection to facilitate trade between Cambodia and Vietnam.
