Maintaining banking and financial knowledge to journalists plays an important role in continuing to share with the public clearly.
(Phnom Penh): The Banking Association of Cambodia, the Cambodian Microfinance Association and the Club of Cambodian Journalists have jointly organized a training course for journalists on "Fundamentals of Banking and Finance in Cambodia".
This 5-day training course is designed to disseminate knowledge of banking and finance to journalists as an important part to continue to share with the public clearly.
Journalist Training Course on "Fundamentals of Banking and Finance in Cambodia" Opening Ceremony on January 19, 2022 with the participation of Mr. Kith Sovannarith, First Deputy Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, Mr. Bun Yin, Vice Chairman of the Board of the Banking Association of Cambodia, Mr. Pen Bona, President of the Club of Cambodian Journalists and Mr. Kea Boran, Chairman of the Board of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia.
Mr. Kith Sovannarith congratulated the organization of this training, which is very important for the media to share.
Education, financial literacy to the people is very important, so the Royal Government through the National Bank of Cambodia has set out a number of strategies. This training course for journalists will help to spread knowledge to the people more widely and clearly through its dissemination.
Mr. Kea Boran said that the training course aims to raise awareness of banking and finance for journalists to contribute to the production of content, whether in the form of articles, audio or video in the context of The growth of the financial sector in Cambodia.
"The press has played an important role in sharing information, following events, as well as reflecting positive or negative points to promote change and achieve social development," he said. "On the economic front, the press also plays an increasingly important role in sharing information, knowledge, as well as new developments to help readers make the right decisions for their lives."
He stated that the Cambodian Microfinance Association recognizes the value and role of the press and has always been actively involved in promoting the role of the press in fulfilling its profession.
Mr. Bun Yin stated that this is the first time that the Banking Association of Cambodia and the Cambodian Microfinance Association under the support of the National Bank of Cambodia have organized this training course and for the purpose of:
1: Increase the relationship between journalists and the banking and financial sector. 2: Improve financial literacy and improve the financial environment through the media. 3. Contribute to the implementation of the National Strategy on Financial Environment 2019- 2025, which was inaugurated and officially announced on December 3, 2021.
He added that "the financial environment in Cambodia still has some challenges, especially the understanding and knowledge of finance in Cambodia is still low, the ability to access information financial services is an important factor in the use of financial services. Efficiency. "Access to clear and in-depth information can help Cambodians understand their right to use, choose, negotiate and communicate financial decisions."
He emphasized that the training will focus on: 1. The role of the National Bank of Cambodia and the regulatory framework. 2. The history of the establishment of banking and financial institutions and risk management in the banking and financial system. : Overview of the banking and financial sector. 4: Financial health monitoring, compliance and customer protection principles, regularity, experience and lessons from Kovid 19.5: Other topics on banking and finance.
Mr. Pen Bona said that this training is very important for Cambodian economic journalists to strengthen their knowledge in the field of banking and finance.
He said that this training really plays an important role for journalists to continue to disseminate to the public, because all the information that journalists do not understand clearly, can not write stories to the public to understand.
Takhmao police arrest 3 out of 10 gangsters after posting motorbikes on public roads
(Kandal): Police in Takhmao City, Kandal Province, arrested three out of 10 street gangsters after they recently drove a motorbike on a public road, causing fear among the people. Citizens travel.
Yi Vanda, police chief of Takhmao City, told Fresh News that the three gangsters were arrested after residents posted a video of the gang carrying five motorbikes, causing unrest in the area. On January 18, 2021, the police force searched and found three people and arrested them and took them to the Takhmao City Police Inspectorate on January 19, 2021.
The three arrested gangsters are as follows:
* First: Name: Chea Chetra, Male, 16 years old, Residence: Prek Hoor Keut Village, Sangkat Prek Hoor, Takhmao City, Kandal Province, Occupation: Student Kandal Province * 3: Name: Hul Ly Heang, Male, 17 years old, Residence: Prek Kat Village, Sangkat Takdol, Takhmao City, Kandal Province.
The other seven factions are known by two names, including:
* First: Name: Chuon Sopanha, Male, 17 years old, Residence: Prek Reang Village, Sangkat Kampong Samnang, Takhmao City, Kandal Province. Occupation: Student. In the middle of the occupation of Hussein Takhmao High School students (escaped). The other five factions have not yet been identified and are on the run.
According to the story, at the time of the incident, these gangs were riding 5 motorcycles with 10 people, one of which was riding with 2 people. Traveling the streets took videos of the activity and posted them on social media.
After receiving the information, Takhmao City Special Forces cooperated with the Post Administration Force to search and identify until January 19, then arrested 3 suspects, including 3 vehicles, and sent them to the Black City Police Inspectorate for legal questioning. Way. As for the other seven factions, special forces are searching for them and arresting them for questioning.
