The Malaysian Tourism Promotion Council also hosted a special luncheon with travel agencies on 17 January to boost the support of its counterparts in promoting Malaysia as a leading and safe destination in the region. Southeast Asia. The meeting also serves to update partners on the latest developments in Malaysia, as well as tourism and development products.
Malaysia Tourism's participation in ATF 2022 aims to provide tourism industry professionals from around Southeast Asia with the latest information on travel to Malaysia, especially after the recent announcement. This is about Malaysia's first international tourism meeting to Langkawi, which opened on November 15, 2021.
