ASEAN officially reopens ASEAN tourism
(Preah Sihanouk): ASEAN Tourism Ministers and Leaders together with the ASEAN Secretary-General on the evening of January 19, 2022 jointly announced the reopening of ASEAN tourism from Sihanoukville.
This ASEAN Tourism Re-Declaration is in line with the vision of ASEAN Socio-Economic Rehabilitation based on the following principles:
1: Launch intra-ASEAN tourism, shape the ASEAN travel portal and create a digital vaccination card.
2. Identify the Kovid-19 vaccine as the key to achieving community resilience towards the revitalization of the tourism industry.
3. Encourage people to live in a new normal path in accordance with the health rules and operating standards of each member country.
4. Ensure that tourism services and businesses operate in accordance with ASEAN principles on hygiene and safety for tourism professionals and communities.
5. Promote trust and confidence by encouraging all tourism operators and service providers in the ASEAN region.
