Senior Ministry of Environment official: More than 60,000 traps to be removed from protected areas by 2021 and 758 firearms confiscated, many wildlife saved
The Secretary of State stated that the number of traps removed in 2021 increased by more than 20% compared to the number of traps removed in 2021, which was 43,270 traps.
With the release of so many traps, the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment considers it a killer to kill wild animals because there are types of traps, electric wires, traps to break the legs and other types.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that traps are still a serious threat to all kinds of wildlife, especially wildlife, and not only Cambodia has a problem with the presence of traps in protected areas, protected areas in countries in Asia is threatened by traps. Millions of traps are known to be placed in protected areas in Vietnam, Cambodia, Laos, Indonesia, Malaysia.
According to the senior official, "The most threatening factor for wildlife is the trap, which is a hidden killer." "Because trapping materials are available in the market and are cheap, the number of traps is estimated to increase, and in Asia more than 12 million traps have been stolen in protected areas across Asia."
On behalf of the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Neth Pheaktra expressed his appreciation and gratitude to the park rangers, partner organizations and all protected area communities who participated in removing traps from the natural forest.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Environment highlighted: "In addition to the traps that endangered wildlife, rangers also confiscated 758 firearms used for hunting in 2021. This amount is about 2020. "
In addition, Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that the increase in recycled guns is also part of the threat to wildlife, and this recycled gun is also the most dangerous weapon. In addition, chasing dogs is also a cause of harm to wildlife. Some people keep herds of dogs chasing them to hunt wild animals, which in turn reduces the number of wild animals that are hunted and die from the disease of domestic dogs.
The spokesman for the Ministry of Environment added that in order to stop hunting, stop trapping animals, people should not eat meat, do not trade in deer, and do not believe in the belief that they eat animal blood or take wild bones for medicine. Tonic or health aid, but it may put you at risk because there may be other viruses.
