(Phnom Penh): On January 19, 2022, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, accompanied by Mr. Chuon Bitthol, Undersecretary of State, Mr. Mao Hak, Chief of Phnom Penh Capital, Technical Officer and GDFC Representative, inspected the work progress. Implement the construction of Prek Tnaot Irrigation and Flood Protection Project in Phnom Penh, Kandal, Takeo and Kampong Speu Provinces with financial assistance from the People's Republic of China.
According to the report from the technical team during the inspection, the construction of the above irrigation system started on December 1, 2021, which so far has achieved about 22% of the plan.
The purpose of the Prek Tnaot Irrigation and Flood Protection Project is to reduce the risk of flooding in the delta, especially west of Phnom Penh and Kandal Province, as well as to increase the cultivated area that can help prevent and reduce flooding. The flood covers an area of 245 square kilometers and can irrigate 10,150 hectares of dry paddy fields and 17,730 hectares of wet paddy fields.
It should be noted that the Prek Tnaot Irrigation and Flood Protection System in Phnom Penh, Kandal, Takeo and Kampong Speu Provinces is directly led by the Minister in planning and cooperating with development partners and friendly countries to implement the project as soon as possible. This benefit in mitigating the impact and avoiding disasters often plague the rapidly developing western part of Phnom Penh.
