ASEAN Plus Three Tourism Ministers vow to revive ASEAN Plus Three (Video inside) (Sihanoukville): The rate of international tourists visiting ASEAN Plus Three has dropped to 81.5% in 2020, therefore, the ASEAN Plus Three Tourism Ministers are committed to further strengthen cooperation to revitalize the tourism movement in ASEAN Plus Three countries.
The meeting was held on the morning of January 19, 2022 with the participation of the ASEAN Tourism Ministers, the Chinese, Japanese and Korean Tourism Ministers, the ASEAN Secretariat, the ASEAN Center, China, Japan and Korea, the leaders of the Ministry of Tourism, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. A total of about 100 international operations.
The ASEAN Plus Three Tourism Ministers expressed grave concern over the 81.5% drop in international tourism by 2020, which will affect millions of jobs due to business closures and travel restrictions.
In the face of this difficult situation, the ASEAN Plus Three Tourism Ministers welcomed the resumption of ASEAN tourism and pledged to further strengthen cooperation between ASEAN Plus Three (China, Japan and Korea) to examine the possibility of promoting Tourism in ASEAN countries plus three, with the safety and well-being of tourists first.
The ASEAN Plus Three Tourism Ministers' Meeting also evaluated the results of the implementation of the ASEAN Plus Three Tourism Cooperation Action Plan 2021-2025, which focused on two key points, including: Rehabilitation of tourism in ASEAN countries plus three and 2. Strengthen better cooperation towards the development of ASEAN Plus Three tourism that is more sustainable, responsible and resilient.
