Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces support for the resumption of ASEAN intra-tourism and urges the ASEAN Tourism Minister to leave Sihanoukville tomorrow (Video inside) (Preah Sihanouk): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia On January 18, 2022, he announced his support for the re-opening of ASEAN intra-tourism, with Samdech urging the ASEAN Tourism Ministers to discuss and unanimously announce the re-opening of ASEAN tourism from Sihanoukville tomorrow.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech was made during the opening ceremony of the ASEAN Tourism Forum in Sihanoukville on the evening of January 18, 2022 in Sihanoukville.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "I fully support the opening of intra-ASEAN tourism, as well as the opening of the whole region to receive international tourists again. "As the chair of ASEAN, I would like to support the ASEAN Tourism Ministers to discuss and unanimously announce the reopening of ASEAN tourism tomorrow from Sihanoukville."
The Prime Minister stated that in order to ensure the success of the re-opening of international tourism, it is necessary to ensure the credibility and confidence as a safe ASEAN tourism destination based on the rate of vaccination as a benchmark indicator.
At the same time, Samdech Techo announced that he would like to support the "Vaccine Tourism" program launched in ASEAN countries and would like to support the launch of the "ASEAN as a warm and safe tourism destination" campaign.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo praised the ASEAN Tourism Ministers for enhancing cooperation and exchanging experiences in response to the 19-Kovid Crisis and launched the ASEAN Tourism Restoration Plan after the 19-Kovid Crisis. ASEAN Tourism on Sustainable, Environmentally and Resilient as well as Strategic Plans, Work Programs and other ASEAN Guidelines.
In the past two years, the Kovid-19 crisis has had a serious socio-economic impact, especially by 2020, ASEAN as a whole received only 25.96 million international tourists, down 80.5% and revenue. From tourism decreased to 75.8%.
"The work of ASEAN in 2022 is not just about Myanmar, as many have said in the last three weeks," Hun Sen said. "We have a lot of issues to do besides Myanmar, and ASEAN is not a hostage of Myanmar's problems," he said.
