BEIJING: China's economy is expected to recover in 2021 with the best growth in a decade due to strong exports, but there are signs that the economy is slowing due to a slowdown in consumption and a strong economy. The decline in the real estate sector, which requires additional policy support. According to Reuters.
China's economy has grown 8 percent this year, the strongest pace since 2011 and higher than the 8 percent forecast, Reuters reported, citing data from the National Bureau of Statistics (NBS). . That is higher than the Chinese government's target of 6 percent and 2.2 percent higher than the economic powerhouse achieved in 2020, the slowest pace in 44 years.
However, economic growth in the fourth quarter was only 4 percent, higher than expected. This is the lowest growth since the second quarter of 2020.
China is tackling issues such as efforts to stem the growth of the real estate sector and the outbreak of Kovid-19, which could cause problems for factories and supply chains.
China's real estate market has slowed in recent months as regulators cut interest-bearing loans, prompting a number of debtors to default. Real estate investment fell 13.9 percent in December last year, the biggest drop since early 2020. According to Reuters.
