The four-point proposal made by Chinese President Xi Jinping at the 2022 annual meeting of the World Economic Forum is a contribution to the "China Plan" for global development after the end of Kovid 19.
BEIJING, Jan. 17 (Xinhua) - The 2022 annual meeting of the World Economic Forum opened on Jan. 17 as the world struggles with the global Kovid-19 pandemic crisis and a series of rare constitutional changes. The last century that has caused the global economy to plummet for two years.
By highlighting these proposals, we can better understand China's position of adhering to multilateralism, facing a common crisis, narrowing the development gap between developed and developing countries, and harmonizing the divisions. Share the "Chinese plan" and "Chinese wisdom" for contributing to global development, as well as working together to overcome obstacles to overcome the dark shadows of various crises, especially the global epidemic crisis ahead.
Since the founding of the People's Republic of China or the new China, China's development has progressed to become one of the engines of the current world economy. The secret of China's ability to transform itself from a "small boat" to a "giant ship" is beyond doubt, adhering to its original purpose of striving for self-development and sharing its development achievements with The world.
In fact, no matter what the circumstances, China has always stressed the need for solidarity and win-win cooperation, which is the foundation of multilateralism, and has set out a number of initiatives to achieve Practicing multilateralism, the "Belt and Road" initiative and the recognition of vaccines as public products have made indispensable contributions to global economic development and the fight against global epidemics.
The world today is a polar one, so disagreement is inevitable, as the Khmer proverb says, "A plate of liquid is no longer mixed." Although the tongue and the teeth are in contact with each other every day, they are inseparable from each other, hence the world of diversification and multiplication is evolving in the pattern of natural law, which tends to move with the times.
After all, there are those who raise multilateral flags, and there are those who raise my flag. Many conflicts now stem from selfish political ambitions, in which everything has become a tool for unscrupulous politicians to attack others to strengthen their hegemonic power. The political game of some individuals has added even more tensions to a world that is experiencing unprecedented public, social and economic health crises.
However, Chinese authorities are often seen to have taken immediate action when reports of the COVID-19 virus have been reported, such as issuing orders to block out areas where outbreaks have occurred. Large-scale testing in the sense of immediately preventing the virus from spreading to other areas.
Forestry Administration cooperates with ACU to launch training on anti-money laundering and forest crime
(Phnom Penh): The Forestry Administration, in cooperation with the Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU), on the morning of January 18, 2022, organized a training course on anti-money laundering and forest crime.
The opening ceremony was presided over by Mr. Kheang Seng, Deputy Chief of the Anti-Corruption Unit, on behalf of the Honorary Legal Officer, Dr. Om Yentieng, Senior Minister, Chairman of the Anti-Corruption Unit, and Dr. Keo Omalis, Royal Government of Cambodia Representative in charge of Forestry Administration at the Research and Development Institute. Forests and wildlife.
The training was also attended by the leaders of the Forestry Administration, the leaders of the relevant departments and officers of the Forestry Administration, as well as the Khans, Divisions and Sangkat Chiefs of the Forestry Administration in 25 capitals and provinces.
The ACU Vice-Chairman stated that in response to this, the Anti-Corruption Unit as well as the relevant ministries and institutions have launched their action plans to implement the action plan set by the APG Joint Group and the action plan set out in the strategy. National Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorism Financing 2019-2023.
