(Phnom Penh): About 30 protesters over land and houses in Sangkat Boeung Kak 2, Khan Toul Kork agreed with the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority after an explanation on the morning of January 18, 2022.
The agreement was made on the occasion of Mr. Keut Chhe and Mr. Mean Chanyada, Deputy Governor, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, meeting with the protesters from Boeung Kak II related to the land and houses.
On that occasion, the authorities explained some principles and points, asking them to keep the status quo, not to be disturbed, because the authorities do not have any policy or instructions to leave the place where they are living.
Mr. Keut Chhe and Mr. Mean Chanyada said, “For more than two years now, the Phnom Penh authorities, as well as Khans and Sangkats, have been busy preventing the spread of Kovid 19, so we do not yet have a policy. Any to develop at this point where you are living.
He said that Mr. Khuong Sreng has always adhered to the principle of housing rights for people, and this solution has already been successful in many places. On the other hand, discussions to find a solution must involve stakeholders, authorities and the people, with frank discussions on content that does not affect the interests of the people.
"On the other hand, if there is any protest or do not clearly understand any development project, it should write a letter to Phnom Penh Capital Hall or send a representative to discuss a solution by mutual understanding. And the solution does not depend on the incitement of any unscrupulous person to harm you. "But the important thing now is that the Phnom Penh authorities do not have any plans that will affect your life." According to the authorities.
After the explanation from Mr. Keut Chhe and Mr. Mean Chanyada, the people who came to protest to Phnom Penh Capital Hall understood and promised to follow the above guidelines.
