Tbong Khmum Provincial Officials continue to inspect products sold in Stung Market to ensure the health of consumers
(Tbong Khmum): On the morning of January 17, 2022, Tbong Khmum Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud Branch (TPC) cooperated with the Provincial Department of Commerce to continue inspecting products at Stung Market. In Ponhea Krek district, Tbong Khmum province.
Mr. San Vichea Saravuth, President of Tbong Khmum Province, confirmed that during the inspection, the sales of traders were very good and there were few non-compliant goods. As a result, officials confiscated 33.20 kilograms of non-compliant products, including Chinese coffee and lotion, without a certificate from the Ministry of Health.
In the same activity, the professional officer explained and instructed the traders who own the mall to sell goods and sell cosmetics to be aware of the display, buy and resell, must have a permit from the relevant professional institutions and paste information standards for you Use in accordance with the Consumer Protection Act.
In addition, the official also explained to the traders to sell products with high standards of hygiene, quality, safety for the benefit of the seller, the buyer has improved health, especially buyers know how to look at the life of goods and products. In accordance with the law before selling to consumers to avoid economic losses to the family and face the law.
Court Detains Former Monk Pouy Meta After Criminal Complaint After Leading Monks to Gather in Front of Sieng Chanheng House
(Phnom Penh): Finally! Phnom Penh Municipal Court Investigating Judge San Bunthoeun has ordered the Ministry of Interior's criminal police to bring former monk Poei Metta to the Phnom Penh Municipal Prison (PJ) for later trial. Law.
Former monk Pouy Metta was arrested on January 14, 2022 after a criminal complaint after mobilizing about 100 monks to gather in front of Duke Sieng Chanheng's house in Thmey Village, Sangkat Takhmao, Takhmao City. Kandal province to protest for her to return the land to the pagoda.
Prior to his arrest, Mr. Chreung Khmao, Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, issued an order for the former monk to appear at the Central Security Department of the Ministry of Interior on February 3, 2022, following a complaint by Ms. Seang Chanheng. .
On December 9, 2021, Poeuy Meta led about 100 monks from Phnom Penh to gather in front of Mrs. Oknha Seang Chanheng's house in Thmey Village, Sangkat Takhmao, Takhmao City, Kandal Province to protest her handover. Land back to the pagoda. The protest lasted from about 2 pm until late at night, after which it was disbanded after Kandal Provincial Governor Kong Sophorn mediated that it would be resolved on December 13, 2021.
Please be informed that the above complaint is subject to the objection to the decision No. 001/22 dated 13 January 2022 of the council meeting, Sangkat Phsar Chas, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh, which has its own plaintiff named Duong Vichet 4 people.
Cambodia, Laos Strengthen Tourism Cooperation to Boost Tourism Flow Between Two Countries and From Other Countries
The Memorandum of Understanding on Cambodia-Laos Tourism Cooperation will focus on:
1. Facilitate cross-border travel and other procedures to facilitate travelers when crossing the border between the two countries.
2: Human resource development and capacity development through the organization and participation in seminars, conferences, trainings and other meetings.
3. Continue to promote the exchange of official visits and exploration visits for public and private institutions as well as journalists.
4. Strengthen cooperation in sub-regional frameworks such as Greater Mekong Subregion Cooperation, Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation, ACMECS Cooperation, CLMV Cooperation and CLV Cooperation.
Both sides expressed satisfaction over the past cooperation in the spirit of friendship and solidarity as tourists who have gone through difficult times in the past.
The Lao side thanked the Cambodian government, especially the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, for providing Kovid-19 vaccine to the Lao people and providing medical equipment and supplies to fight this deadly disease. Laos.
Please be reminded that Cambodia and Laos have always supported each other in participating in international programs organized by each country. In particular, the Minister of Laos confirmed the participation and seek to travel to participate in this event by land, but due to urgent business, she appointed Deputy Minister to lead the delegation instead.
Banteay Meanchey Provincial Authority Leads Police Forces to Plant Trees in Three Tonle Sap Flooded Areas for the Fourth Time
(Banteay Meanchey): The Provincial Unity Command, led by Banteay Meanchey Provincial Governor Oum Rath, led police forces and provincial officials to replant trees in three areas adjacent to the Tonle Sap Lake for the fourth time in Prasat commune. And a part of Phnom Leap commune, Preah Net Preah district, Banteay Meanchey province on January 16, 2022.
Mr. Oum Rath confirmed that the seedlings were replanted and that local authorities had to take care of the seedlings every month to confirm that the seedlings were not dead.
In the fourth tree planting process, more than 400 provincial police commissioners, armed forces, provincial halls, relevant departments, and armed forces participated in planting 1,000 bamboo trees, 700 water hyacinth trees, and palm trees. 3,400 in the area of 3 Tonle Sap Lake in Preah Net Preah District, Banteay Meanchey Province.
It should be noted that this is the fourth tree planting campaign that Banteay Meanchey provincial authorities have held.
