Ministry of National Defense Groundbreaking Ceremony for Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Administrative Training Center
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of January 18, 2022, General Sam Vanthan, Secretary General of the Supreme National Defense Council and Secretary General of the Ministry of National Defense, presided over the groundbreaking ceremony for the groundbreaking ceremony of the Military Training Center. Royal Khmer.
The ceremony was attended by senior officers from the General Secretariat of the Ministry of National Defense, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Command and local authorities.
Lt. Gen. Kim Raksmey, Deputy Secretary General of the Ministry of National Defense in charge of the Administrative Training Center of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chairman of the Construction Committee of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces' Administrative Training Center, briefed officers from Institutions under the Ministry of National Defense and the General Command of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
The first training course was established in 2001 under the management of the Sub-Committee and continues until now, under the management of the Administrative Job Training Center of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces through Prakas No. 076, dated September 11, 2019 of the Ministry of National Defense.
Mr. Kim Raksmey continued that along with the work progress, the Administrative Job Training Center of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces also encountered some shortcomings, especially the work place for officers and classrooms for trainees.
To address these challenges, General Sam Vanthan initiated the construction of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) Administrative Training Center on Lot 1, Street 13, Sleng Roleung Village, Sangkat O Bek Kam, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh, which is owned by the Ministry of National Defense. Using the contribution of philanthropists and officers in the General Secretariat of the Ministry of National Defense.
Speaking at the ceremony, General Sam Vanthan praised and appreciated the work management, training and responsible spirit in implementing the construction plan to move forward. "Everything has to start, to progress and achieve the goal. Although we do not have enough resources, we must start," he said.
In the past, the Secretary General of the Ministry of National Defense has built a lot of achievements for both the unit and the local work without affecting the national budget, so this construction is the same, we will strive to achieve success to keep it as a work. History of the Secretary General of the Ministry of National Defense.
At the same time, the General requested and appealed to officers as well as philanthropists near and far to join this construction movement, as administrative training is very important for officers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to perform their duties in accordance. Procedures, standards, hierarchies and unification of common standards, as well as more accurate in compiling, managing, managing documents effectively, ensuring the quality of military secrecy.
At the end of the ceremony, the General laid the foundation stone and ordered the drilling rig as a symbol of the construction process. Police crack down on 6 thieves and confiscate a large number of exhibits in Por Sen Chey district
(Phnom Penh): Under the command of Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, Colonel Mon Vuthy, Police Inspector of Por Senchey District, led the Khan Police Force in cooperation with the 1st Kakap Post Until the arrest of six thieves who often actively seize the property of passengers on the street.
