(Kampong Thom): Mr. Kieng Sengky, Chief of Tbong Krapeu Commune, Santuk District, urged parents of students to study at least at the basic level.
He said this during a meeting and provide study materials to more than 500 students at Wat Mony Pothinhan in Ampos village, Tbong Krapeu commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province on January 17, 2022.
Mr. Kieng Sengky said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has made great efforts to implement in-depth reform and development strategies in all areas, especially agriculture, industry and education, which are playing an important role in promoting social and economic development. In providing food security to the people of Cambodia and reducing the poverty of the people, as well as solving challenges.
He called on parents to promote their children's education, because education is self-reliant, with patience, attention at all times, and parents need to support and encourage more.
In addition, education for change helps all Cambodian children to pay attention and explore all possible ways to obtain a selection mechanism for building a foundation of change through thinking to build faith. The mind is full of hope, which is the energy that drives all the actions and responsibilities it performs for itself, others, family and society, and when "the vine grows well, it depends on the bamboo to help it."
He reminded that all Cambodian children, from previous generations to the next generation, must uphold the national honor by working together to maintain peace and political stability. He urged all people to have self-confidence, believe in the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia to continue the journey on the Cambodian ship to the coast of peace and development of the country.
At the same time, Mr. Kieng Sengky thanked the monks and philanthropists near and far who always help the people in Tbong Krapeu commune to get development.
It should be noted that 502 students received books, pens, pencils, erasers and some money, teachers, 1 krama and some money.
