ASEAN Secretary-General fully supports Cambodia's Ministry of National Defense to host ASEAN Defense Ministers 'Meeting and Defense Ministers' Meeting Plus in 2022
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Lim Chok Huy, Secretary-General of ASEAN, announced his full support for the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia to host the ASEAN Defense Ministers 'Meeting and the Defense Ministers' Meeting in 2022 and committed to working with the Ministry. Defend Cambodia and coordinate all work with all partner countries to jointly organize the meeting to be successful.
The announcement of support by the ASEAN Secretary-General was made during a meeting between Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, on the afternoon of January 17, 2022 at the Ministry of National Defense.
On behalf of the host of the ASEAN Defense Ministers 'Meeting and related meetings in 2022, Samdech Picheay Sena is committed to making the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting and related meetings a success.
In addition, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh stated that so far, Cambodia has just received a request to organize an informal meeting of ASEAN Defense Ministers Plus 1, including: Russia and Japan, request the ASEAN Secretariat to promote and coordinate with the country. Other partners in proposing the ASEAN Plus One Informal Meeting of Defense Ministers, scheduled for the end of 2022.
Mr. LIM Chok Huy thanked for the warm welcome from Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh and congratulated Samdech Pichey Sena for hosting the ASEAN Defense Ministers 'Meeting and the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting Plus. In the year 2022.
On behalf of the Secretary-General of ASEAN, he will continue to focus on facilitating all matters related to the defense sector, in particular three conceptual documents, including: 1. ASEAN Armed Forces Cooperation on the Prevention of the Crossing of Kovid 19; Participate in the ASEAN Women's Peacekeeping Operations, Peace and Security; and 3rd: Establish the ASEAN Defense University Cooperation and Joint Statement.
In addition, the Secretary-General of ASEAN will set up a special task force in collaboration with the Ministry of National Defense in charge of ASEAN affairs.
