International Analysis: What changed when the United States changed its strategy against China?
(California): During the Cold War, Europe was a priority strategy for the United States. But such tactics have changed, with the US security strategy now shifting its focus to China and East Asia, which have replaced Europe as a geopolitical challenge.
A China-focused strategy emerged after the United States withdrew its troops from Afghanistan, leaving the pro-Western Kabul government to be overthrown by the Taliban. But as the United States focuses on China, Russia and Iran also take the opportunity to expand their influence.
Iranian leaders may be feeling that US President Joe Biden will not join or intervene in a new war in the Middle East, as the United States is preparing for a possible conflict with China. President Putin has been deploying large numbers of troops near the Ukrainian border, and he is likely to think the same way about Iran.
But in the Middle East, most countries rely almost entirely on US security, which would allow the entire Middle East to learn to live without US support or support. Moreover, if the United States maintains a strategy focused on China, it may or may not lose its geopolitical influence, such as in the Middle East.
However, the decline in American influence is also a good thing, as it will prevent the United States from going to war unnecessarily. For more than three decades, after the end of the Cold War, the United States used its military forces abroad every year, wreaking havoc and spending large sums of money on wars in Iraq and Afghanistan. And so on.
Thus, the new US strategy focusing on China will force other countries that used to rely heavily on the United States to focus on strengthening their own capabilities. In the Middle East, many Arab countries have restored relations and strengthened peace, and the reconnection of some Arab states with Israel is an example.
On the other hand, Europe also emerged with an "autonomous strategy", which proved that Europe could no longer rely solely on the United States to protect its security, and one fact that the world had to recognize was the "Cold War in the New Age." Between the United States and China.
