Short Documentary on Tuol Sleng Genocide Museum Archive Released
(Phnom Penh): A short documentary on "Tuol Sleng Genocide Museum Archive" was officially screened on January 17, 2022 at the Bophana Audiovisual Resource Center. The documentary was produced under the project "Preservation and Integration of the Tuol Sleng Museum Archive into a Computer System."
The screening of the film was held under a strong partnership between the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) and the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization (UNESCO), Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts. Cambodia and the Bophana Audiovisual Resource Center.
Under the framework of the project "Preservation and Integration of the Tuol Sleng Museum Archive into a Computer System" with the support of KOICA, more than 700,000 pages of Tuol Sleng Genocide Museum archives have been preserved and nearly half a million archives have been preserved. Integrate into a computer system. This legacy is the most detailed account of the prison system of the Khmer Rouge regime.
The archive contains thousands of stories about what happened at S-21 during the Khmer Rouge regime. Some of the stories were filmed by the Bophana Audiovisual Resource Center as five short documentaries that UNESCO-UNESCO presented at the premiere of the short documentary, which was officially released on January 17, 2022.
Short Documentary: "Tuol Sleng Genocide Museum Archive" will raise awareness among Cambodians, especially the younger generation, about the events of the Khmer Rouge regime and will help them better understand Their past to promote reconciliation and peace education.
