By 2021, electronic payments will reach a record high of nearly 200 billion dollars
(Phnom Penh): According to a senior official of the National Bank of Cambodia, Mr. Ouk Sarath, Director of the Payment System Department of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that in 2021, electronic payments will increase compared to 2020 due to the number of payment transactions. 698.8 million transactions, valued at 199.76 billion US dollars, accounting for 787% of GDP.
"Cambodia's payment system has grown significantly and is evolving towards digital payments with new service infrastructure and payment tools," he said. "In 2021, electronic payments increased compared to 2020, with 698.8 million electronic payment transactions amounting to 199.76 billion US dollars, accounting for 787% of GDP."
He added that with the advancement of financial technology, some banking and financial institutions have introduced digital money transfer and cross-border payment services in addition to the provision of services through agents and counters.
"For banks or microfinance institutions, electronic payments have increased the efficiency of services by reducing the cost of paperwork and facilitating data management," said Kaing Tong Ngy.
He said that now customers can transfer money immediately via mobile phone using the Bakong system without having to wait for time or go directly to the institution, while the fee is low and some microfinance institutions do not have to pay the service fee. Also.
He added, however, that some customers are not yet familiar with and use electronic payments, so microfinance institutions, including the Cambodian Microfinance Association, have been actively involved in promoting and encouraging customers. Use this electronic payment system.
Obviously, the creation of this electronic payment service has been simplified, simplified and faster for customers as well. The establishment always offers a variety of services and according to the needs of customers, in general, customers can still seek support or services directly from the staff of the institution.
