Construction of Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant has reached 50% and is scheduled to be operational in 2023
(Phnom Penh): The construction of the first phase of Bak Kheng water treatment plant with a capacity of 195,000 cubic meters per day has reached about 50%, which is scheduled to be completed and put into operation in 2023.
Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has confirmed that it has been accelerating the construction of Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant with a capacity of 390,000 cubic meters per day (Phase 1, 195,000 cubic meters per day and Phase II). 195,000 cubic meters per day) Achieved about 50% of the first phase of construction project, which is scheduled to be completed and put into operation in 2023 to meet the needs of the people in Phnom Penh and Takhmao.
The Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority (PPWSA) has highlighted that the current population growth, investment in the construction sector (condominiums, warehouses, supermarkets, supermarkets ...), trade and other sectors in Phnom Penh and Takhmao are increasing day by day. Stagnant, which leads to the demand for clean water exceeding production capacity (demand of more than 700,000 cubic meters per day, the production capacity is only 600,000 cubic meters per day).
Seeing this shortage, the Royal Government decided to invest more in the construction of additional water treatment plants, such as the Bak Kheng water treatment plant, and is also preparing to build the Takhmao water treatment plant.
He emphasized that the Bak Kheng water treatment plant will increase water production capacity by 70% throughout Phnom Penh and Takhmao, in addition to the current water production capacity from 600,000 cubic meters per day to 1 million cubic meters. Per day in 2025.
The construction site is located in Sangkat Bak Kheng on a large area and the road on both sides is wide, easy to install main pipe with a large diameter to pass through the bottom of the Tonle Sap and connect to some areas in Phnom Penh.
Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant has a pumping station on the Mekong River and the installation of a two-meter diameter pipeline along Win-Win Boulevard and the drilling of a 800-meter-long pipeline through the Tonle Sap River. . The Tonle Sap Pipe Backing Project is the largest project to be implemented in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
