Resolving disputes in Myanmar and bringing Myanmar back to the ASEAN Forum is a hot topic for Cambodia to chair ASEAN in 2022. The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, and as chair of ASEAN, has made every effort to explore and use the strategies that Cambodia has experimented with in the past as a concession in the dispute in Myanmar.
The issue of Myanmar remains an important and necessary topic for Samdech Techo Hun Sen in a working meeting with ASEAN Secretary-General Lim Chok Huy this morning, July 17, 2022.
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn continued that in this meeting, Samdech Techo also highlighted Samdech's initiative to push this work forward. In particular, assistance to Myanmar based on the "Troika" mechanism and the humanitarian assistance mechanism in critical situations.
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn emphasized that "Samdech Techo Prime Minister highlighted the ASEAN mechanism , which must have the current ASEAN chair, ASEAN chair last year and ASEAN chair after Cambodia. Brunei, Cambodia, Indonesia, plus the ASEAN Secretary-General work together to monitor the implementation of the ceasefire in Myanmar. In particular, evaluate the progress of the five ASEAN consensus principles agreed in April 2021.
According to Kao Kim Hourn, the ASEAN Secretary-General fully supports Cambodia's initiative to monitor the implementation of the ceasefire in Myanmar.
"Regarding the Prime Minister's initiative to enhance the ASEAN mechanism to monitor the ceasefire, the ASEAN Secretary-General will provide full support for this work." This is a quote from Mr. Lim Chok Huy by Mr. Kao Kim Hourn to confirm to the media.
Lim Chok Huy not only supported the expansion of the "Troika" mechanism to monitor the ceasefire in Myanmar, but also supported the establishment of mechanisms to provide assistance to Myanmar, which is important.
The ASEAN Secretary-General informed the Prime Minister that in August 2021, the ASEAN Secretariat convened a meeting to mobilize humanitarian aid to Myanmar, and for the first time in October 2021 to Myanmar.
During today's working meeting, Samdech Techo also requested the ASEAN Secretary-General to hold another meeting to mobilize aid to Myanmar. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded of Japan's readiness to provide humanitarian assistance to Myanmar. According to Samdech Techo, the information on humanitarian assistance in Myanmar was confirmed by the Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia.
The results of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit are seen as a step and a light in resolving the crisis in Myanmar. Many countries have supported this result.
