The Ministry of Environment and partner organizations are committed to improving biodiversity conservation and improving community livelihoods in the Boeung Prek Lpou Landscape Protected Area.
This was stated by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment on January 16, 2022 during the visit of the delegation of the Ministry of Environment to learn about the progress of wetland conservation projects in protected areas. Boeung Prek Lpou.
"Currently, we are implementing four main activities: biodiversity conservation, community improvement, education, outreach and research," he said.
In addition, we also have other forms of outreach programs, such as screenings of educational films and mobile audio in the villages adjacent to the protected area. "In particular, we have been conducting evaluations of ecosystem services and hydrological services in the area."
Ms. Sun Leang, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Protected Areas of the Ministry of Environment, said that as a signatory to the Ramsar Convention, the Ministry of Environment always participates in the implementation of the three pillars of the Ramsar Convention on the wise use of wetlands. Identify and establish new Ramsar sites and international cooperation, especially the management of transboundary wetlands.
Mr. Hong Phea, Deputy Director of Takeo Provincial Department of Environment, said that the Takeo Provincial Department of Environment has taken care of the protection and conservation of biodiversity in the Boeung Prek Lpou Landscape Protection Area. Partners in the protection, conservation and education to the people about the laws and values of the ecosystem of the Boeung Prek Lpou landscape.
It should be noted that Boeung Prek Lpou Landscape Protection Area covers an area of 8,305 hectares and is rich in biodiversity, including 132 species of birds, 138 species of fish and 30 species of aquatic plants.
