Understand the business: Well-known officials and businessmen encourage students to turn to high-demand technical skills for investors
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia considers the development of technical and vocational education and training as a high priority in promoting economic growth.
In fact, the Rectangular Strategy, the fourth phase of the Royal Government of the sixth legislature, has given the highest priority to the development of human resources through technical and vocational education and training.
The Royal Government has strengthened the quality of education, science and technology to build a workforce with clear skills, creativity and high competitiveness, and to ensure "a young man with at least one life skill".
At the same time, well-known officials and assistants in Cambodia also encourage students, especially students who have just passed the high school diploma (Bakdup) and turn to study more technical skills that are in demand in the market and for investment.
Mr. Thong Samon, Advisor and Deputy Director General of the General Department of Vocational Education and Training of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, confirmed to Fresh News that the labor market demand for technical and vocational students is still high. The future because Cambodia is a developing country.
He added that each year, Cambodia needs more than 300,000 professional workers, and for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training can train only 60,000 skilled workers per year, so there is still a shortage.
Mr. Thong Samon added, "Cambodia is developing and the economy needs to recover after the Kovid 19 crisis. Many professionals are needed, so young people as well as students who have just finished 12th grade should come and learn technical skills." To help develop the Cambodian economy.
Tycoon Lim Heng stated that "in the factories and enterprises that come to invest, there is a great need for skilled workers, and in the new investment law, there is an incentive for those who establish schools and training courses for skilled workers."
At the same time, the Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce also said that young people, especially students, must be able to grasp certain skills in order to be able to meet the needs of the current labor market.
In the past, Duke Pung Kheav Se, known as a well-known billionaire in the Cambodian business community, also mentioned the importance of studying technical and vocational training skills.
Duke Pung Kheav Se claimed that technical and vocational training skills were in high demand, with many foreign companies telling him that they needed technical experts and that there were not many in Cambodia, forcing them to go. Find back experts from abroad.
Duke Pung Kheav Se said that in the future, Cambodia will have more investment companies with high technical skills from abroad to invest in Cambodia, and if young people know this technical skills, it is an opportunity for us.
He also pointed out that every year, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training always provides more than 20,000 scholarships to students to study in technical and vocational education and training institutions in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government.
In fact, in 2022, the Ministry of Labor has announced to provide scholarships to 20,168 students to study at the technical and vocational degrees, master's degrees / associate degrees, technical / specialized and bachelor's degrees in technology, specialization, engineering degrees according to The number of skills and occupations as well. North Korean train enters Chinese territory for first time since blockade of Kovid-19
SEOUL (Reuters) - A North Korean freight train entered a Chinese border town on Sunday, the first such crossing since Pyongyang took action. Strict closure blocks COVID-19. This was released by Mean Yonhap on Sunday, January 16, 2022.
North Korea has so far not reported any cases of COVID-19 infection, but has imposed restrictions, including border closures and travel restrictions, since the outbreak. The scourge has been rampant since 2020.
It was not immediately clear if the train was carrying cargo, with emergency supplies expected to return to North Korea on Monday.
