The 12th Royal School of Administration Senior Student Selection Exam Reaches Oral Examination with 126 Candidates
(Phnom Penh): The 12th Senior Civil Servants Recruitment Competition of the Royal School of Administration has reached the oral test on January 16-17, 2022, after completing the exam for the first written subject last December 26, 2021 at the Examination Center of the Royal University of Law and Economics and for the second writing subject on January 10, 2022 at the Royal School of Administration.
The opening of the oral exam on the 16th was presided over by Mr. Youk Bunna, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Public Works, Director of the Royal School of Administration and Chairman of the examination center for the examination process.
The exam has 3 majors and is divided into 3 rooms, including 1 room for Public Administration, 1 room for Economics and Finance, and 1 room for International Relations.
No different from the previous exam, in this oral exam, the Ministry of Public Works and the Royal School of Administration paid the most thorough and accurate attention, including the participation of the Anti-Corruption Unit and the Chairman-Vice-Chairman. Members of the Sub-Committees for the 12th Senior Student Recruitment Competition of the Royal School of Administration from relevant ministries and institutions and also from universities.
At the time of entering the exam number, each candidate must draw the question sheet in the box by himself when caught, and the candidate must read the question by himself, then start answering the question immediately, that is, without preparing the questions in advance. No commission. In addition, in each examination room, there are also officials of the Anti-Corruption Unit to check.
