Kazakh authorities claim 225 dead in violent riots
Kazakhstan authorities say violence in the country has killed 225 people, according to the latest official figures. This was released by the AFP news agency on Sunday, January 16, 2022.
"During the state of emergency, 225 people were killed, including 19 law enforcement officers and the military," a Kazakh prosecutor said in a briefing on Saturday. He added that armed robbers involved in the terrorist attacks were also killed, but unfortunately many civilians became victims of terrorism.
Violent violence in Kazakhstan stems from peaceful protests against rising fuel prices. Peaceful protests escalated into violent riots, culminating in Russian military intervention that calmed the situation as the Russian military withdrew from Kazakhstan.
