She also sent a message from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit and advised the players to go to the hospital for foot treatment, and she will pay for the treatment. The National Bank of Cambodia has set out a 10-point policy to support the recovery. Of Cambodia's economic growth in 2022
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia will continue to introduce 10 main policies to support the recovery of sustainable economic growth in 2022. These 10-point policy will fully support the growth of the national economy, which continues to be threatened by the 19 new Kovid disease.
Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, said at the closing ceremony of the National Bank of Cambodia Annual Meeting 2021 and 2022 Work Targets that by 2022, the emergence of new measles virus will continue to threaten The recovery of the global and regional economies could slow growth to lower-than-expected levels.
In the United States and Europe, infections are beginning to recover rapidly, and in ASEAN, daily infections are still high. This situation will continue to put pressure on the recovery of the Cambodian economy, especially the impact on tourism, disruption of the transport chain, exports and imports of goods and the slow growth of foreign investment flows.
In addition, the risk of an outbreak of Kovid 19 in Cambodia could lead to the introduction of strict preventive measures that could disrupt domestic production and economic activity.
However, the recovery of the global economy will continue to support the export of garments and non-garments, such as electrical components and bicycles, he added. Control over the Kovid-19 epidemic and continued economic launch will boost economic activity such as trade, investment, transport and telecommunications and domestic tourism.
The agricultural sector is expected to continue to grow well, supported by the protectionist policies of the Royal Government and the implementation of regional and bilateral free trade agreements. Under these optimistic expectations, Cambodia's economic growth in 2022 is projected at 5%.
To support the recovery of sustainable growth, the Royal Government will set out a strategic framework and programs to rehabilitate and promote economic growth in line with Kovid 19 along the new normal trajectory, which aims to revitalize and strengthen the economy. In line with this direction, the National Bank of Cambodia as well as the Cambodian banking system will continue to introduce 10 main policies, including:
In this situation, the National Bank will continue to intervene in the exchange market to keep the riel exchange rate against the US dollar stable at a level appropriate to the economic situation.
2. Promoting the use of the riel: The Kovid 19 crisis clearly demonstrates the incomplete role of monetary policy in supporting the economy, such as the ability to lower interest rates to stimulate investment or consumption due to the high level of dollarization. Promoting the use of the riel continues to be a top priority in strengthening the sovereign efficiency and independence of monetary policy in order to actively support the process of economic recovery and resilience.
In this regard, the National Bank of Cambodia has been supporting the issuance of state securities in riel, which is not only a source of long-term financing for public investment, but also an important driving force in promoting the use of the riel. As well as the development of new monetary policy instruments based on market mechanisms.
3. Implement targeted support measures: Due to the economic recovery of different sectors, the implementation of support measures will be targeted to support growth. In this sense, the banking system will contribute to the recovery of priority sectors by easing appropriate regulations and depending on the level of risk.
At the same time, the National Bank will implement a crisis exit strategy that will be carried out in a cautious manner and in line with the evolution of the actual economic situation, taking into account the psychological risks and stability of the banking system.
4: Improving the environment and financial knowledge: Currently, access to affordable financial services is still limited, which is an obstacle to contributing to the development of small and medium enterprises, which are the backbone of the economy.
In this context, the National Strategy on the Financial Environment will continue to be a guide for improving the financial environment for banking and financial institutions and stakeholders. At the same time, financial literacy will continue to be strengthened through the integration of both curricula and promotional campaigns on the use of money, culture, credit and savings.
5. All branches of the National Bank of Cambodia, the Capital-Provinces, must continue to support the economic growth of the region through the provision of active and efficient cash management services and contribute to the promotion of financial literacy and customer protection through the Hotline system. Provide information and help solve problems related to the use of financial services to citizens.
At the same time, the branch must continue to cooperate and support the implementation of the Royal Government's public financial reform program to strengthen the transparency and accountability of cash management operations.
10. As the chair of ASEAN in Cambodia in 2022, the National Bank of Cambodia will contribute to strengthening regional financial integration and financial safety net through the liberalization of banking services, integration of payment systems, promotion of the use of regional currencies and financing mechanisms. For crisis prevention and resolution.
Companies from Japan, Malaysia and Singapore plan to build four cashew processing plants in three provinces of Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Companies from Japan, Malaysia and Singapore plan to build four cashew processing plants in three provinces Three will be in Kampong Thom, Kampong Cham and Kratie provinces in the near future, which will boost the export of cashew nuts to international markets to increase value added to farmers.
Uon Silot, President of the Cambodian Cashew Association, told Fresh News on January 15 that Japan's TPJ, which plans to build cashew processing plants in Kampong Thom and Kampong Cham, has already received permission from a major Japanese company. The company planned to build in November 2020, but was put on hold due to an outbreak of Kovid 19.
He said that although the specific construction has not been determined, but the company intends to build in 2022, which may be completed in 2025. The company's plan to open a factory due to local handicrafts that cooperate in the production of the company to supply less than the demand.
"Actually, the Japanese company wants to make Cambodia a cashew block for export to developed countries, because the Japanese standard is a standard recognized by Europe, so he does not focus on Japan at all, he focuses on the world market," he said. "Especially the rich country market."
Separately, another Malaysian company has already studied all the angles to build another cashew processing factory in Kratie province. Singapore-based Olympus, which also has a manufacturing facility in Vietnam, has indicated its intention to build a factory in Kampong Thom province. However, due to the problem of Kovid 19, the company suspended the study of the project but continued to buy raw materials for processing.
The president of the association stated that the reason for investors to choose the three provinces because these three provinces are the triangle of cashew nuts, with the largest number of cashew farmers, especially in Kampong Thom ranks first with the area of cashew cultivation. Most.
He also said that each factory will collect 20,000 tons of cashew nuts per year for processing, if the four factories will collect from 80,000 to 100,000 tons per year for farmers. Export to international market.
"When we have a factory in our district, first we help increase the value added to the farmers, we mean that the farmers can sell at a stable price, not like now. Nowadays, the cocktail trader can do whatever he wants, so if he has a factory, he can produce cashew nuts according to factory standards and sell them at the best price. Another benefit is to create jobs for workers. Mr. Uon Silot added.
According to the report of the Cambodian Cashew Association, the area under cashew cultivation is more than 490,000 hectares, but the association estimates that there may be up to 800,000 hectares. Cashew is the most widely grown in 10 provinces: Kampong Thom, Ratanakiri, Kampong Cham, Mondulkiri, Tbong Khmum, Stung Treng, Siem Reap, Kratie, Kampong Chhnang and Preah Vihear.
