NEC Receives 36 Complaints at Commune / Sangkat Councils
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) said that as of January 14, 2022, during the posting of the first voter list and the list of voters to be removed from the voter list. 2021 Commune / Sangkat Councils (CPCs) across the country have received a total of 36 complaints, all of which are separate complaints at the NEC level and at the Constitutional Council level. No.
According to a press release obtained by Fresh News on January 15, 2022, the filing, receipt and settlement of complaints during the posting of the initial voter list and the list of eligible voters will take place. Removed from the 2021 voter list has three stages, including:
* The filing of a complaint with the KRC shall be made no later than 10 days after the date of the first voter list posting and the settlement of the complaint shall be no later than 3 days after the date of receipt of the complaint.
* The filing of a complaint with the Constitutional Council shall be made no later than 5 days after the date of receipt of the NEC Decision (T.1203) and the resolution of the complaint shall be filed no later than 10 days after Day received the complaint.
At the same time, the NEC continued that the process of posting the initial voter list and the list of voters to be removed from the voter list in communes across the country in 2021 went smoothly in a calm environment. Violence and no threats.
Please be informed that the NEC will publish information on the process of filing, receiving and resolving complaints during the posting of the first voter list and the list of voters to be removed from the 2021 voter list in the future. Coming soon.
