Cambodian-Singaporean leaders agree on ASEAN foreign ministers to continue meeting to review ASEAN work, especially the work of special envoys
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Prime Minister of Singapore Lee Hsien Loong have agreed to continue the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting to review the work of ASEAN, especially the work of the Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair to facilitate the resolution of the crisis. Myanmar.
This agreement was made during an online video meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Ly Sean Long on January 14, 2022.
The resumption of the meeting came after the ASEAN Ministerial Retreat (AMM Retreat), scheduled for 18-19 January 2022 in Siem Reap, was postponed. This is due to the fact that it is difficult for many ASEAN foreign ministers to travel to the meeting.
In response, the Prime Minister of Singapore thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for informing him of the outcome of his visit to Nay Pyi Taw and also thanked Cambodia for its intention to contribute to resolving the country's crisis. This Myanmar. He stated that we really support the efforts of Cambodia, especially the role of the ASEAN Chair at this time, including the work of the Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair.
