Following is a press release from the NEC: From February, the authorities will fine those who store solid waste indiscriminately and dispose of garbage on time.
(Phnom Penh): From February 2022 onwards, the authorities will impose fines in accordance with the laws and regulations in force, as well as sue in court for actual misconduct for those who keep solid waste not properly divided between garbage. Wet and dry rubbish and dumping at the wrong time.
This was confirmed by Mr. Huot Hay, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh on the afternoon of January 14, 2021 in the ceremony to promote the management of solid construction in Phnom Penh at Phnom Penh Capital Hall before proceeding to impose fines in accordance with the law and the letter. Legal norms in force.
On behalf of Phnom Penh Governor Khuon Sreng, Mr. Huot Hay stated that the current meeting is aimed at promoting better waste management in Phnom Penh before imposing fines. According to the law.
He said that the reform of waste and solid waste management in Phnom Penh from the beginning to the end of the line has achieved proud results, including the bidding for a new company to provide cleaning, collection and transportation of waste. Hard in Phnom Penh is also done. Three companies have been selected and have started to improve their operations day by day from July 1, 2021.
The three companies include:
In order to implement the new system of solid waste management in Phnom Penh more effectively, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has introduced the separation, packaging, storage and disposal of solid waste, including solid waste and solid waste before discharge. Drain the water and put it into the sewer system properly. Separate solid waste into two types: wet waste and dry waste in separate bags.
Wet litter, such as food waste, organic waste, fruits, flowers, should be placed in black bags - dry litter, paper, cardboard, plastic, foam, metal, cans, bottles ... should be placed in white bags. The company will collect and transport solid waste packed in these two designated bags only according to the separate program. Putting solid waste in bags of colors other than black and white, the company will not collect.
People can buy these two colored bags in various markets. Do not pack hazardous waste such as glass fragments and sharp objects mixed with wet and dry rubbish. Properly dispose of these hazardous wastes in a separate bin or container, the company will collect every Sunday.
