(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment on January 14, 2022 presented data on the presence of various species of wildlife in Cambodia's protected areas in Pursat, Battambang and Koh Kong provinces.
With the presence of this rare species, Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, said that 10 endangered, endangered and endangered species were identified through data collected from Photographs of self-portraits taken by professional officials of the Ministry of Environment under the auspices of the Ministry of Environment's Cambodian Sustainable Landscape and Ecotourism Sustainability Project.
The senior official said that the Ministry of Environment would like to thank the efforts of professional officers of the Department of Environment, park rangers and local communities of Pursat, Battambang and Koh Kong provinces supported by the Ministry of Environment's Sustainable Landscape and Ecotourism Sustainability Project of the Ministry of Environment. Funding from the World Bank.
In addition, he said that in this study, the Ministry of Environment officials installed 49 automatic cameras, including 23 in the wildlife sanctuary in Pursat, 16 in Battambang and 10 in Koh Kong. .
In order to include: increase knowledge of methods to study and collect biodiversity data, identify the presence and absence of endangered and threatened species, as well as assess the status and distribution of important wildlife.
It should be noted that this is the second time that within the framework of the Sustainable Landscape and Ecotourism Sustainability Project in Cambodia, professional officials of the Ministry of Environment have collected data from automatic cameras to obtain images and videos of wildlife in protected areas.
It should be noted that the Cambodia Sustainable Landscape and Ecotourism Sustainability Project is funded by the World Bank and this project was officially launched on October 17, 2019 and is scheduled to end on December 31, 2025. The project aims to improve the management of protected areas, promote opportunities for ecotourism development, and to increase the value chain of non-timber forest products in the Cardamom and Tonle Sap landscape.
This project is divided into 5 components: 1: Strengthening the capacity to plan and manage landscape areas in protected areas, 2: Strengthen opportunities for the development of ecotourism and non-timber forest value chains, 3: Promoting cable connectivity Rural Access Roads: Fourth: Project Management, Monitoring and Evaluation, and Fifth: Emergency Response.
When selecting wildlife sanctuaries in Pursat, Battambang and Koh Kong provinces to install the camera, Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that because the protected area is covered by semi-dense forest mixed with bamboo forest and fields. Weeds.
In addition, the geographical location of the wildlife sanctuaries in these three provinces includes streams, lakes and rivers, which are excellent sources of water for wildlife and to support the national economic development that requires consistent management and conservation. According to guidelines and techniques.
With the good news of the discovery of many rare wildlife, on behalf of the Ministry of Environment, he called on all Cambodians to join together to stop eating wildlife meat, using wildlife products, and trading animals. Forests, which can pose a high risk to human health and contribute to the protection and preservation of Cambodia's natural resources and biodiversity to survive for generations to come.
On January 14, 2022, priority groups, including civil servants, the armed forces, doctors and journalists, received the fourth dose to continue the fight against the spread of Kovid 19. In particular, the new transformation "Omi Krong".
Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the National Committee for the Prevention of Kovid 19 Vaccine, also inspected the fourth dose at the National Center for Maternal and Child Health (Japanese Medicine). There was also the participation of Ms. Lee Iceland, a representative of the World Health Organization.
According to Ms. O Vandin, the fourth vaccination process was initially carried out only in Phnom Penh, using the Pfizer vaccine, while other provinces will start when there is enough cold storage for the vaccine.
The official in charge of the vaccine claims that the Pfizer vaccine requires very cold temperatures to be stored up to -80 degrees Celsius, so it can not be sent to the provinces at this time. She said that during February 2022, if nothing changes, the cold equipment will arrive in Cambodia and will be distributed to the provinces to store this type of vaccine.
Despite taking the next step in vaccinating against measles 19, the third dose, or booster dose, is still active across the country, so people who are ready for the booster dose can go to a health facility. Which is near their house. This is according to what Ms. O Vandin highlighted.
For those who have not yet received all the basic doses, Ms. O Vandin noted that the number is still small because they seem to be uncertain in their decision due to physical illness, but she said the vaccine. Kovid 19 is so important that individuals need to be fully vaccinated to strengthen their immune system.
At this point, Ms. O Vandin also called on people who have not been vaccinated in all local doses to hurry to get everyone, and those who need to be vaccinated should also be vaccinated as well. Kovid 19 can actually prevent an individual from dying from Kovid 19 and reduce hospitalization during this deadly disease.
It should be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, on the morning of January 14, 2022, already vaccinated against Kovid 19 at his residence. Takhmao City.
With the fourth dose, Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on people to vaccinate everyone, both at the local level and at the dose to protect ourselves, our families, our villages, our communes and our nation.
