BEIJING: China hopes that the United States can improve the conditions and environment conducive to the expansion of trade cooperation after the purchase of US goods by China in the past two years is lower than the target set in A trade agreement established under the Donald Trump administration. According to Reuters.
Reuters reports, citing data compiled by the Peterson Institute for International Economics, that China could not live up to its promises made in the "Phase 1" trade agreement to create US purchases of 200 b. Millions of dollars during 2020 and 2021 compared to the level in 2017, achieving only about 60 percent of the target by November 2021.
"Since the agreement came into force, China has made great efforts to overcome the difficulties posed by the effects of the epidemic," Shu Jueting, a spokesman for the Chinese Ministry of Commerce, said in an online news conference. "Illness, the global economic downturn and supply disruptions have prompted the implementation of agreements between the two sides."
"We hope the United States can create a favorable environment and conditions for both sides to expand trade cooperation," he said.
He added that the two countries' trade task force is maintaining communication.
US Secretary of Agriculture Tom Vilsack said Tuesday that the United States will continue to press China to fully implement the trade agreement before any delays are discussed. According to Reuters.
