Minister of Education Instructions on Maintaining Safety Measures During the Announcement of Bankruptcy Exam Results
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on January 14, 2022 announced the maintenance of safety measures during the announcement of the results of the high school diploma exam.
According to a letter from the Ministry of Education, the Ministry will announce the results of the Higher Secondary Diploma Examination Exam Session: December 27, 2021 in Phnom Penh and Kandal Province on the afternoon of January 14, 2022 and in other provinces on the morning of January 15. 2022.
The announcement of the results of the high school diploma exam will be made in an environment where Cambodians need to be extremely vigilant as some new cases of the Kovid-19 mutation virus emerge.
The Minister of Education stated that during the announcement of the high school diploma results, the following safety measures should be promoted:
1: Disseminate to the candidates of the high school diploma exam that the results of the exam will be announced by live broadcast at the examination center and will also be posted on the official Facebook of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, so candidates do not need to follow Results at the examination center.
2. Set up a place to post exam results away from the playground or gathering place of other students and must declare a ban on students who are not involved in the exam to enter the place to post exam results.
3: Tie a rope or put a fence around the location to post exam results as much as possible.
