Samdech Techo Hun Sen has emphasized that taking office as Prime Minister after Samdech served as Minister of Foreign Affairs, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs for 6 years and also served as Acting Prime Minister for more than 3 months. When Chan Si went to Moscow for medical treatment and died in the Soviet Union.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, who has been the Prime Minister since the youngest and continues to be the oldest Prime Minister under the support of the people, once said that the position of Prime Minister for the first time. Samdech received the support of party and state leaders. Especially Samdech Heng Samrin, Samdech Chea Sim, Mr. Say Phu Thong and Mr. Chea Soth etc.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, who took the life to put out the flames of war, recalled that Samdech's inauguration as Prime Minister came at a time when the country was severely short of food due to the floods and drought in 1984.
Despite leading the country in such a food shortage, the young prime minister told the National Assembly that no one should be left to starve unknowingly and unresolved. This theory has survived to the present day, not just the theory, but the actual activities of the CPP as a whole.
The beginning of his life as Prime Minister in the country, just liberated from the flames of war and disturbed by the flames of war along the border, as well as the economic blockade from neighboring countries, is the most difficult discipline of leadership for Samdech Techo. Hun Sen.
* Cambodia's economic development under the leadership of strong man Techo Sen
The veteran life of the veteran who went through and overcame countless battles was fraught with difficulties as the country was economically besieged by liberal countries and disrupted by the Khmer Rouge's attempted occupation. Country again.
The 1980s was a time when Cambodia struggled to overcome all obstacles. Cambodia is considered the poorest country in Southeast Asia. The poorest Cambodians depend on farming, rice, and small-scale trade, with no major trade.
Apart from the economic problems, there are many other issues such as education, training, human resources and ending the fires of war in Cambodia are all things that this young Prime Minister has to struggle to decide as the one responsible for fate. Nation and people.
After the 1993 elections, and with the help of countries in Asia and Europe, the momentum of Cambodia's development has been steadily rising under the sharp development policies of the Royal Government. Led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
It cannot be forgotten that, despite foreign aid and clear policies, Cambodia could not be as strong in its development if the Khmer Rouge movement along the border Khmer-Thai is not closed.
Under the clear vision that the end of the border war is the key to national development, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has launched a plan and implemented a win-win policy. Negotiations with the Khmer Rouge until the Khmer Rouge resistance forces took refuge under the roof of the same Royal Government, leading Cambodia to end the fighting between its own nation on December 28, 1998.
Cambodia, after being liberated from the genocidal regime with a population of just over 5 million, has become a country of about 16 million people today.
Cambodia, which used to lack a system of roads, bridges and roads for people to travel and serve in the past, is becoming a country with a system of roads, bridges from one province to another, including large bridges across the river. Many that have never been in the history of Cambodia.
Bridges across the river were born during the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Neak Leung Bridge, Monivong II Bridge, Koh Thom Bridge, Chroy Changva II Bridge, Sekong Bridge, Stung Treng Province, Prek Kdam Bridge, Pretamak Bridge, Mekong Stung Treng Bridge and Takhmao Bridge, Prek Pnov Bridge. ... etc.
Phnom Penh, with few residential buildings left over from the fires of war, is becoming a capital with many high-rise commercial buildings.
In total, during his 37 years as Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has been at the helm of the Cambodian navy with the utmost care to restore and bring this miserable country to the forefront of a new era of development. All areas are remarkable and have helped people to have a better life. Build honor, fame, pride and hope for progress and prosperity.
Through political messages, the Cambodian Prime Minister is setting his goal of pushing Cambodian ships to become high-middle-income countries by 2030 and high-income countries by 2050, while large investment projects with thousands of dollars Millions of dollars are emerging today.
