French Embassy Welcomes Young Cambodian Doctors Returning from France
(Phnom Penh): The French Embassy in Cambodia on the night of January 13 hosted a reception for 79 young Cambodian doctors who have completed a one-year internship at hospitals in France, where they Provided invaluable support to French doctors as well as learning from those experienced doctors.
The event, which was attended by many Cambodian-French health professionals, was an opportunity to highlight the important role of doctors who have been at the forefront of the fight against Kovid 19. Such as working on various battlefields of the health sector to treat patients.
According to a press release issued by Fresh News, the French Ambassador to Cambodia, Jacques Pellegrini, reminded of the importance of cooperation between France and Cambodia in the field of health, which is more meaningful in the context. The current crisis of the Kovid 19.
The Ambassador commended the young doctor and thanked his Cambodian counterparts for their support.
Health is among the longest-standing areas of the partnership between France and Cambodia and is one of the most vibrant and important. Since 1996, more than 900 Cambodian medical and pharmaceutical students have continued their studies in France to pursue various medical majors within the framework of the DFMS / A (Advanced Medical / Diploma in Medicine) program.
Of the 44 countries, Cambodia ranks fourth in the number of countries sending students to study health in France.
