Mr. Chhay Sophal, book compiler and professor of information, told Fresh News that in order to commemorate the active, strategic and responsible efforts in the history of humanity of the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially the Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen. In order to save the lives of the people from Kov-19, he also spent a lot of time monitoring, recording and compiling events for this book.
He said that it was not easy when the disease broke out in the community and, as Samdech Techo said, bombs can destroy a house and a village by attacking them in war, but if An exploding economic bomb could destroy the entire country, which is why the Royal Government is seriously considering one shoulder trying to improve public health while the other shoulder trying to stabilize macroeconomics by curbing inflation.
The author of this book goes on to say that some Cambodians are quick to forget, so this record is indeed a reminder of the history of humankind in this period.
Mr. Chhay Sophal also stated that the release of the book on January 14 is also intended to commemorate the 37th anniversary of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's inauguration as Prime Minister since 1985.
"It is undeniable that the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Ministries of State Institutions, the Armed Forces, including the Cambodian Red Cross, Samdech Techo Volunteer Doctors (TYDA) "And the medical union of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia has joined hands in difficult times to save lives during the epidemic."
According to Chhay Sophal, in addition to describing the country's activities in the fight against this deadly disease, some regional and international political events, including developments involving Cambodia in the context of the epidemic Kovid-19 is also included in this record.
Political events include the amendment of the Constitution, the closure of the top position for Cambodians of more than one nationality, the Prime Minister of the Cambodian People's Party, the issue of Cambodia and the US-China, the issue of Cambodia, Myanmar and ASEAN-China, as well as the willingness of Cambodia to share abroad. Also. This is according to the description from Mr. Chhay Sophal.
The book was initially printed in 5,000 copies, each costing more than $ 14. According to Mr. Chhay Sophal, this book, in addition to selling some at the banks, he also distributed at the National Library and the libraries of public and private universities in the capital-province.
Then another journalist went on to ask, "Why did you write a book that everyone knew?" Mr. Chhay Sophal replied, "In this generation, some of them are not very interested, but in later generations, the book is even more important and Smer has already thought about this." "For example, some of the scriptures that our ancestors wrote in the past may not have been very interesting at that time, but they are valuable in later times to the present."
