(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neou Dim, Chief of Vallisor Commune, Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province, made a strong impression on the press conference on commune development in Kampong Speu Province, organized by the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit. This interest came after he presented some of the work he has done for the people, both in terms of services and development in the commune, and has earned him the support and satisfaction of the people.
Vallisor commune can be considered as a model commune in Kampong Speu province and has developed remarkably. The progress of this commune is due to the development policy of the Royal Government as well as the provincial level, but the progress in the commune also comes from the significant contribution of the commune chief and commune council. Born from the election every 5 years.
Neou Dim is a commune chief in Vallisor commune from the Cambodian People's Party. He has been running and working in Vallisor commune for 4 terms. In this new term, Mr. Neou Dim also gained the trust of the leaders of the Cambodian People's Party and elected him as the candidate for commune chief of the Cambodian People's Party in this commune.
The decision to nominate Mr. Neou Dim as the first candidate in Vallisor commune by the Cambodian People's Party after examining the excellent performance, especially to gain the respect of the people as voters in In the commune itself.
Answer the question, what is the strategy that leads the commune chief to receive the support and love of the people? Mr. Neou Dim shared many experiences that have been completed in his commune for the past 20 years.
Mr. Neou Dim shared the factors that lead to the people's satisfaction and support: the development efforts in the commune and the focus on providing services quickly. In addition to these two factors, Mr. Nou Dim also prepared food stored at the commune hall to distribute to people when there is a shortage.
Mr. Neou Dim stated that through this activity to serve the people, he never worried about losing the election in his commune. "I'm not worried about the election, why?" He said. "Because we know the morale of the people, there is nothing to worry about. 9 out of 9 know, but that's it."
