If the authorities suspect this case of electric shock. US releases report accusing China over South China Sea
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The United States on Wednesday rejected China's claim to sovereignty over the South China Sea, which it considers illegal on the basis of geography or history. This was released by Reuters on Thursday afternoon, January 13, 2022.
In a 47-page study, the State Department's Office of Oceans, International Environment and Science states that China has no basis under international law to claim its disputed sovereignty. Philippines, Vietnam and other countries in Southeast Asia.
"China's claim to sovereignty or exclusive jurisdiction over the South China Sea is illegal and seriously undermines maritime and international law," the report said. Convention. The convention cited by the report refers to the 1982 United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea, which was ratified by China while the United States has not yet ratified it.
