(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neou Dim, Chief of Vallisor Commune, Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province, in his position as Commune Chief for the last 4 terms, he removed 3 Commune Clerks for obstructing the provision of services to the people in the Commune. .
Mr. Neou Dim is a model commune chief in fulfilling his duties to serve the people in Vallisor commune. Due to his dominance in serving the people as well as the construction and development of the commune, Mr. Neou Dim has been elected by the Cambodian People's Party as a candidate for the 4th term of Vallisor commune chief and has always received popular support from the people.
In response to the request of the media to share experiences in leading the commune in the press conference on the progress of the commune in Kampong Speu organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government on January 13, 2022, Mr. Neou Dim said. To satisfy the people is the effort to build and develop in the commune and to provide good services to the people.
Recalling the work of providing services to the people, Mr. Neou Dim also reminded of the obstruction of some work due to the commune clerk and made him request to remove all three commune clerks.
Commune / Sangkat clerks play an important role in the commune / sangkat administration, and in particular the clerk is assigned to hold the commune / sangkat seal to cast on various documents of the commune / sangkat administration as a mechanism to ensure balance and cleanliness in the administration. Commune / Sangkat.
Mr. Neou Dim claimed that he had difficulty in providing services to the people because he sometimes had to wait for the seal from the clerk to cast on the people's letters.
According to Mr. Neou Dim, this problem no longer exists because the Royal Government has delegated power to the provincial level to have the right to change clerks, so clerks have also changed their attitude and paid attention to their duties.
