Japan is considering providing assistance to Cambodia for demining and other areas
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Japan is considering providing assistance to the Royal Government of Cambodia for demining and other areas.
This intention was expressed during Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and Mr. Hayashi Yoshimasa, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan, on January 11, 2022.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated that during the meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, on behalf of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, expressed his sincere gratitude to the Government and people of Japan for their continued assistance to support Cambodia's socio-economic development, including assistance. It is invaluable to support Cambodia's fight against Kovid-19 and to reduce the negative effects caused by this global epidemic.
