Ministry of Foreign Affairs announces the results of a telephone conversation between Cambodian and Japanese diplomats
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia issued a press release on the outcome of a telephone conversation between Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and Mr. Hayashi Yoshimasa, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan, on January 11, 2022
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated that during the meeting, the Deputy Prime Minister on behalf of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia sincerely thanked the Government and the people of Japan for their continued assistance to support Cambodia's socio-economic development, including invaluable assistance in Supporting Cambodia's fight against Kovid-19 and reducing the negative effects of this global pandemic.
Mr Hayazi congratulated Cambodia on its chairmanship of ASEAN this year and reaffirmed Japan's support and readiness to work closely with Cambodia for the success of the ASEAN Chairmanship.
In addition to Japan's past assistance to Cambodia in response to the global Kovid-19 pandemic, the development of the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port as a core port of Cambodia and in other areas, Minister Hayazi informed Deputy Prime Minister Prakash. Sokhon said Japan was considering providing more assistance to Cambodia for demining, water supply and electricity, among other sectors.
In response, Foreign Minister Hayazi congratulated the Deputy Prime Minister on his appointment as Special Envoy of the ASEAN Chair and reaffirmed Japan's support for Cambodia's efforts and coordination to create a conducive environment for ASEAN. Negotiations on the Myanmar issue. The two foreign ministers also exchanged views on regional and international issues of common concern and interest, including the Korean Peninsula.
At the end of the dialogue, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon expressed his eagerness to welcome the visit of Foreign Minister Hayazi to Cambodia at a convenient time. Mr Hayazi looks forward to visiting and participating in relevant ASEAN meetings this year.
