(Phnom Penh): The Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC) has decided to issue certificates for the registration of investment projects of nine other companies with an investment capital of more than $ 38 million to invest in Cambodia, creating more than 10,000 jobs.
According to the Ministry of Economy and Finance, in the first 11 months of 2021, the investment situation in Cambodia has not improved. In the first 11 months, the total number of private investment projects was 107, down 34 projects. Compared to the same period last year.
Ministry of Foreign Affairs announces the outcome of the meeting between the Head of the Cambodian Diplomatic Mission and the Deputy Foreign Minister of the United Kingdom
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation has issued a press release on the outcome of a meeting between Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, and Amanda Milling, Deputy Minister for Foreign Affairs of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Kampuchea. And Development of the United Kingdom, held on 11 January 2022.
A statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated that during the meeting, Mr. Prak Sokhon conveyed the gratitude of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to the Prime Minister of the United Kingdom, Boris Johnson, for his participation. Video of the 13th Asia-Europe Summit, which Cambodia successfully hosted and chaired in November 2021.
The Deputy Prime Minister thanked the United Kingdom for continuing to provide preferential tariffs (GSP) to Cambodia, along with other Least Developed Countries (LDCs), and for providing socio-economic assistance in the areas of education, demining, environment and NGOs. Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia.
In response, Ms. Amanda Milling thanked Cambodia for its strong support of the United Kingdom in becoming an ASEAN dialogue partner. She expressed her strong commitment to support Cambodia as the chair of ASEAN in 2022 and looked forward to further strengthening bilateral relations between Cambodia and the United Kingdom and ASEAN-UK cooperation, especially the ASEAN-UK Action Plan. English for 2022-2026.
Both sides noted a decrease in trade volume due to the impact of Kovid-19 on trade activities. In this regard, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon encouraged more UK investors to invest in Cambodia, taking into account the benefits of entering the Cambodian market, including the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP). Cambodia-China Free Trade and Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement.
The two sides recalled Dominic Raab's visit last June and shared a common desire to further strengthen bilateral relations and cooperation in areas of mutual benefit. Go back and forth, especially on trade-related cooperation. In addition, the two sides agreed to seek more opportunities in various fields of cooperation.
Mr. Prak Sokhon proposed a political consultation mechanism between Cambodia and the United Kingdom. He also reaffirmed Cambodia's support for the UK-led "Global Ocean Alliance" and its participation in the "Highly Ambitious Unity for Nature and Humanity".
The visit of Samdech Techo Prime Minister is to break the deadlock for the step-by-step progress on the implementation of the five-point unanimous agreement. Any peace process to resolve the crisis in Myanmar must be led by Myanmar and owned by Myanmar.
Ms. Amanda Milling thanked Mr. Prak Sokhon for informing her about Cambodia's priorities as chair of ASEAN in 2022 and the current state of the complexities of the Myanmar crisis. She reaffirmed the UK's commitment to supporting the ASEAN Community and looked forward to further enhancing ASEAN-UK relations.
The meeting ended in an atmosphere of mutual understanding and frankness and honesty.
ASEAN Tourism Forum is an opportunity to promote "Cambodia as a safe tourism destination" and announce the reopening of tourism in the ASEAN region
(Sihanoukville): The ASEAN Tourism Forum 2022 will be a milestone in the official re-opening of tourism destinations in the ASEAN region after being disrupted by the 19-year-old Kovid epidemic for more than two years. This international will help promote Cambodia as a safe tourism destination in the ASEAN region.
Minister Thong Khon confirmed to the meeting that "the ASEAN Tourism Forum 2022 will be an important event in the official re-opening of tourism destinations in the ASEAN region." He expressed optimism that the international event would help promote "Cambodia as a safe tourism destination in ASEAN."
The Minister said that this preparatory work is to make the event run smoothly, safely and be able to respond to all situations, avoid any shortcomings until the owner loses something. In addition, to help keep the leaders, delegates and participants safe, which can promote the promotion of Cambodia as a safe tourism destination.
The three delegations and the whole meeting agreed to promote the 4th dose of vaccination to the leaders, civil servants and the Cambodian team responsible for organizing the ASEAN Tourism Forum (for those who reach the 4th dose) to strengthen safety. Together during and after the event.
The meeting discussed the coordination of transportation of senior national and international officials from Phnom Penh International Airport, Kang Keng International Airport and the international border gates adjacent to some neighboring countries, as well as accommodation, food and programs. Some entertainment. In addition, there was a discussion on the work of monitoring, coordinating and maintaining security and order to the leaders of the delegation as well as the whole program.
The meeting discussed the protocol of each meeting program, the content of the dissemination, the coordination with the media and national and international media, and the preparation of the ASEAN Tourism Ministers' press conference to announce the opening of tourism in the ASEAN region. Officially back.
