Suspect Arrested in Takhmao City for Stealing Photograph of Woman Taking a Bath
(Kandal): Police in Prek Hoor commune, Takhmao city, arrested a man after receiving a complaint from a woman who allegedly stole a photo of her while taking a bath in the bathroom.
This case happened on January 11, 2022 at 05:55 at the bathroom of a rented house in Batachi 1 village, Sangkat Prek Ho, Takhmao city, Kandal province.
The victim was 20-year-old Masoth, and the suspect was 38-year-old Khmer male.
Police recounted the incident that at the time of the incident, while the victim was taking a bath in a shared bathroom, the suspect, who was staying in a rented room next door, entered the adjoining bathroom. With the victim and put the phone to take pictures through the hole in the floor.
At that time, the victim saw the suspect's phone, stole the camera and downloaded the phone to see the body in the suspect's phone. The suspect immediately returned the phone call to the victim and apologized to the victim as the victim deleted the image and returned the phone to the suspect.
When the suspect went missing, the victim filed a complaint at the Prek Hoor police station. When the suspect returned from work, the police detained him for questioning at the police station and then sent him to the Takhmao City Police Inspectorate for further action. Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Removes Colonel Huot Seiha from Samrong Thom Police Station Post
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, has decided to remove Colonel Huot Seiha from the post of Samrong Thom Administrative Police Station of Kien Svay District Police Inspectorate of Kandal Provincial Police.
Although the dismissal and demotion of the police chief did not specify the reasons for the "national police force misconduct", some reports said the removal was suspected of involvement. Three young men were charged with drug trafficking and extorting $ 3,500 in exchange for their release.
The following is the decision of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng: In 2021, the insurance premium of Cambodia will increase to 300 million dollars
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Bou Chanphiro, Director General of the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia, on January 12, 2022, highlighted that in 2021, the insurance premium of Cambodia will increase to about 300 million US dollars, despite the global Kovid-19 crisis. Anyway.
In addition, the Director General of the Cambodian Insurance Regulator noted that the Cambodian insurance market is growing rapidly with an average annual growth rate of about 25 percent.
Mr. Bou Chanpirou said that the number of insurance companies has now increased to 40, with 20 insurance agents and banks partnering with insurance companies to sell insurance products.
According to Mr. Rath Sovannak, Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, the insurance sector is part of the promotion of the financial sector in Cambodia in line with the financial sector development strategy and the national strategy on the financial environment.
He stated that allowing banks and financial institutions to do business with insurance products will benefit all parties, including:
* Banking and financial institutions can establish more relationships, produce services, receive additional costs and expand credit funds for their operations.
* Customers can reduce costs with the use of financial services with convenience and access to financial services with better quality and reasonable prices.
* Insurance companies can expand their customer base, reduce costs, generate revenue, share products and services with banking and financial institutions, and create a market for Cambodian insurance.
