(Kandal): An investigating judge of Kandal Provincial Court has decided to charge and detain a man after stealing a picture of a woman taking a bath in the bathroom. This is according to Mr. So Sarin, spokesman for Kandal Provincial Court, confirmed to Fresh News on January 12, 2022.
The spokesman confirmed that Ouk Sovannarith, an investigating judge at Kandal Provincial Court, had decided to charge the suspect with "infringing on the rights of an individual image", a crime punishable by imprisonment.
Please be informed that the police in Prek Hoor commune, Takhmao city, arrested a man after receiving a complaint from a woman claiming that someone had stolen a photo of her while taking a bath in the bathroom. This case happened on January 11, 2022 at 05:55 at the bathroom of a rented house in Batachi 1 village, Sangkat Prek Ho, Takhmao city, Kandal province.
The victim was 20-year-old M.S.T., and the suspect was NT, a 38-year-old Cambodian male, a factory worker.
When the suspect went missing, the victim filed a complaint at the Prek Hoor police station. When the suspect returned from work, he was detained by the police for questioning at the police station and then sent to the Takhmao City Police Inspectorate for further proceedings.
