Mr. Hun Many offers condolences to the families of three demining officers who died in a landmine explosion in Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province
(Phnom Penh): Mr. HUN Many, Member of Parliament for Kampong Speu Province and President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, expressed his deepest condolences to the families of the bodies of three demining officers who lost their lives in demining missions and An unexploded ordnance in Sen Tech village, Moratok commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province.
This tragic incident reminds us again of the consequences of war, which, despite years of peace, continues to plague and threaten the lives of its people.
As a country that has gone through the tragedy of decades of internal conflict, we clearly understand the value of peace for humanity. "Peace and well-being of the people is not only a precious" jewel "for our country, but also for our region and the world."
