Taipei: The Taiwanese parliament on Tuesday approved an additional $ 8.6 billion budget to boost military development to protect its island security in the face of threats. This was released by the AFP news agency on Tuesday evening, January 11, 2022.
The government of Taiwan has set a special budget for five years to support the military from 2022 onwards. It was formed after several Chinese fighter jets moved into the island's air defense zone.
In 2021, Taiwan recorded a total of 970 Chinese military aircraft flying into its air defense zone. According to an AFP report, that number more than doubled from 380 in 2020. In particular, the above budget will be used in accordance with the annual budget for the military sector, which has already been approved 17 billion US dollars.
