International Analysis: By 2022, Unity Can Overcome Kovid 19 Outbreak
BEIJING: As 2022 approaches, many people consider overcoming the epidemic of Kovid 19 a wish in the new year. Tedros, Director-General of the World Health Organization, also issued a New Year message saying that if countries work together to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, humanity will overcome the disease. Kovid 19 in 2022.
Effective prevention and control work should be done, and the economic and social impact caused by Kovid 19 should be kept to a minimum. Governments have been working to find such a balance. First, the international community must increase vaccination rates, achieve immunization to the best of its ability to create effective barriers to collective immunity.
Finally, countries should work together to prevent the spread of political viruses. Together, facing the common threat of humanity, only by uniting, mourning, and caring for one another can we overcome this vicious Kovid 19 disease. By 2022, the international community must continue to work together to prevent the politicization of Kovid 19 or paint and slander, and should continue to achieve the prevention of Kovid 19 by science and take targeted action.
In particular, developed countries need to abandon ideological bias, support developing countries and low-income countries in terms of capital, technology and capacity, in order to jointly achieve the ideal of "ending the spread of disease." Kovid 19 in 2022. "
