Report on the implementation of yesterday's measures: Educate and disseminate the law in 39 locations, educate 100 people on road traffic
(Phnom Penh): In the implementation of measures across Cambodia on January 10, 2022, yesterday, there were no perpetrators, health measures and administrative measures. However, yesterday, the police educated and disseminated the law in 39 locations and educated 100 road traffic targets (65 vehicles).
This is according to the announcement of the Kovid-19 Law Enforcement Commission, which was received by Fresh News this morning. To China succeeds as expected
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian and Chinese sides have both confirmed the success as expected around the risk analysis and control process of Cambodian gourds through a video made in the first week of January 2022. .
The Chinese Customs Administration conducted a video analysis and risk assessment of Cambodian longan to implement the relevant consensus set by the Chinese and Cambodian leaders and to complete the procedures for testing and inspecting Cambodian longan exported to China. Fast.
From January 4 to 6, 2022, the Chinese Customs Administration conducted a risk analysis and inspection of Cambodian longan through the video. Live location.
During the evaluation, the team inspected 3 orchards in Pailin and Battambang provinces and 2 packaging factories in Pailin and Kampong Speu provinces, as well as phytosanitary and safety laboratories.
Speaking to Fresh News, Mr. Ngin Chhay, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Agriculture, confirmed that the Chinese and Cambodian working groups had inspected a total of three locations in the past two days and places. Packing, washing and killing the harmful components in 2 locations.
"After two days of evaluation, the representative of the Customs Working Group of the People's Republic of China concluded that our plantations were in good condition, which could be in line with China's import standards," said Ngin Chhay. "There are only minor adjustments."
He added that the Cambodian packaging site has already been set up in Pailin province and another is underway, so it will be completed when Cambodia receives the technical protocol in accordance with Chinese requirements.
He stressed that the overall assessment of the Chinese side is good, and so far the online evaluation team has been submitting a report to the customs team in Beijing to review the decision to respond to the country. Cambodia.
In the past, Cambodian gourds were exported to China by companies from neighboring countries only due to hygienic conditions, which made it impossible for Cambodia to export gourds directly to China.
In Cambodia, there is an area of ten thousand hectares of Pailin longan, of which the harvested area is about 8,000 hectares, with a yield of between 15 and 20 tons per hectare, which yields more than 100,000 per year. Tons.
