The White House responded immediately, but suspicions arose that Biden had a long-standing problem in the context of the Republican Party's use of the issue to undermine Biden's popularity. . However, the White House has denied rumors that the president is ill, with Biden even planning to run for president again in 2024.
Of course, age is a separate issue, but the main issue is that now Biden's popularity has plummeted compared to the day he was sworn in in January 2021. The handling of the COVID-19 crisis and the fall of the US-backed Afghan government at the hands of the Taliban were the main reasons for Biden's declining popularity.
