The Ministry of Labor announces the implementation of standard operating principles on the operation and management of factories in the new normal trajectory in the context of Kovid-19
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has announced the implementation of standard operating principles on the operation and management of factories in the new normal environment in the context of Kovid-19 disease to ensure the sustainability of the business production chain, maintaining job stability. And income that benefits both employers and workers by contributing to the prevention of risks arising from the spread of infectious diseases, especially Kovid-19.
This announcement was made under the presidency of Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, on the morning of January 10, 2022.
The key points of this standard operating principle include: 1: Mechanisms of operation and management 2: Measures of work processes in a new normal trajectory (before the start, during and after the end of the daily work process) 3: Positive case management 194: Risk assessment 5: Inspection, monitoring and evaluation mechanisms
The Minister called on factory owners, enterprises, workers and all relevant partners to continue to cooperate with ministry officials to promote the implementation of this standard to be highly effective and responsible.
