Key Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen Inaugurating National Road No. 5 on Former Battlefield Land
(Phnom Penh): Battambang and Banteay Meanchey Province, the land of Cambodia's bitter former battlefield, on Monday morning, January 10, 2022, achieved a smooth road connecting the two provinces, National Road No. 5, with a length of nearly 85 km. M.
The inauguration ceremony of this important road for living and economy of Cambodia was presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia.
During the inauguration ceremony, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia gave a speech for about 1 hour and 40 minutes, the following are the main contents of Samdech:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he was very happy to receive the new achievements of National Road No. 4 North connecting Battambang and Banteay Meanchey. Samdech Techo stated that this section of National Road No. 5 is an achievement born of the cooperation between Cambodia and Japan.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that National Road No. 5 is a good road. Samdech Techo thanked the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, the Mine Authority and all relevant authorities for their joint efforts to bring about the presence of National Road No. 5.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that just one more year, National Road No. 5 connecting Prek Kdam to Thla Mam in Pursat province will be ready. While from Thla Mam to Battambang province may also be ready.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the Cambodian government and people for helping to build roads and bridges in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Japan has contributed to peace and development in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in order to find peace in Cambodia, it was decided to spend time with the Japanese leaders from 7 pm to 2 am.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the process of finding peace in Cambodia has a lot of contribution from the Japanese side.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that 2022 is the 30th anniversary of Japan sending peacekeepers abroad and sending them to Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Japanese Navy Self-Defense Forces will be preparing to visit the Ream Naval Base when visiting Cambodia this year.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is the exporter of Japanese peacekeepers abroad and the people of Japan should be proud of the mission of Japanese peacekeepers who are carrying out peacekeeping activities in the world.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen commemorates the war with the Khmer Rouge in Battambang province. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the war at that time was a strategic mistake that led to the Khmer Rouge troops breaking the line and seizing some territory.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he saw clearly that the war could not be ended. Due to this, Samdech set up talks to find an end to the war.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that when there is war, roads are destroyed, bridges are destroyed, bridges are destroyed, schools are destroyed, nothing can be done.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the lessons of Cambodia are sufficient, which requires that we jointly protect the peace in order to achieve the construction and development of Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that after Samdech put an end to the flames of war, the number of tasks that Samdech must pay attention to is to turn the flames of war into a market and development.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Kovid 19 destroyed Cambodia but could not completely destroy it, apparently the road construction project is still underway.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the relevant actors and people who followed the call of the Royal Government to vaccinate and implement measures as set out by the Royal Government.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls for continued vaccination to boost the fourth dose.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces that he has ordered an additional 5 million doses of vaccine, while the remaining 10 million doses are in stock. The order is to ensure that citizens have adequate vaccines for the booster dose.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Japan has announced its support for Samdech's visit to Myanmar to resolve the Myanmar issue.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the scripture that Samdech used to negotiate with Myanmar is the ASEAN Five-Point Convention and the ASEAN Charter.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the results of his visit to Myanmar are threefold: the postponement of the ceasefire, assistance and dialogue with Myanmar stakeholders.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he had instructed Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon to seek coordination with ASEAN to implement the ceasefire in Myanmar.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that it would be very good that there would be no war and no armed clashes in Myanmar in order to lead to elections and solutions.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed hope that ASEAN will work hard to resolve the Myanmar issue. Samdech Techo stated that the Myanmar issue cannot end until Cambodia chairs ASEAN, it will continue to Indonesia as ASEAN chair.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks Japan to provide material and technical support for humanitarian aid operations in Myanmar.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this action was not an intervention by Myanmar, but a facilitation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the reactions to Samdech's visit to Myanmar are the opposition in Cambodia, along with the people of Myanmar.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he did not care about the reaction of some Myanmar people to his efforts on the Myanmar crisis, but to help the people of Myanmar avoid the flames of war.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen told the people of Myanmar that Cambodia is fed up with divisions and the flames of war.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the establishment of a mechanism to provide assistance to the people of Myanmar without discrimination is necessary.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that establishing a ceasefire and providing assistance to the people is a necessary task before reaching a dialogue with stakeholders made by ASEAN envoys.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is poor but has a wide heart, in which the vaccine, which is part of Cambodia through the ASEAN Center, Cambodia has given to all of Myanmar worth a total of about 1 million dollars.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the budget provided to Cambodia for the development of road, bridge and port infrastructure has a total budget of approximately $ 1.4 billion.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he intends to appoint the President of the Japan Aid Center as an advisor to the President of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) to help resolve the Myanmar crisis.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen told the former ASEAN Secretary-General, a Singaporean, that ASEAN's five principles of unanimity on the issue in Myanmar did not mention the election.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that his visit to Myanmar yielded results beyond his expectations. In particular, the consent of General Ong Ming Lang allowed the ASEAN envoys to meet with the parties to the conflict.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that his visit to Myanmar was more successful than expected, especially with the consent of General Ong Ming Lang, allowing the ASEAN envoy to meet with the parties to the conflict.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that those who oppose the ceasefire as well as provide assistance to Myanmar are the ones who want the shootings and the famine in Myanmar.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech will visit the Japanese Navy Self-Defense Forces when entering Cambodia if allowed.
