Letter to readers: "Prime Minister Hun Sen presses key to pave the way for a solution to the Myanmar problem"
(Phnom Penh): The visit of Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen on behalf of the Cambodian leadership and chair of the ASEAN rotating presidency to Myanmar is an important key in paving the way for a solution to the crisis in this country.
In fact, of the five ASEAN consensus points, at least three are the initiative of the Cambodian leader. In particular, the results of the current visit of Prime Minister Hun Sen reflect almost all points.
Cambodia's efforts in general and the efforts of Prime Minister Hun Sen in particular are only for the harmony of ASEAN, as well as for the harmony of Myanmar.
Therefore, this effort will definitely be strongly encouraged by the peace-loving, ASEAN-loving and peace-loving people of Myanmar.
On the contrary, there are those who seem to want to see ASEAN split and want to see Myanmar continue to bleed, instead hindering and attacking Cambodia's efforts. However, the outcome of Prime Minister Hun Sen's visit to Myanmar has really paved the way for a solution.
The results of this visit are also among the five points of ASEAN consensus. Therefore, we can say that Prime Minister Hun Sen's visit to Myanmar is very important for the regional and global context, because the issue of Myanmar is currently receiving a lot of attention around the world.
Now the key to a solution has been opened by Prime Minister Hun Sen. Yet stakeholders, both outside and in conflict in Myanmar itself, need to show a willingness to find a solution. Cambodia, as the chair of ASEAN in 2022, has already demonstrated its commitment, as well as practical actions in its efforts to resolve the Myanmar issue.
The time ahead will confirm to critics, dissidents and opponents both inside and outside Myanmar: "What is the result of Hun Sen's decision to go to Myanmar and press the key to open the door to a lasting solution to the crisis in Myanmar?" "Myanmar is now a blessing or a curse."
