"If we look at the evidence presented by the authorities and their actions, it is not an exercise in freedom of expression or peaceful assembly, but a plot with malicious intent," said Jean Malin. "The unrest affects social security, public order, and there seems to be more organization and organization from abroad through funding, planning and strategy."
According to the spokesman, what the authorities found was a strong and clear legal basis to prove that it was a crime related to incitement, so only law enforcement in court proceedings is a legal means. Only in response in a democratic society and the rule of law.
Mr Malin said that if the protests were related to labor disputes, there would be no unjust plan behind them, so it could be easily resolved under labor law, so that international human rights activists and some civil society organizations could look deeper. This is a bit, do not be politically biased, they can see the actions and actions of the protest leaders.
