NEC Clarifies the Completion and Use of Ballot Counting Records (T1102) of the Polling Station Commission
(Phnom Penh): Recently, there have been concerns from election-related parties about the inability to guarantee a free, fair and just election in line with the principles of multi-party liberal democracy if the political party agents Participated in monitoring the election process and counting the ballots, could not get the record of the counting of ballots (T. 1102) at the polling station, and the packaging of security package "A" was made incorrectly.
Regarding this case, the spokesperson of the National Election Committee would like to clarify as follows:
According to Article 132 of the Law on Commune / Sangkat Council Election, the record of counting the ballots as stated in article 131 of this law shall be made in 3 copies:
* A copy posted publicly at the polling station until the day the official election results are announced.
* A copy will be posted publicly at the CEC until the day the official election results are announced.
Pursuant to the above-mentioned provisions and in order to strengthen the technical conditions for the implementation of Article 132 of the Law on Commune / Sangkat Council Election, the NEC has established three media outlets where political party agents can obtain records. Of Ballot Counting (T.1102) on Election Day:
Second: When sending the record of counting the ballots (No. 1102) to the NEC, this document will be signed, dated and stamped by the President of the NEC, then the record of the counting. This ballot (T.1102) will be scanned, entered into the election results management system and printed out for distribution to the agents of the political parties present.
Third, once all the documents have been scanned and entered into the election results management system, stakeholders, including citizens, can find the photos, forms, which are the basic documents for verifying and summarizing the results of the election. Elections in all communes across the country in the NEC website.
As for the packaging, delivery and receipt of the "A" security package, nothing has changed from the previous election. The NEC only strengthens the mechanism and adjusts the workflow to be smoother and more efficient.
