(Phnom Penh): Mr. Phay Siphan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit, told reporters of all tendencies to report directly to the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit. Ministries and institutions that do not respond or respond to journalists contrary to the policy of the Royal Government.
Mr. Phay Siphan's remarks were made this morning, January 6, 2022, during a meeting between him, the head of the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit, and various journalists to share experiences and exchange opinions, especially Past challenges in finding information in various ministries and state institutions.
The head of the Royal Government Spokesperson 's Unit noted that in the past, he has often heard criticism from national and international journalists for asking spokespersons of ministries and institutions about inactivity or not responding to you. News, but he did not receive any complaints from journalists. He said that the only way to report is through his own phone and the official Facebook page of the Government Spokesperson's Unit.
Mr. Phay Siphan stated, "I believe that some of the problems we face, some national or provincial ministry spokespersons have not yet responded to what the government wants and also your difficulties. The press. "And our journalists have not yet complained about which ministry spokespersons or provinces have not yet fulfilled their duties or a complaint."
He asserted that the spokesperson has two very important responsibilities: first, to spread the word about transparency, and second, the duty to respond, which is in response to accountability. He added that his unit is not a place to monitor the work of spokespersons in ministries, institutions or the work of journalists, but a place to create opportunities for journalists to access information for the benefit of the public.
He stressed that in order for journalists to be able to communicate well with the spokesperson, the journalists themselves must be understanding and qualified. He said that if we have quality and capable journalists, people will also get the efficiency and quality of access to that information, so all this is very much the attention of the spokesperson of the Royal Government.
Formerly a journalist, Phay Siphan claimed that journalists have a very important role to play in nation-building and peacekeeping. He recalled that during the time Cambodia had border disputes with Thailand, in some places, journalists even stood before the army and described the problems to the Cambodian people.
He also reminded all journalists to fulfill their role as professional journalists and avoid acting as activists of political parties, whether in the ruling party or the opposition.
At the same time, Mr. Phay Siphan also urged spokespersons in all government ministries and institutions to be spokespersons with a lead, avoiding a spokesperson without a lead. In this sense, he wants to emphasize that the spokesperson of the Ministry of Institutions must fully control what their institutions achieve what happens to their institutions.
