(Siem Reap): The family of Miss Sam Vicheka Raksmey has been making soy milk for sale since 2013. This business can help ease the family's livelihood and can feed nearly 20 nieces and nephews from rural areas.
The soy milk of Ms. Sam Vichheka Raksmey's family was recently shown at a rural food fair in Preah Dak village, Banteay Srei district. In an interview with Fresh News, Ms. Sam Vicheka Raksmey said that her family started making soy milk as a family with a mother who was a teacher and a father who was a civil servant.
The family's subsistence business came after Raksmey's parents welcomed her niece, a student from the countryside, to live with up to 20 people, and the family was not well off. That's why her family is looking for an extra job to support herself by deciding to sell soy milk.
The special feature of Miss Soy Sauce is that it contains a lot of soy flour, focusing on quality without adding a lot of water, and the beans are from Mondulkiri province, which is a local product. There are three types of flavors: soy flavor, herb flavor and butterfly flavor, all of which are self-grown and have health benefits.
