International Analysis: Can the promises of the five powers avoid a nuclear war?
PARIS (Reuters) - The five nuclear powers on Monday pledged to curb nuclear proliferation and avoid future conflicts or nuclear war in the face of current tensions between the two countries. West and East.
In a joint statement, the five nuclear powers and permanent members of the UN Security Council, including China, France, Russia, the United Kingdom and the United States, stated: "We strongly believe that The proliferation of nuclear weapons must be prevented in the future. "No one can win a nuclear war and never let such a war happen."
Many experts agree that nuclear weapons are only used as a means of reciprocity between the superpowers. But no one has said in advance whether they will not use this weapon after the United States became the first country to use nuclear weapons, while Japan was the first country to taste this deadly weapon. At the end of World War II.
