(Phnom Penh): Ouk Srey Mom set a new record for Cambodia at the World Petanque Championships by winning a gold medal to make Cambodia the reigning gold medalist in the World Patent Games for five consecutive seasons. Each. Ouk Srey Mom's victory and gold medal in the petanque competition brought pride and enhanced Cambodia's national prestige in the field of petanque.
Ouk Srey Mom recalled that when she was young, her family was not very prosperous and her mother cooked for the players at the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Sports Center, or as it is often called, the old stadium. Through her mother who cooked for the players, Ouk Srey Mom came and went in and out of the old stadium, where the players train almost every day.
One day, when Ouk Srey Mom was playing Krasang, a basketball coach saw a straight throw and said that the Bowling Federation was in need of players to train. Ouk Srey Mom was also called up to train in bowling in 1997, when she was only 16 years old.
After training for about a year, Ouk Srey Mom also had the opportunity to go to the SEA Games in Singapore and also won a gold medal.
With the talent and hard work of training with the help of bowling leaders, with Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An as the President of the Federation and Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng as the Honorary President as well as the coach, Ouk Srey Mom became A strong athlete.
Ouk Srey Mom said that so far she has won a total of more than 40 medals. More than 10 gold medals and two world-class gold medals. The first world gold medal was won in 2017 and the second in November 2021.
Ouk Srey Mom said that in order to become a good bowler, in addition to natural talent, it is necessary to train. If the training is not intense, it can not be strong.
The petanque world gold medalist also said that in order to be a good bowler, it takes a combination of physical fitness such as arms, legs, torso, waist and eyes. In addition, during each match, the mood must be as high as possible.
Ouk Srey Mom expressed her happiness and pride in herself, which can contribute to the pride of the nation and the people of Cambodia. This achievement is the result of our hard work, as well as the support of national leaders, bowling and petanque leaders, as well as coaches and colleagues.
Ouk Srey Mom expressed her determination that as long as she was strong, she would train hard to win medals for other competitions. Especially the 2023 SEA Games, which Cambodia is hosting. Pursat Deputies Hold a Joint Meeting to Summarize the Annual Work Results and Raise Further Directions
