Phnom Penh Capital Hall Spokesperson: Construction of flyover and subway at Chom Chao roundabout is still ongoing, so far 92%
(Phnom Penh): Although the situation of Kovid 19 has lasted in Cambodia for many years, the development of infrastructure in Cambodia is still ongoing. In fact, the construction of the flyover and subway at the Chom Chao roundabout is still ongoing without any interruption. This is according to Mr. Met Meas Pheakdey, the spokesman of Phnom Penh Capital Hall, told Fresh News on the afternoon of January 5, 2022.
Mr. Met Meas Pheakdey said that according to the plan, if there is no obstruction due to Kovid 19 disease, the construction process of the flyover and subway at Chom Chao roundabout will be completed by now, but due to the irregularities due to Kovid 19 Continued to be delayed until the construction is completed about 92%, of which is scheduled to be completed in March 2022.
It should be reminded that the flyover and subway of Chom Chao roundabout is a project of the Royal Government of Cambodia through the administration of Phnom Penh, under construction contract by the Overseas Cambodian Investment Company (OCIC), using construction in 30 months and construction cost of about 22 million USD.
Based on the technical specifications of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, this construction site is divided into 3 parts, including:
* Bridge 1: It is the main flyover connecting traffic from Russian Boulevard to National Road 3, with a total length of 408 meters and a width of 15.8 meters, with two lanes and two lanes to the bridge slope of 4.5 meters and a maximum height The traffic under the bridge is 5.5 meters.
* Second Bridge: Separate from the main flyover, turn left and connect the traffic from Russian Boulevard to Veng Sreng for one-way traffic with one lane for cars and one lane for motorcycles with a total length of 202 meters (40 meters of flyover, lower road) The land is 118 meters long and the road is 44 meters long and 5.25 meters wide.
The surface road is the main road connecting traffic from National Road 4 to Veng Sreng Road with a total length of 235 meters and a width of 8.5 meters for one-way traffic with two lanes for cars and one lane for motorcycles.
The subway is a 470-meter-long, 8.5-meter-wide lane from National Road 4 to the Russian Federation Boulevard for one-way traffic with two lanes for cars and one lane for motorcycles. Safety speed 40 km per hour for 8.5 meters wide road. 25 km / h for 5.25 m wide and 5.5 m wide.
It should be noted that the flyover and subway at the Chaom Chao roundabout officially opened the construction site on June 29, 2018 under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany. Hun Sen. Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan Requests Relevant Ministries to Review Imports of Some Medical Chemicals After Finding Local Drug Production Locations
