Samdech Mey Library Releases Statue of "Cambodian Heroines: Hope" to Commemorate January 7 Victory Day
(Phnom Penh): To commemorate the Victory Day on January 7, the Samdech Mey Library of the Documentation Center of Cambodia has released a statue of "Cambodian Heroines: Hope". The statue is the work of Indonesian artist Neo Menota, honoring all women who survived the Khmer Rouge regime, along with a story provided by Youk Chhang, director of the Documentation Center of Cambodia.
The story that accompanies the statue above is as follows:
In the dark ages, human life seems meaningless. The massacre took place for no apparent reason.
Only the powerful can see their future and desire more than they need. When the Khmer Rouge came to power, atrocities and bloodshed ensued.
The Khmer Rouge left many women isolated from their families. The world knows that there is genocide in Cambodia, but only a handful of people are aware of the struggles of these women for themselves and their children.
These women have gone through many hardships, but they are still strong and not easily overcome. Using their hands, these women rebuilt their families and their nation. This statue is dedicated to all women who survived the Khmer Rouge regime as Cambodian heroes.
