In addition to cracking down on tons of drugs in Kampong Speu province, on the night of December 30, 2021, the police also cracked down on large-scale drug crimes, arrested a suspect and a total of 181 kilograms of drugs and 370 grams.
Separately, this morning's meeting will proceed on six agendas, including:
First, the meeting was chaired by General Ke Kim Yan, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs.
Third: Report on the results of chemical inspection in the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Health.
Fourth, the report on the results of the inspection of chemical compounds in the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Industry, Handicrafts, Science, Technology and Innovation and the case of importing chemical compounds of Shenzhen Chenhui and Xin Yinfeng.
Fifth: Review and discussion on the draft amendment of Resolution No. 28. Pillar. Dated 12 May 2000 on the Establishment of the Inter-Ministerial Working Group on Chemical Compounds
And 6: Summary and guidance of Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, Chairman of the National Anti-Drug Authority.
Minister of Labor: The National Union of Cambodia is a partner in protecting the rights and interests of workers in line with the main goals of the Royal Government
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, stated that the National Union Council of Cambodia is a partner in contributing to the protection of workers' rights in accordance with the main goals of the Royal Government.
"The National Union Council of Cambodia is a partner in contributing to the protection of workers' rights in line with the main goals of the Royal Government," he said.
As the Minister in charge of Labor and the senior Ream who used to work in the union, Mr. Ith Sam Heng gave five recommendations, including:
* 1: Must consider the benefits, including good internal unity through transparent leadership, clear work management for the overall growth of the unit and serve the interests of the motherland.
* 2: To strengthen the dissemination to member workers to have a clear understanding of the labor law and the law on trade unions, as well as the proclamations and guidelines issued by the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training. At the same time, we need to expand our membership, but please do not grab each other's members, which is a sensitive point that leads to conflict and unity.
* 3: To train and guide local union leaders, to study clearly about the signing of collective agreements, what conditions are required in relation to the work of factories, enterprises, establishments, without deviating from the labor law, and to avoid leading and participating in work. Illegal demonstrations.
* 4: To strengthen and continue to expand cooperation with trade unions both in the region and outside the region to mobilize support in terms of materials, budget and capacity building training.
