Tycoon Hun Lak, who invests in mangoes and bananas, said that the growth of bananas and mangoes throughout 2021 is really good.
He said the better growth of bananas was due to the fact that bananas are a crop that harvests in rotation from the beginning to the end of the year and is exported every week, unlike mango exports. Good export growth will bring many benefits to exporters and growers.
He added that in the beginning of 2022, banana and mango will have better growth because both crops have entered the harvest season, another factor is that Cambodia can export fresh mangoes directly from the port of Sihanoukville to the target market. Especially the Chinese market.
"From the beginning of January 2022, there will be more orders with better prices as the mango harvest season arrives and demand is high," he said. "However, we are still concerned about the lack of containers, especially refrigerated containers, because mangoes need to use refrigerated containers to transport fresh fruit for export."
