(Phnom Penh): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen presides over here on Wednesday morning the award ceremony of Ouk Srey Mom after winning the world gold medal in the petanque competition in Santa City. Susana, Spain in November 2021.
Ouk Srey Mom adds another world record to the title of Ke Leng after winning the gold medal at the 2021 World Petanque Championships in Spain in the women's singles on Tuesday. November 14, 2021.
Ouk Srey Mom's World Gold Medal in November 2021 is the fifth consecutive world gold medal for a Cambodian athlete in a petanque competition in scoring. Ke Leng has won four seasons, including 2013 in France, 2015 in Thailand, 2017 in China and 2019 in Cambodia.
Ouk Sreymom's world gold medal tally is breaking the world record of Cambodia's five consecutive victories after Ke Leng, with no other country from Cambodia.
Please note that the patent competition in scoring in Spain runs from 12 to 14 November. Ouk Srey Mom finished first in the scoring qualifiers, ranking third among the 36 strongest women in the world.
Ouk Srey Mom then defeated Canada in the last eight by 29-2 and Norway by 25-18 before defeating Thailand 37-29 to win the gold medal. Only once. In the women's 3-3 event, the Cambodian patent team dropped to the last eight.
Please note that the heroine Ouk Srey Mom also won the world gold medal in 2017, but in the individual event. In petanque, Sok Chanmean also won a world-class gold medal in the individual event.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen paid high attention to the athletes who are the representatives of the nation. In order to encourage the athletes who have worked hard to train, Samdech Techo issued a sub-decree setting the prize money of about 40 million Riels for the athletes who won world-class medals in this patent competition.
Bowling and petanque have the potential to win medals and show national prestige on the international stage. Since the establishment of the federation until 2020, Cambodia has won a total of 370 international medals (108 gold, 131 gold and bronze). 131).
This great achievement comes from the great support of the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as well as the pioneering leadership of the previous generation, with Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An as President of the Federation and Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng as President. Honors as well as many other founders who have sacrificed their physical, mental, busy time and personal budget to push bowling and petanque to world fame and admiration.
