Analysis: The entry into force of the RCEP and the China-Cambodia Free Trade Agreement will strongly support Cambodia's economic recovery.
According to World Bank data, by 2020, Cambodia's economy will shrink by 3.1 percent, and by 2021, the growth rate will be only 2.2 percent. But over the past 20 years, Cambodia's average annual economic growth rate has risen to 7.7 percent, making it one of the fastest growing economies in the world.
The signing and implementation of a free trade agreement between China and Cambodia is a good example. Dr. Chheang Vannarith, Executive Director of the Asian Vision Institute, said that the free trade agreement will be conducive to production cooperation between the two countries and increase the construction of Cambodia's industrial chain to attract enterprises from other countries to invest. In Cambodia.
The Asian Development Bank (ADB) Representative in Cambodia stated that the Sino-Cambodian Free Trade Agreement will encourage Cambodia to achieve export diversification and provide more market opportunities for Cambodia to expand its agricultural production, processing and non-agricultural products. Textiles.
Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce of Cambodia, stated that the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia will actively cooperate with other Ministries to strive to expand the export of goods to trading partners within the framework of bilateral and multilateral free trade agreements. Separately, the Ministry of Commerce will officially launch a new data center to collect and analyze commercial big data.
