Royal Government Appoints Mr. Keo Remy as Cambodia's Representative to Icha in 2022
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to appoint Mr. Keo Remy, Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, as the Cambodian Representative to the ASEAN Intergovernmental Commission on Human Rights (ICHA) for the fifth mandate in 2022-2024 and in 2022. This Cambodia will be the president of Icha as well. This is according to the decision of the Office of the Council of Ministers, which was received by Fresh News on the evening of January 3, 2022.
According to the letter, the Royal Government agrees on the following principles:
First, assign the role of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee in charge of ACHA, the ASEAN Regional Human Rights Mechanism, to manage the coherence of the national, regional, and UN human rights processes.
Second: Appoint Mr. Keo Remy, Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, as the Cambodian Representative to AIC, because in 2022, Cambodia will be the Chairman of ACHA, which may have many politically sensitive issues to be discussed. In meetings.
