Five blood washing machines and medical equipment were provided to Kampong Cham Provincial Referral Hospital
(Kampong Cham): Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the National Commission for the Prevention of Kovid 19 Vaccination, handed over 5 washing machines and Sakkin disinfectant on the afternoon of January 3, 2022. And medical equipment were provided to Kampong Cham Provincial Referral Hospital.
Customer support is a driving force for the company to continue its efforts to bring the best new products and technologies to the Cambodian people to use to help strengthen and improve the health and well-being of the Cambodian people.
Today, the company is pleased to provide 5 washing machines, Sakkin disinfectant and some medical equipment to Kampong Cham Provincial Referral Hospital for use in the health sector. She added that all these materials will help contribute to the Royal Government of Cambodia in improving the well-being of the people of Cambodia.
Ms. O Vandin claimed that the company provided 10 washing machines, including 5 to Kampong Cham Provincial Referral Hospital and 5 to Battambang Provincial Referral Hospital, which will be handed over and received in the near future. Battambang Province.
At the same time, Ms. O Vandin noted that when obtaining machines that serve the modern health sector, human resources with the skills to use must also be necessary. She said that if there is a modern machine and we do not know how to use it is not possible, but according to the doctor in Kampong Cham is knowledgeable to use this machine.
In addition, Ms. O Vandin also highlighted the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia to vaccinate people against measles 19 from the basic dose to the third dose or boost dose, while some countries have not yet achieved such. Cambodia.
The chairman of the National Committee for the Kovid 19 Vaccine claims that after the Royal Government successfully completed the basic dose vaccination, the vaccination has now reached more than 34 percent.
However, she noted that only a small number of people have not been vaccinated due to misconceptions, especially pregnant women, lactating women and the sick. At this point, she stressed that, of course, pregnant and breastfeeding women are the priority to get vaccinated, the vaccine can go to provide more protection for children.
In particular, people with a chronic illness, such as high blood pressure or diabetes, should consult a specialist at a vaccination center in their village to be able to be vaccinated against Kovid 19.
However, Ms. O'Vandin cautioned that even if the vaccine was given in full, from the basic dose to the booster dose, the individual should not be neglected with Kovid 19, that is, the health rules, especially the three measures, must be properly applied. Protect and 3 do not. Have to say no to drugs! Nationwide drug crackdown for January 3: 11 cases cracked, 17 arrested
