(Phnom Penh): In 2021, in order to maintain the stability of the riel in the market, the National Bank of Cambodia has released a budget of about $ 500 million, which contributes to protecting the purchasing power of the people.
The release of the dollar has helped keep the market exchange rate stable at around 4,099 riel per dollar, a decrease of about 1% compared to 2019. This is according to the report on "Macroeconomic progress and the banking sector in 2021 and the outlook for 2022".
Exchange rate stability and appropriate cash flow management have contributed significantly to price stability, with inflation at a low rate of 2.9%. Inflation in 2021 contributes to the recovery in the prices of fuel-related goods and services, while food prices and core inflation slowed. This is according to the report of the National Bank.
Kaing Tong Ngy, spokesman for the Cambodian Microfinance Association (CMA), said that in order to help stabilize the riel, the association has encouraged microfinance institutions to encourage their clients to use the riel more, including higher interest rates. For savings as well.
He added that currently for the MFI, there are 20% of customers using riel.
Overall inflation for 2022 is projected by the National Bank of Cambodia to be 2.6 percent due to lower growth in the food sector, driven by improved supply and a slowdown in fuel and commodity-related prices. And the official exchange rate continues to be stable at around 4,075 riel per US dollar.
