Commentary: RCEP should be expected in the future
BEIJING, Jan. 1 (Xinhua) - The Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP) officially entered into force on January 1, 2022, marking the world's most populous free trade area. It has the largest economic and trade scale and the largest development potential in the world, officially established.
The RCEP covers 2.2 billion people worldwide and 30% of the world's gross domestic product. The first countries to allow the agreement to enter into force were six ASEAN countries, China, Japan, New Zealand and Australia. In addition, South Korea will allow the agreement to enter into force on February 1. "Expectations" have now become the common goal of businesses in the region.
As the world's second largest economy, China has always stood by the right side of history, firmly adhered to multilateralism, adhered to equality and justice, and has been increasingly becoming a partner of the country. Development path.
In addition, the draft law is aimed at China, which fully reflects the Cold War ideology and ideological bias. The so-called "response to the test from China" is just a necessary excuse for the United States to increase its military budget and expand its military force, which has embodied hypocrisy in seeking hegemony and stifling China's development.
The US military budget has risen sharply again, and people's livelihood projects have often been hampered. Such a United States is not only the grief of the American people, but also the greatest threat to world peace. Senior Minister Sun Chanthol unveils road project to be opened and inaugurated in 2022 (Video inside)
