Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Occasion of Opening Ceremony of Preah Sihanouk-Koh Kong Road
(Koh Kong): 2021 has closed its pages, but the construction and development of Cambodian society, which is the hunger of the people, there is no time to close, especially the road infrastructure system. Welcoming the New Page of 2022 On the morning of Monday, January 3, 2022, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen inaugurated the construction site and upgraded National Road No. 48 connecting Sihanoukville to Koh Kong.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a speech for about 1 hour and 40 minutes with the following main contents:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presides Over the Groundbreaking Ceremony for National Road No. 48 Connecting Preah Sihanouk Province to Koh Kong Province
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech was really pleased with the gathering to celebrate the construction of national achievements under the shadow of peace.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the construction of National Road No. 48 has to wait a little late because it has to find the budget. However, it is better not to build late.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the future, Koh Kong province will have more economic zones than other provinces, not losing to Sihanoukville.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in Cambodia's past, the connection between Sihanoukville and Koh Kong was a dangerous ferry trip.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that Samdech had a memory with the people of Koh Kong province on May 14, 2008, the day of the inauguration of National Road No. 48, the people ran to hug Samdech and shed tears because Remember the sadness when Koh Kong province had no roads in the past.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pride in the efforts of Samdech and his colleagues in building and developing Koh Kong province from the difficult situation. Samdech Techo stated that peace is an important factor leading to the construction and development of this province.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded in the past that some members of the Cambodian People's Party had advised Samdech to cut off trade between Koh Kong and Thailand. Samdech Techo confirmed that he strongly opposed this proposal. Samdech Techo considered this to be a democratic policy in the Cambodian People's Party.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it takes no less than 200 hours to describe in detail the life of Samdech in the construction and development of the nation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that National Road No. 48 is a seaside line that not only serves the local area but also serves the trade between Cambodia, Thailand and Vietnam, while now becoming an important tourist destination. .
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that do not expect progress without internal connections and neighboring countries through the construction of road and bridge infrastructure.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that sometimes he is tired of the procedure of seeking foreign loans to build road and bridge infrastructure.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that foreign aid from borrowing countries is around 20 percent, while 80 percent has returned to the lender. Samdech Techo confirmed that he had raised this issue in front of the United Nations.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the South Korean government and people for funding the construction of National Road 48, as well as other national roads.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the South Korean government for helping to build a bridge across the river connecting Phnom Penh to Arey Ksat.
* Samdech Techo stated that this bridge will improve the area of Arey Ksat and Lvea Em district, which is a satellite city of Phnom Penh.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that relations between Cambodia and South Korea have improved significantly. The relationship that Samdech Techo has established is benefiting Cambodia in terms of economy, trade and providing many jobs for Cambodians.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if Cambodia did not engage with South Korea, there would be difficulties during the ASEAN-South Korea meeting.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Global New Year event is a big test of Cambodia for the condition of Kovid 19.
