(Koh Kong): 2021 has closed its pages, but the construction and development of Cambodian society, which is the hunger of the people, there is no time to close, especially the road infrastructure system. Welcoming the new page of 2022, on Monday morning, January 3, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, continued to open the construction site and upgrade the quality of National Road No. 48 connecting Sihanoukville to Koh Kong.
The construction project to upgrade the quality of National Road No. 48 with a total length of 148 kilometers starts from the intersection with National Road No. 4 at km 141 + 750 in O'Chrov village, Boeung Preav commune, Sre Ambel district, until Khemarak Phoumin city, Koh Kong province. The project includes: 2 lanes with a length of 122.9 km, a width of 11 m and 4 lanes with a length of 25.1 km, a width from 18.5 m to 21.5 m.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also said that this road has 5 intersections that will be modified, including: Chamkar Luong intersection, Sre Ambel intersection, intersection to the entrance to Kirisakor, intersection to the dam. Hydropower, and junction to Koh Kong Airport.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, National Road No. 48 is an important infrastructure of the Second Economic Pole, which includes: Sihanoukville, Kep, Kampot and Koh Kong provinces, which are industrial, eco-tourism and coastal areas.
