Source: CFR (Friday, December 31, 2021) The Minister of Tourism and the Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province chaired a meeting and inspected the actual location for the organization of the ASEAN Tourism Forum 2022.
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, chaired a meeting to review the remaining work and inspect the actual location for the 40th ASEAN Tourism Forum 2022 (ATF 2022) in Preah Sihanouk Province. Sihanouk to prepare for the reception of international delegates, ministers and senior officials.
Meeting and inspection of the actual location for the ASEAN Tourism Forum was held on January 2, 2022 at Sokha Beach Hotel, Sihanoukville, Sihanoukville, with the participation of officials of the Ministry of Tourism, law enforcement and relevant working groups. And the working group of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration.
It should be informed that Cambodia will host the 40th ASEAN Tourism Forum which will be held from 16-22 January 2022 in Sihanoukville, Sihanoukville Province.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun received the recommendation of the Minister and the meeting and assigned Deputy Governor Mr. Mang Sineth to organize health and safety for the delegations from ASEAN member countries upon arrival and return.
The provincial governor will also review the promotion of the third dose of the vaccine to the staff who participated in the ATF event at the event and at the Sokha Beach Hotel.
Minister Thong Khon further stated that the ASEAN Tourism Minister will take this opportunity to announce the reopening of tourism in his region from Cambodia.
It should be noted that the 40th ASEAN Tourism Forum in January 2022 was attended by the Ministers of Tourism of nine countries: Cambodia, Thailand, Laos, Myanmar, Singapore, Malaysia, Indonesia, Brunei and the Philippines, while Vietnam was represented by the Deputy Minister of Tourism. Its Minister of Tourism. Kovid-19: France to ease stimulus measures from next Monday
