Understand the business: Well-known businessmen in the agricultural sector call on farmers to change their cultivation habits using chemicals to a safe system (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Well-known businessmen in the agricultural sector, Oknha Hun Lak called on farmers Change the practice of cultivating with chemicals, energy, and return to the practice of safety assistance.
The call comes on the occasion of Tycoon Hun Lak, CEO of Tropicam, inaugurating the Model Vegetable Safety Center and establishing a partnership to promote the chain of safe vegetables in accordance with Good Agricultural Practices (GAP) standards.
"Why modernize agriculture? My goal is for farmers to change their cultivation habits, use chemicals, energy, and return to a safety aid system," he said.
In addition, Duke Hun Lak said that the security system is compiled by professional farmers who can help farmers 'cultivation, because in the past, farmers' cultivation was planted on the field and done about three to four times. Per year only.
Oknha Hun Lak continued that at the same time, the yield of farmers is low and need to use chemicals to prevent pests, but the Center for Vegetable Safety Model and the establishment of a partnership to modernize agriculture technically.
In addition, the well-known agricultural trader stressed that future security systems will help improve the health of consumers while building consumer confidence while planting and harvesting throughout the season. Dry, rainy season up to 8 times a year.
According to Duke Hun Lak, in the early stages of setting up the center, the company used its own investment capital from the beginning of March 2021 until now.
Oknha Hun Lak added that for about a month now, the company has been working hard to turn this location into a reality, despite the difficulties posed by the weather and the outbreak of Kovid-19 at the February 20 event. By.
Highlight the 6-hectare Model Vegetable Safety Center with key infrastructure inside and around the center, including:
Excavation of ponds, filling of soil to prevent flooding during the rainy season, installation of waterways, electricity, installation of nets connected to the irrigation system, 10 meters by 49 meters, 20 houses to ensure cultivation in both dry and wet seasons Using less water and less fertilizer, and cultivating and harvesting between 8-9 times / year, vegetable nurseries and daily indoor vegetable growing operations.
Construction of washing, packaging and storage facilities for vegetables at appropriate temperatures, and the installation of automatic washing, treatment and packaging machines, along with various means of transportation. At the same time, the company also studied the cost of vegetable production in The net house will also guarantee a full year crop rotation. A fire engulfs a parliament building in Cape Town, South Africa.
