78-year-old grandmother raises two grandsons who were abandoned by their mother at an early age, now living in poverty and suffering from severe burns to one leg
(Kampong Chhnang): Mrs. Petum, 78 years old, lives in Kbal Thnal village, Phsar commune, Baribo district, Kampong Chhnang province.
Currently, she lives in poverty and lacks daily life. Not only that, more than 10 days ago, she also suffered from soup burns on her left leg, which brought more difficulties to her, making it impossible for her to travel to feed her grandchildren.
Nowadays, she asks her neighbors for land to build a small leaf hut to bring her grandchildren to live temporarily, but now this small leaf hut is very dilapidated and she has no money to repair it. She said that the two grandsons she had been trying to raise since she was a child were 14 years old and 10 years old.
She said that the day the soup was burnt that day, she mixed brown fruit with lard and had no meat. When the soup was cooked, she picked up the pot of soup, but the pot stuck to the legs of the pot and clasped her hands, spilling the soup on her left leg and thigh, causing serious burns and injuries. Due to her poverty, she did not go to the hospital, but the neighbors helped her buy medicine and apply it to her wounds at home.
She raised her hand to ask for the generosity of the people near and far and the Cambodian Red Cross to help save her and her two grandsons with compassion, because now she has a difficult life and no Decent housing. The land where she built a hut today is someone else's land.
