National Bank of Cambodia: Cambodia's economy will continue to grow at 5% in 2022
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia has forecast that the Cambodian economy will continue to grow at a rate of 5 percent in 2022.
The National Bank of Cambodia's "Macroeconomic and Banking Progress 2021 and 2022 Outlook" report states that Cambodia's economic recovery is supported by the export of garments and non-garments, especially imports. Launches electronic components and bicycles that will enhance Cambodia's export diversification.
The construction and real estate sectors are expected to grow slowly, supported by growing domestic revenue and investment inflows into Cambodia. The agricultural sector, which accounts for nearly a third of the total workforce, is expected to continue to grow better than in 2021.
With the reopening of the economy, domestic economic activity, including wholesale, retail, telecommunications and transportation, and domestic tourism is expected to increase steadily, while international tourism may gradually increase and require time and effort to The sector is growing like it was before the crisis.
The recovery of tourism will have a positive impact on the improvement of the hotel and restaurant sector and other support services. In particular, the return of overseas workers who have received training and experience has been contributing to improving productivity and domestic production, especially in agriculture and handicrafts.
The gradual improvement of the economy will support the government's revenue, accumulate fiscal support, and especially boost public investment, which will provide returns for long-term growth.
Overall inflation for 2022 is projected at 2.6%, driven by lower growth in the food sector, driven by improved supply and declining fuel and commodity-related prices, and the official exchange rate. Stable around 4,075 riels per US dollar.
