(Phnom Penh): 2021 is a difficult time and a bitter life experience for people on the planet, including the people of Cambodia, due to the severe outbreak of Kovid 19 virus. For Cambodia, 2021 is off to a good start after the end of the Community Crossing Event on 28 November 2020, but the replacement of the 20 February Community Event has put Cambodians in a difficult situation for living and doing business.
To prevent the spread of Kovid 19, the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen has introduced and implemented a number of hot measures, including blocking people from leaving their homes and restricting traffic. Measures to combat the 199 Kovid epidemic have left many businesses in a state of disrepair, and some Cambodians have lost their jobs and are struggling to make ends meet.
Business failures and job losses are a tragedy for 2021, but even more tragic is the fact that some people have lost their loved ones to the Kovid 19 virus.
Obstacles cannot end life on this planet. With the emergence of the obstacles and difficulties of the 19-year-old Kovid, the presence of the Cambodian people's perseverance has also risen, from the national leadership to the general population to overcome the 19-Kovid. Implement the health rules, implement the "3 do not and 3 prevent" rules, especially the campaign for the provision and acceptance of vaccines.
The passing of 365 days in 2021 marks the end of a difficult time for the nation and the people of Cambodia, and has left many bitter memories. 2021, while leaving bitter memories, however, also left a spirit of unity, great efforts for the Cambodian people in the fight against Kovid 19.
