The Ministry of Foreign Affairs announces the results of a press conference on providing information on Cambodia's priorities as ASEAN chair in 2022 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, held a press conference to Provide information on Cambodia's priorities as the chair of ASEAN in 2022 under the theme "ASEAN works together: solve all challenges" at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
The Deputy Prime Minister emphasized that the theme of "ASEAN Working Together: Solving All Challenges" reflects the efforts to promote the spirit of ASEAN as a single family with ten strong members "All together". To work together to achieve common goals, to contribute more constructively to the maintenance and promotion of peace, stability and sustainable development in the region and the world.
The Deputy Prime Minister also highlighted four clusters of challenges that have a strategic impact not only within ASEAN, including the urgent need to achieve rapid economic recovery from the effects of the Kovid epidemic. 19 Serious pressures arising from geopolitical competition, security challenges, both traditional and non-traditional, and challenges within and within ASEAN institutions.
Cambodia also intends to complete the process of accepting Timor-Leste as a member of the ASEAN family. The Deputy Prime Minister also announced plans for two major follow-up events, including the ASEAN Global Dialogue on Comprehensive Rehabilitation after the Kovid-19 Crisis and the 2nd ASEAN Women Leaders' Summit on Entrepreneurship.
