National University of Battambang Celebrates Two Years of Confucius Institute
He added that in 2022, the Confucius Institute at the National University of Battambang will cooperate with the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Battambang Province by opening Chinese language classes to target high schools such as Pich Chenda High School.
In the past, the Confucius Institute has set up two Chinese language teaching centers in Chinese private companies: Battambang, Cement and Hunan Eurocang (Cambodia) Pharmaceutical Investment Company, and has more than 100 Cambodian staff. .
Dr. Sam Rany emphasized that the Confucius Institute at the National University of Battambang has an important role to play in teaching Chinese to the public at all levels. Pedagogical training for Chinese language teachers and opening of Chinese language classes in educational institutions and private entities.
Establish an international Chinese language test center and provide international Chinese language teacher certification. Consulting on information, society, economy, culture and education in China. Joint doctoral research and development of doctoral and youth leadership scholarship programs.
In order to achieve the "One Road, One Belt" development strategy, the Confucius Institute supported the National University of Battambang in opening the "Chinese Language" Department, which was officially inaugurated on December 16, 2021. Ago.
Sok Khorn, Rector of the National University of Battambang, said that on the occasion of the New Year 2022, this is a new page for strengthening the friendship between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the People's Republic of China.
The Rector also thanked Prince Sar Kheng and the leadership of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports for supporting the establishment of the Confucius Institute. He also stated that in 2021-2022, the National University of Battambang will include basic Chinese in the undergraduate education program from the second year in collaboration with the Confucius Institute and the Chinese Department of the Global Institute of Foreign Languages. Battambang National High School.
He stressed that the Kingdom of Cambodia has become an important trading partner of the People's Republic of China and will be a destination for investment and business in all fields in Southeast Asia. And recently, the two governments have set new strategic goals to boost bilateral trade between China and Cambodia to 10 billion US dollars by 2023.
