NEW DELHI: India's Tiger Conservation Society has reported that 126 tigers will die in 2021, the highest number since data began a decade ago. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Thursday, December 30, 2021.
India is home to about 75% of tigers around the world. Over the past decade, the biggest cause of extinction has been "natural causes", but many tigers have also suffered from poaching and "human-animal conflicts".
