Please be informed that the Victory Monument was inaugurated on February 25, 2016 under the presidency of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense and Chairman of the Commission for Study and Construction of the Victory Monument. It was officially inaugurated on December 29, 2018 under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
Victory Monument was built on an area of 8 hectares located in front of the Moradok Techo Stadium in Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh. This historic building was built based on the content of the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. The construction of the Victory Monument covers an area of 117 meters by 117 meters and a height of 54 meters.
The vision of building a win-win monument starts from the great results of the implementation of the win-win policy, the understanding of the suffixes and effects, combined with the achievements of research and compilation of books related to the win-win policy, which provided important concepts. In the construction of a win-win monument to achieve an architectural structure that is a public property, an identity of culture, contribution and sharing of gratitude as well as a symbol of peace.
No. 3 is the top three corners. The upper part of the Victory Monument represents three types of guarantees: first, physical and life insurance, second, career and occupation guarantees, and third, property and movable property guarantees. And real estate.
The Victory Monument is divided into three areas: the first: modernization and post-war achievements, the second: the harmonization of Khmer history, and the third: the Victory Monument.
