This also makes it clear to the Cambodian people that Sam Rainsy and his opposition group have only spoken out but are not responsible for their actions as usual, and also made it clear that the opposition Use referendums, slander and defamation to serve their political ambitions. They continue to live and deceive their activists with falsehoods and deception.
Through the actions of the opposition, led by Sam Rainsy, a veteran defeated politician, Chak Smok analysts can draw the following conclusions:
First, Sam Rainsy and his opposition do politics without a clear position and speak freely and without responsibility. This group is really a white-eared politician who dares to use all kinds of dirty tricks to fulfill his desires, but without responsibility. Because they are politicians who behave like children, they do stupid things without knowing anything. That is why they always fail forever.
This visionary politician has been involved in politics from the time he is a party until he is a non-partisan politician and has been involved in politics from the time he left the country until he fled the country. Prisoner Sam Rainsy has now reached the crossroads and is nearing the end of his political and natural life, but has not yet considered taking turns. Certainly politicians who have no political maturity and no vision for the party and the nation.
Fourthly, when it comes to losing, Sam Rainsy, nicknamed the "old loser politician", seems to be capturing the nation with the star of destiny "losing forever and losing his career" even more. In fact, competing in the election with Samdech Techo Hun Sen was a political life until he was 72 years old, but Sam Rainsy always failed until there was no standing party and disappeared and fled Cambodia.
This immature and visionary politician like Sam Rainsy has always lost the race against Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the hero of the Cambodian People's Party and of Cambodia, and this old politician will continue to lose until the end of his life. It's more if it dares to compete with Hun Manet, the CPP's future prime ministerial candidate.
A small suggestion that Chao Chak Smok wants to give to Sam Rainsy, a politician who is mature in age but not politically mature, should be ashamed and should retire from politics to open the way and leave opportunities for young people The next generation to do politics once, as the Cambodian People's Party has been preparing, is to take turns planning to continue to maintain, protect and ensure peace, stability and development for the nation, motherland and the people of Cambodia.
By: Chao Chak Smok, Phnom Penh, December 29, 2021 The Minister of Information encourages all media to increase production to attract the audience.
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, encouraged all media to increase production to attract the audience.
The Minister said this while the Minister and his team visited government officials and inspected the broadcast equipment at the Information Department of Kampong Thom Province on the afternoon of December 29, 2021.
On that occasion, the Minister said, "All media must increase production to attract the audience by making them understand our feelings."
The Minister said that the head of the unit must think about broadcasting, focusing on education, entertainment and providing unique information to demand creativity, and broadcasting is a smart competition with a lot of consideration without losing quality. .
Khieu Kanharith said that do not be intimidated by the word "modern" but learn to change the way you work and your business.
At the same time, the Minister urged all department heads to increase the production and dissemination of information quickly through different programs, and to be interested and share encouragement to those who have worked hard.
The Minister commended all the officials for their hard work, professionalism and sense of responsibility, based on the principles of good cooperation and solidarity to make the unit grow.
At the same time, Ms. Nget Narin, Director of Kampong Thom Provincial Information Department, made a brief report on the situation, including the lack of human resources, production work, lack of technical equipment and means.
Regarding the challenges of the Information Department of Kampong Thom province related to the lack of technology and information production, he promised to send national officials to help train to find a better way out.
