General Vong Pisen sends a message to all officers, deputies and soldiers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces on the occasion of the 2022 Global New Year
(Phnom Penh): General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, on December 29, 2021, sent a message to all officers, deputies and soldiers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces on the occasion of the upcoming Global New Year 2022. Arrive in the next two days.
Through this message, General Vong Pisen said, "On behalf of the leadership, the Commander-in-Chief and on my own behalf, I would like to send my deepest greetings to the officers, deputies and soldiers. "All of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, which in the past year has worked hard to overcome all difficulties, make all kinds of sacrifices to maintain peace, social stability, protect the territorial integrity and sovereignty of our beloved motherland."
With this remembrance, he urged officers, deputies and soldiers in all subordinate units to actively implement the policy of the Royal Government, Ministry of National Defense, General Intelligence, aiming to build a strong and orderly Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. Adequate ability to fulfill duties and responsibilities in national defense.
On the occasion of the Global New Year 2022, I would like to pray for the three jewels and all the soldiers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to be healthy, strong, strong, wise, long-lived and successful in all tasks for the motherland. Beloved of us.
He sent his condolences and greetings to the officers, deputies and wounded and sick soldiers who are being treated in hospitals and at home. I wish you a speedy recovery. In a happy family. With this, I would like to send my condolences to the veterans, the disabled, the disabled and the retired people who are in the localities all over the country. May all be happy and prosperous.
I would like to send my best wishes and greetings to all officers, deputies and soldiers who are on international missions in the field of humanitarian and peacekeeping under the auspices of the United Nations. Abroad and wish you good health, strength, achieve international missions and success in your studies with honor.
