"American higher education institutions are renowned for their unparalleled quality and excellent English language skills to prepare for future careers," she said.
BEIJING: A Beijing government official on Wednesday warned that China would take "immediate action" if Taiwan dared to act towards independence, adding that the Taiwan issue could be "extremely tense". More in 2022. This was released by Reuters on Wednesday, December 29, 2021.
Ma Xiaoguang, a spokesman for the Chinese government's Taiwan Affairs Office, said China is willing to do its utmost to find a peaceful reunification with Taiwan, but will take immediate action if the line is reached. Any red related to the declaration of independence has been skipped by Taiwan.
Ma said provocations by pro-independence forces in Taiwan, along with external interference, could escalate further in the coming months, with the situation in the Taiwan Strait next year. Will be more complicated and serious.
Taiwan is considered by Beijing to be one of its provinces, and in the last two years China has stepped up military and diplomatic pressure on the island, sparking outrage. From Taiwan and concerns from the United States, Taiwan's biggest backbone.
