According to the Progress Report of the Public Financial Management Reform Program, Phase 3 Plus 2, for the third quarter of 2021, the overall performance of the Public Financial Reform has improved, despite the situation in the 19 crisis.
In fact, the total revenue collection in the first nine months was about 15.895 billion riels, equivalent to 75% compared to the law, the progress of this revenue collection is a recovery that is better and better compared to the implementation in the period. Same in 2020.
Implementing Expenditures The Royal Government has focused on the social sector, where expenditures in this sector account for 98% of the law as of November 2021, and expects the implementation of total annual state expenditures to be Will achieve an estimated level of 108.7% compared to the law.
This can clearly reflect the effectiveness of strengthening the budget credibility of the Public Financial Management Reform Program, which provides the Royal Government of Cambodia with sufficient cash in times of crisis to address emergencies as well as Continuing daily work smoothly.
At the same time, the development partners also congratulated the achievements and expressed the willingness to participate and ready to continue to support the public financial management reform program to achieve sustainable reform.
The development partners also provided additional key comments on strengthening public financial management, in particular requesting an understanding of the Royal Government of Cambodia's strategic plan for the country's economic recovery after the Kovid-19 crisis.
