Announcing the new Governor of Boribo District, Kampong Chhnang Province, Mr. Cheng Chandona, replacing Mr. Yim Sarin
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Cheng Chandona, Deputy Governor of Kampong Leng District, has been announced as the new District Governor in place of Mr. Yim Sarin, who has been transferred to work in the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration. The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Long Chhun Lay, Chairman of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Council and Mr. Am Sophea, Deputy Governor.
The ceremony was held at Boribo District Hall on the morning of December 29, 2021, with the participation of provincial leaders, district councils, including civil servants working in the joint district hall and village and commune authorities under Boribo district, a total of about 70 people. .
After the administrative representative of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hall read the sub-decree of the Head of the Royal Government, Mr. Cheng Chandona, who was appointed as the new Governor of Boribo District, made a commitment in front of the presidency and many participants. He promised to do his best to serve the people, especially to follow the instructions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
On December 22, 2021, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, issued a sub-decree appointing Mr. Cheng Chandona as the Governor of Boribo District, while Mr. Yim Sarin returned to work at the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration.
