Samdech Techo Hun Sen's instruction was made at the request of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, to cancel the debt of 9,190,000,000 Riels for the use of electricity in the unit of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, which is a 5-year debt. Year from 2016 to September 3, 2021.
The reason for this debt is that the consumption of electricity is increasing every year according to the progress of the country and the defense sector, but the annual consumption of credit, the Ministry of Economy and Finance remains the same. In fact, before there were only 140 units, now there are up to 240 units. This is according to the statement of Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh.
In addition, Samdech Picheay Sena also requested the additional budget for the annual electricity consumption of the Ministry of National Defense at the request of the unit in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Saving electricity is part of the fight against waste, and all units are able to save this electricity. National Assembly resumes session to discuss and approve three draft laws to promote trade
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, presided over the 6th session of the National Assembly of the 6th legislature this morning, December 29, 2021, with three agendas related to domestic and foreign trade.
The draft law that the National Assembly is currently discussing and approving is:
1: Draft Law on the Amendment of the Law on Commercial Enterprises 2: Draft Law on the Amendment of the Law on Commercial Rules and Commercial Registration 3: Draft Law on the Approval of the Free Trade Agreement between the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia And the Government of the Republic of Korea.
The Draft Law on the Amendment of the Law on Commercial Enterprises aims to contribute to the continuation of the Royal Government's reforms in the socio-economic recovery of Cambodia from the Kovid 19 crisis and to improve the ease of doing business in Cambodia due to the Law on Commercial Enterprises. Promulgated by the Royal Kram on June 19, 2005.
The draft law on the amendment of the law on trade rules and business registers aims to facilitate trade in the technological age. In the past, the Royal Government has established procedures for business registration, taxation and enterprise notification, by launching a joint registration system through online data exchange nurseries.
Through this draft law, it removes some unnecessary conditions for registration and helps to make the automation system run smoothly and transparently with high standards in line with the global business and improve the business environment in Cambodia. Facilitating trade and competition aims to contribute to the socio-economic recovery of Cambodia from the Kovid 19 crisis and to boost economic growth.
The draft law on the ratification of the Free Trade Agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of the Republic of Korea will become a bilateral legal standard for mutual trade. Through this law, Cambodian agricultural products will have a bigger market by exporting to the market in the Republic of Korea, which will play an important role in improving the livelihood of farmers.
The draft law will boost the flow of trade and investment between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Republic of Korea, which will further benefit the two countries' economic, development, people's well-being and business connectivity. And can create new jobs for people.
