US orders aircraft carriers to remain in Mediterranean presence in Russia
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The United States has ordered its aircraft carriers stationed in the Mediterranean to maintain operations in the area to ensure security for European allies amid concerns that Russia could strike Ukraine. This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday morning, December 29, 2021.
A US Defense Department official described the move as a reflection of the continued US military presence in Europe, which is essential to ensuring the security of US allies and partners. The United States is also in line with Washington's commitment to collective defense.
