Lao Ambassador's thanks to Cambodia for supporting Laos in all circumstances, especially assistance in the fight against Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Amphay Kindavong, Ambassador of the Lao People's Democratic Republic to Cambodia at the end of his term, thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia for its support to Laos in all circumstances, especially in The epidemic phase of Kovid 19, in which Cambodia provided a series of mass vaccines and medical supplies to Laos, despite Cambodia's needs and necessities in the fight against Kovid 19.
Such a statement of thanks to the outgoing Ambassador of Cambodia was made on the occasion that he was allowed to pay a courtesy call and bid farewell to the National Assembly President Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin. This morning, December 28, 2021.
The National Assembly President praised and appreciated the efforts of his diplomatic mission in Cambodia over the past three years, which have brought many achievements and actively contributed to the promotion of traditional friendship and solidarity. And cooperation in all fields between the Royal Government Party and the people of both Cambodia and Laos.
He stressed that despite the Ambassador's diplomatic tenure in Cambodia being interrupted by the global crisis of Kovid 19, bilateral cooperation between Cambodia and Laos has been consistent, quality and effective. .
On behalf of the National Assembly of Cambodia, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin said that he was pleased with the fruits of the two governments' cooperation in the fields of politics, diplomacy, economy, trade, investment, tourism, education and vocational training. Development and mutual benefit.
Mr. Amphay Khin Davong supported the remarks made by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin. He thanked the President of the National Assembly as well as the National Assembly of Cambodia for their good cooperation in contributing to the success of his diplomatic mission.
He said that despite the outbreak of Kovid 19 during his diplomatic mission, he had made every effort to promote and promote the follow-up visits between the two countries' leaders. The legislature and the executive branch in promoting traditional and fraternal cooperation between the country and the people to be stronger and stronger.
In addition, the Ambassador thanked the National Assembly of Cambodia through the Cambodia-Laos Parliamentary Friendship Group for providing scholarships to Lao National Assembly officials to study in Cambodia. Mr. Amphai Khin Davong emphasized that although he had to leave Cambodia to fulfill his new duties, he would still have good relations with Cambodia and would try to mobilize more Lao people to visit Cambodia.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin stated that in 2022, the National Assembly and the Royal Government of Cambodia will be the rotating chair of the ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly and the chair of ASEAN. He hopes that the National Assembly and the Government of Laos will continue to support the important role of the National Assembly and the Royal Government of Cambodia in bringing about the success and prosperity of both nations and the ASEAN region as a whole.
