(Siem Reap): Preah Moha Vimal Dhamma Pin Sem Sereysovano, Supreme Councilor, Supreme Advisor, Priests, Director, Member of the Buddhist Parliament of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Chief Inspector of Wat Reachbo, Siem Reap City An invaluable heritage of Khmer ancestors dating back hundreds of years, he sought to collect and preserve these artifacts from the 1980s to the present.
The artifacts he collected included stone, copper, bronze, copper, bronze, deities, Buddha statues, and pottery items kept at Wat Reachbo for storage and display in the museum building at Wat Reachbo. This museum is called the Museum of Maha Vimol Dhamma Pin Sem Reachbo, a museum of Buddhism for all mankind in the world to see the works of art left by Khmer ancestors.
He reiterated that he had this intention for a long time, and only in 2021, Ms. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts and Chairman of the Board of APSARA Authority, visited Wat Reach Bo and saw the artifacts. She also decided to support the construction of a museum to suit his wishes.
Preah Moha Vimal Dhamma Pin Sem Serey Sovanno, he insisted that at the same time, the APSARA Authority also participated in the construction of the museum for the preservation of these archeological sites. Apart from this, there are some other achievements that the APSARA Authority has helped to Wat Reach Bo, including: Renovation of a temple and a school that is very old.
The construction of the Pin Sem Reachbo Museum is planned to cost about 900,000 US dollars, which will begin construction in 2022. At present, Preah Moha Vimal Dhamma is collecting donations from philanthropists to build this museum.
Please be informed that at the beginning of December 2021, Ms. Phoeung Sakona presented the architectural plan and suffix totaling 20,000 USD from the participation of her and the civil servants under the supervision of Preah Moha Vimal Dhamma Pin Sem Sereysovano. The museum and for him to start collecting more charitable suffixes to build the above museum.
