The Ministry of Public Works announces to take strict measures to stop overweight trucks for one year without exception
(Phnom Penh): After observing that some car owners are still angry and overweight, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has announced that it will take strict action against overweight trucks by 20% by stopping them for one year. There are no exceptions.
In order to strengthen the measures to comply with the provisions of the law on the road and the relevant legal documents to be highly effective and efficient, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport has once again reminded the following truck owners:
1: The owner of the transport company, the owner of the heavy truck, the owner of the stone business site, the owner of the sand depot, the owner of the land excavation site or all the heavy transport operators must strictly comply with the notification No. 049. October 28, 2020 on the enforcement of additional strict measures for heavy transport vehicles driving on the road network.
2. The owner of the cement factory, the owner of the stone business, the owner of the sand depot, the owner of the excavation site or all the heavy transport operators must instruct the driver of his truck to carry the correct weight before transporting the goods from Each original destination.
3: In case of still allowing the driver or the traffic of overweight vehicles, especially the load of more than 20 (twenty) percent to traffic on the road network, the vehicle will be detained for 1 (one) Year in accordance with Article 60 of the Law on Roads, without further exemption.
4: Local authorities at all levels will cooperate with the Standing Coordinating Committee to take action to crack down on overweight vehicles that destroy the road infrastructure in each jurisdiction.
5. Participation in the compliance and compliance with the rules, regulations and legal documents of all heavy transport operators is an important part to ensure the protection of road infrastructure, bridges and road construction to be stable and stable. Adhere to the technical age and contribute to reducing the national budget for road maintenance at a time when the country is facing the crisis of Covitt-19 (Covid-19).
