South Korea urges North Korea to start new year by accepting dialogue and cooperation
SEOUL: South Korea's Unification Ministry on Monday called on North Korea to start the new year by opening the door to dialogue and cooperation, while Pyongyang will convene a major party meeting this week. Discuss domestic and foreign policy issues. This is according to the release by Yonhap on Monday, December 27, 2021.
South Korean Unification Ministry spokeswoman Lee Jong-joo said a meeting of the ruling North Korean Central Committee, expected this week, would normally take place between 1-4 days with the presence of North Korean leader Kim Jong Un.
According to Lee, South Korea is looking forward to the event, which could have a message on inter-Korean relations or nuclear talks, and South Korea hopes North Korea will enter the new year by opening its doors. Welcoming dialogue as well as cooperation with the international community.
The process of nuclear talks between North Korea and the United States has stalled since the fruitless meeting between the two leaders in Hanoi in 2019. So far, Pyongyang has not responded to the call for a resumption of talks, demanding that Washington stop what it considers to be two standards and hostile policies against its country.
TOKYO: Heavy snowfall has caused traffic congestion, flight cancellations and disruption to train services in central Japan as of Monday. This was released by the AFP news agency on Monday evening, December 27, 2021.
Traffic jams reportedly began when a truck skidded across the road near the city of Hikone, where 68 cm of snow fell in the distance. 24 hours until this morning.
In addition, nearly 200 passengers were stranded overnight on a local train, while about 130 domestic flights were also canceled on Sunday due to heavy snowfall. About 50 more flights were canceled on Monday. Xi Jinping Highlights Responsibility for Organizing Food Security at Rural Communist Party Meeting of the CPC Central Committee
* Jointly take responsibility for food security
* Strongly guarantee the main types of agricultural products
In recent years, China's food supply has been adequate, but large-scale imports of soybeans and vegetable oils are heavily dependent on foreign countries. By 2020, China will import more than 100 million tons of soybeans and 983,000 tons of vegetable oil.
Xi Jinping stressed that ensuring the supply of primary products is an important strategic issue, so it is important to focus on the production of food and the supply of key agricultural products, fully stabilize the size of food crops, greatly expand Soybean production and oil material.
* Must maintain 1.2 million hectares of farmland for sure
Farmland is the root of food production and the foundation of the sustainable development of the Chinese nation. The meeting organized a number of measures, such as the implementation of good protection of farmland, strengthening the responsibility for conservation of farmland, increasing control over the use of farmland and the establishment of 100 million mu of agricultural land (equivalent to 6 .67 million hectares) by high standards.
(Kampong Thom): From the consideration of the problems of the local people that always happen on a regular basis, Ms. Khuon Khun Dy, Senator and Chairman of the Local Working Group of Kampong Svay District, Kampong Thom Province, continued to advise the local working group to work hard to serve the people. By paying attention and in a timely manner so that the people can see more of the Royal Government's efforts.
Ms. Khuon Khundy held this morning, December 27, 2021, on the occasion of visiting members in Phat Sanday commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province and submitting plans to local officials to manage security, public order and disseminate information. Letters of the Royal Government to the people.
