Mr. Meas Sophea reminded the people of the past when our country went through a chronic war, especially in the border area of An Ses, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province. He said that under the win-win policy, founded by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the long-running war in the country was completely ended and brought peace and development to the country to this day.
Achievements at Wat Oddar Chey Kiri Chumdasen Chey, also known as Wat An Ses, inaugurated at this time include: the gate of Wat Srah Tuek, as well as the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of Buddha statues and Pali schools.
Mr. Meas Sophea said that Oddar Chey Kiri Chum Sen Chey pagoda, also known as An Ses pagoda, was originally established with the donation of nearly 4 hectares of land by Mr. Meas Thipanha and his colleagues, and the construction of the pagoda gate and pond, as well as philanthropists.
The Senior Minister also thanked the philanthropists everywhere who contributed to the construction of this pagoda, especially he also thanked the Choam Ksan District Assistance Team and Mr. Muong Khim who contributed $ 25,000 to build a Buddha statue in this pagoda. Well.
During the inauguration ceremony of the achievements at Wat An Ses, Mr. Meas Sophea donated to about 100 families in the area, more than 150 teachers and students, as well as 58 members of the Armed Forces. Get 1 box of noodles, 1 fish, 1 sarong, 1 scarf, 1 large bottle of hand wash gel and some money.
