About 1,000 Russian troops took part in the exercise, and some returned to their bases after closing the exercise near Ukraine, the source said.
The latest military exercise comes as the Russian Foreign Ministry has announced that it has received a request from NATO to hold a meeting on security concerns in Moscow. That could happen on January 12, 2022, and Russia is considering joining.
Russia, which has in the past been accused by the West of increasing its large-scale military presence on the border with Ukraine, last week released a draft of security talks outlining key points it wants to raise. Talks with NATO, and most importantly, Moscow wants NATO to abandon military action in Eastern Europe and Ukraine.
