Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group visited Kampong Thom province to chair the annual meeting and set out 9-point plan to continue to implement for 2022
(Kampong Thom): In the meeting to review the work results in 2021 and work directions for 2022 of the Royal Government Working Group visited Kampong Thom province this morning, December 27, 2021, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman The Royal Government Working Group in Kampong Thom Province has set 9 important work directions for the working group to continue to implement effectively in 2022.
The meeting was attended by Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province and Permanent Deputy Chairman, Mr. Sao Sopheap, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Deputy Chairman of the Working Group, as well as members of the working group and other relevant officials. Meeting hall of Kampong Thom province.
After the meeting discussed and exchanged views, Minister Thong Khon also set out the implementation direction of 9 points, such as:
* Second: Continue to implement the work to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid disease and the process of vaccination, full dose and encouragement to the people according to the instructions of the Royal Government and the Ministry of Health, especially to continue to implement 3 measures to prevent 3 of Samdech Techo. The Prime Minister is firm.
* Third: Continue to examine and resolve the challenges, concerns and requests of the remaining 165 cases, including attention to resolve disputes or disputes outside the judiciary.
* Fourth: Continue to organize public forums at the local level of municipalities, districts, communes, sangkats to review and resolve intellectual requests, concerns and suggestions of local people effectively and transparently.
* Fifth: Continue to strengthen security, public order and social security through the implementation of safe village-commune policy.
* Sixth: Continue to strive to promote the provision of public services with a sense of responsibility, transparency and accountability to the people.
* 7th: Continue to promote the issuance of new model Khmer identity cards to all citizens.
* 9th: Strive to eliminate inaction / shortcomings and do good deeds to increase the trust, confidence and warmth of the people on the Royal Government.
After the meeting, Minister Thong Khon also led a team to inspect the location along the Stung Sen River to prepare for the river festival in March 2022. Svay Rieng Provincial Governor Encourages Students Who Fail the Baccalaureate Exam to Do Their Best and Strictly Obey the Examination Rules and Regulations
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng Province, encouraged all students who have passed the high school diploma exam (Bakdup) to do their best to complete all subjects by strictly adhering to the rules and regulations. Internal regulations of the exam.
With this, the provincial governor also wished all students to achieve successful results and get good grades, and the provincial administration will continue and prepare rewards for students who get good grades.
Please note that in the academic year 2020-2021, Svay Rieng province has 3,811 candidates registered for the high school diploma exam, 1,924 females, divided into 7 districts and 154 rooms, of which 803 science students, 482 females Divided into 2 districts (33 rooms) including: Hun Sen Chek High School and Hun Sen Kantuy Wai Primary School.
In the Social Science class, there are 3,008 candidates, 1,442 females, divided into 5 districts (121 rooms), including: North Svay Rieng High School, South Svay Rieng High School, South Sihanoukville Primary School, 2 December Primary School. And provincial pedagogical and vocational training centers.
Prey Veng Provincial Governor instructed the judges and supervisors in each examination room to follow the instructions of the Ministry of Education to ensure the examination is transparent and quality.
This kind of instruction of Prey Veng Provincial Governor was made on the occasion that he led the working group of relevant departments, units and authorities to inspect and cut the subjects of the Higher Secondary Diploma Examination and Completion of the 2020-2021 academic year on the morning of December 27th. 2021 at Preah Ang Duong High School in Prey Veng City, Prey Veng Province.
The provincial governor also encouraged all the candidates to do their best and participate in good health care, get enough rest and wish them all good results and become pillars. To enhance the honor of the school, society and family as well.
