Prek Khsach Commune Residents Ask Samdech Krala Hom to Change Commune Clerk
(Koh Kong): Residents of Prek Khsach commune, Kirisakor district, Koh Kong province, gave a thumbprint to Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, requesting the transfer of Mr. Hoeun Bunheng from Prek Khsach commune clerk in Kirisakor district, Koh Kong province.
In this proposal to change the Prek Khsach commune clerk, the people reported to Samdech Krala Hom that since the country was peaceful, they have benefited from the continuous development of the nation, lived in peace, security, happiness and always supported Lead of the Royal Government.
They thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister, and Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng for holding the commune elections so that they would have the right to vote for the Prek Khsach commune council. But in recent years, the Prek Khsach commune clerks who have been sent by the state to work have left their jobs as officials, not serving the interests of the people, not taking the law seriously and committing corruption, causing them to lose confidence.
The villagers claimed that Mr. Hoeung Bunheng, a clerk, did not care about the well-being of the people. The main land or these lands are owned while the people actually own them.
Citizens further described that Mr. Hoeung Bunheng used his authority to sell oil illegally, and while the local area of Yeay Sen village, Prek Khsach commune has developed infrastructure in almost all areas is attracting national and international tourists to visit. He has committed illegal acts by flooding the canal, which is rich in biodiversity.
What upset the people was that the commune clerk did not listen to Samdech Techo's instructions on providing public services. When people ask for birth certificates, children or marriage certificates and other documents, people never meet Mr. Hoeung Bunheng to fill out the request at their place of work and instead use the working hours for customers to buy land. Almost every day.
According to the people's representatives, they hope that the Ministry of Interior will address their concerns and requests. They are confident that Samdech Krala Hom will take steps to replace Mr. Hoeung Bunheng and appoint a new clerk as an official, as he once said: "People."
Siem Reap Provincial Administration Receives Donation from the Cambodian Association for Land Development and Construction
(Siem Reap): On the morning of December 27, 2021, the Siem Reap Provincial Administration received a donation from the Cambodian Association for Land Development and Construction to contribute to the fight against Kovid 19.
Siem Reap Provincial Governor Tea Seiha thanked the delegation of the Cambodian Association for Land Development and Construction for bringing donations to the provincial administration to join the Royal Government in fighting, preventing and eradicating Kovid-19 transmission and addressing people's livelihoods. Vulnerable people in Siem Reap.
According to the provincial governor, the Siem Reap provincial administration, under the guidance of the people everywhere, strives to explain and educate the Ministry of Health on the methods and guidelines of the Ministry of Health, as well as other measures of the Royal Government. Government in the fight against Kovid-19 disease.
Currently, the Siem Reap provincial administration is focusing on implementing measures to prevent the spread of a new type of Kovid disease (Omegrong) through imports. Mr. Tea Seiha continued that the issue of the fight against Kovid-19 is a common problem of all of us, not the problem of any individual, including leaders, government officials, the armed forces, monks, the general public must participate. Prevent this deadly infectious disease.
Dr. Ley Sopheap, President of the Federation of Cambodian Investors and President of the Cambodian Federation of Land and Construction Development Associations, said that the donation is to be used during the difficult period of Kovid-19 infection in order to contribute to the Royal Government, especially the provincial administration. Siem Reap during the fight to prevent and cut off the transmission of the virus of Kovid-19.
(Siem Reap): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation on December 27, 2021 organized a training course on minimum policies and standards on "Protection of the Rights of Victims of Human Trafficking" in Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province.
On behalf of Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, I would like to express my excitement to participate in the opening ceremony of the training course on policies and minimum standards on the protection of human rights victims of human trafficking today.
On that occasion, the Secretary of State said that human trafficking has been occurring everywhere in the form of transnational crime and in organized countries, and that this crime has had a negative impact on individuals, families and communities in particular. Both nationally, regionally and globally.
Mr. Nhek Vannara said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has been working to develop, compile, disseminate and implement policies, strategies, plans, bilateral and multilateral agreements and mechanisms aimed at combating and minimizing human trafficking and trafficking. Doing business with people in the national, sub-regional, regional and global.
The "Minimum Policy and Standards on the Protection of the Rights of Victims of Human Trafficking" training course was organized in two sessions in Kang Meas and Koh Sotin districts, Kampong Cham province, with the aim of providing new knowledge and experience to providers. The local service, the authority, has the authority to help the victims in time in their villages.
