(Phnom Penh): As of November 20, 2021, 7,127 companies registered with the Ministry of Commerce, an increase of nearly 100 companies, or 0.3% compared to the same period in 2020 . This is according to the report of the Ministry of Commerce.
Pen Sovicheat, spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, told Fresh News on December 27 that more than 7,000 companies had registered online after the Ministry of Commerce. Called and opened online registration.
"Our registration system is now a system that allows all companies that come to register with the Ministry of Commerce to follow online and all the necessary data that he uploaded to us stored online. And when he registers online, he automatically submits to the General Department of Taxation and can link to the Ministry of Labor. So the statistics of more than 7,000 are new companies that come to register online.
According to the report of the Ministry of Commerce, the number of companies and enterprises that applied for registration for companies and enterprises was 11,583, a decrease of 8.41%.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce claimed that the removal from the business list could be due to the companies' bankruptcy or other issues that led the companies to request the ministry to remove them from the business list.
