Ministry of National Defense to Celebrate Victory Monument to Celebrate 23rd Anniversary of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Victory Day
(Phnom Penh): As of December 29, 2021, it has been 23 years since Cambodia has achieved complete peace and complete national unity in history after being divided since the post-Angkorian Empire. The end of the war, the torn apart and the divided nation came through the victorious policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in 1998.
Ending the war by winning politics is a philosophy of peace and strong political commitment of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. The end of the war is not a miracle or a coincidence, so in the process of ending the war requires a combination of highly talented and scientific leadership, as events change dramatically.
Therefore, to celebrate this day, the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia will celebrate the Victory Monument from the 30th until midnight on December 31, 2021 to celebrate the 23rd anniversary (December 29, 1998-29). December 2021) of Victory Day, the day that ended Cambodia's civil war and the third anniversary of the Victory Monument.
The celebration will be presided over by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, and Chairman of the Working Group on the Construction of the Victory Monument. Phnom Penh.
General Nem Sovath also reminded the meaning of the construction of the Victory Monument that this monument is a three-cornered monument representing the three key policies that lead to a successful political victory, including:
The meaning of building a win-win monument is to inscribe and preserve all the symbols, relics and related achievements as a memory and a lesson for future generations. The second plaque shows the groundbreaking of the Victory Monument, the name of the benefactor who built and maintained it, as well as the appeals of all the benefactors who have good intentions for the historic building.
