Mr. Steng Sokhom congratulated and announced the results of the 43rd Central Committee Meeting of the 5th Mandate of the Cambodian People's Party on the occasion of the opening meeting of December 2021 and the direction for implementation in January 2022. Kamchay Mear District Party Committee in the morning of December 26, 2021.
Mr. Steng Sokhom stated that this decision strengthened the CPP leadership structure with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as President, Samdech Maha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin as Honorary President, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Vice President, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Vice President, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Vice President and Mrs. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Vice President.
The meeting also discussed a number of issues on the implementation of the joint plan towards the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022. The meeting had an in-depth understanding of the content of the 2021 situation and the main tasks of the party in 2022.
The Chairman of the Working Group said that at the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the President of the party, also informed the meeting about the results of the management of Kovid 19 better compared to other countries in the region and the world, which so far Cambodia Controlled the spread of Kovid 19 and reopened the country and full socio-economic activities from November 1, 2021 with vigilance and high responsibility.
"Cambodia's success in finding and vaccinating people almost 100 percent faster than planned has led the World Health Organization, development partners and many countries to be amazed and appreciative. "The leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the fight against Kovid 19 has put Cambodia out of the risk and epidemic of Kovid 19 and is reopening the country in all areas." Mr. Steng Sokhom further confirmed.
The conference also presents the draft policy of the commune party for commune development from 2022 to 2027. This policy also plays a part in attracting the people who are the supporters and members who attend the conference, if the policy is in line with what the local people want, will be supported. But if it is not in line with what the people want, this policy will not be fully supported.
Regarding the selection of candidates for the Commune Council for the upcoming election, the Chairman of the Working Group called on the working group and the commune party to stand on the principle of having the ability, knowledge, experience and youth to continue their turn through the election. This must be done with the utmost caution, we need human resources, but also to maintain internal unity within the party.
