(Phnom Penh): General Nem Sovath, Special Adviser to Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh and Director General of the General Department of Politics and Foreign Affairs, said that the celebration of the 23rd anniversary of the Victory Day ended the Cambodian Civil War in the context Kovid 19 is another turning point in history under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who is the sole guide in all processes of the Cambodian nation.
This statement was made by General Nem Sovath during an interview with the media this morning, December 27, 2021, on the occasion of the General's inspection of the exhibition booths of the units. Troops at the Victory Monument to celebrate the 23rd anniversary of December 29, 1998 - December 29, 2021, the end of the civil war in Cambodia under the victorious policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The general underlined, "Well, now we see more clearly the realism of the win-win politics that Samdech has led in his life from the beginning, and especially since June 20, 1972, he has become Direct leaders in all national journeys so far, our country has been as peaceful as it is today.
Well, this year's Victory Day celebrations also have a special meaning, we have just achieved a brilliant achievement, possibly on a global scale, with the 19-year war against Kovid. Opened a society that can be said that because Samdech Techo is still the guide of all national processes, which put strategic measures and all other measures until we can open society, open economy, open activities.
In addition, General Nem Sovath emphasized that for the organization of the Victory Political Day in 2021, it is a new sign of new achievements and achievements in the history of Cambodia, in fact, the fight against 19 diseases in Cambodia today. Under the sketch of Samdech Techo Hun Sen is unprecedented in history, so the gathering and celebration of the Victory Day is a new event of the motherland of Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): 120 military trainees of the Special Military Zone successfully completed a 19-day Disaster Search and Rescue Technical Skills Training on the morning of December 27, 2021.
The Closing Ceremony was presided over by Mr. Hang Samoeun, Advisor to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, on behalf of General Kun Kim, Senior Minister, First Vice Chairman, National Committee for Disaster Management. Participation from local authorities at the Phnom Penh Special Military Zone Headquarters.
Mr. Hang Samoeun, on behalf of General Kun Kim, highly appreciated and appreciated the dedication of the Special Zone Commander in organizing this training program to be an excellent reserve for disaster response, especially by Flood.
He said that the disaster relief equipment, which is a precious gift from Samdech Techo Prime Minister to equip the search and rescue operations of the regional army, especially the training program on search and rescue and disaster relief was also organized to 706. Special Zone Military, with the participation of trainers of the National Committee for Disaster Management.
At the same time, Mr. Hang Samoeun confirmed that in 2021, the magnitude of the impact and damage caused by floods is small compared to 2020. But even if the disaster is small, attention needs to be paid to the emergency response in a timely manner, because if the response is slow, it can turn a small disaster into a major disaster.
Mr. Hang Samoeun asked the search and rescue operation to remember that the search and rescue work is the most dangerous task, which requires a highly disciplined force, strong health care, constant development of skills, exercises and regular training. Perform search and rescue operations, believe in your own ability to help each other, ensure the ability to operate automatically, quickly and promptly.
In addition, he hopes that through the past training will provide yield and efficiency, can correct the shortcomings of our past search and rescue capabilities for a quick response to save the lives of the victims, and please close. Closing Ceremony of Technical Training for Disaster Search and Rescue Squadron 706 of the Special Zone Army "From now on.
On behalf of the National Committee for Disaster Management, I would like to express my full support for the outcome of the 43rd General Assembly of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party, which continued to support Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister and was unanimously decided. Nominate Dr. Hun Manet as the future Prime Minister.
