Russia, which has in the past been accused by the West of increasing its large-scale military presence on the border with Ukraine, last week released a draft of security talks outlining key points it wants to raise. Talk to NATO, and most importantly, Moscow wants NATO to abandon military action in Eastern Europe and Ukraine.
"We have received a request from NATO ... We are considering this," TASS quoted a statement from the Russian Foreign Ministry as saying. The United States and Ukraine have accused Russia of plotting to attack Ukraine, while Russia has denied any wrongdoing.
Although Russian President Vladimir Putin on Thursday last week said his country wanted to avoid conflict, it also wanted an immediate response from the United States and its allies to Russia's demands. Russia has also said it expects talks with US officials during January 2022 in Geneva, Switzerland.
