In the academic year 2020-2021, a total of 114,183 candidates registered for the exam, 60,397 females. There are 25 candidates per room, except for the last room and the room with the candidates from the special education high school. Separately, there are 204 writing centers with 4,616 rooms.
The bankruptcy exam lasts for two days, December 27-28, 2021, divided into social sciences and science.
For Social Science: The subjects to be tested on December 27, 2021, which are the first day in the morning, are two subjects: Earth and Ecology, 60 minutes, and History, 90 minutes. In the afternoon, there are also two subjects: 90 minutes geography and 60 minutes foreign language.
December 28, 2021 is the second day in the morning, there are two subjects: 90 minutes of mathematics and 90 minutes of ethics, 90 minutes. In the afternoon, there is one subject, Khmer literature, lasting 150 minutes.
For Science Class: Subjects to be examined on December 27, 2021, the first day in the morning, there are two subjects: History 60 minutes and Biology 90 minutes. In the afternoon, there are two subjects: 90 minutes of chemistry and 60 minutes of foreign language.
December 28, 2021 is the second day, in the morning there are two subjects: 90 minutes of Khmer literature and 90 minutes of physics and 150 minutes of mathematics in the afternoon.
The duration of the exam is 2 days equal to 630 minutes, with a maximum exam score of 500 points, but since the foreign language subject is an optional subject, the passing score is 500 minus 25 and then divided by 2 equals 237.5 points to 237 points.
