Australian Government vows to continue working with Cambodia in response to Kovid 19 pandemic
(Phnom Penh): The Australian Government is committed to continuing to work with Cambodia to respond to the Kovid 19 outbreak. This is according to the announcement of the Australian Embassy in Cambodia on the provision of vaccine assistance by the Australian Government of 2.35 million doses to Cambodia on December 26, 2021.
A statement from the Australian Embassy stated: "Australia will continue to work with Cambodia to respond to this global epidemic. "We remain committed to working together to ensure the security and prosperity of our people, our country and the region as a whole."
A statement from the Australian Embassy added: "This is part of Australia's commitment to share 60 million doses of Kovid-19 vaccine with the Indo-Pacific region by the end of 2022, with more than 10 deliveries. Millions of doses have come until now.
At the beginning of the epidemic, Australia worked with partners to support the Cambodian Ministry of Health in purchasing diagnostic, treatment and transport equipment for Kovid-19 patients, including 110 resuscitation aids and monitors. 370 diseases and 80 ambulances.
