(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Justice has prepared a plan and direction related to the establishment of out-of-court dispute resolution mechanisms at the local level for 2022. This is according to Mr. Chin Malin, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Justice, confirmed to Fresh News on December 26, 2021.
According to Jean Malin, the non-judicial dispute resolution mechanisms at the local level for 2022 include:
* First, the Ministry of Justice will jointly disseminate with the European Union in Cambodia a concept paper on the settlement of extrajudicial disputes through local mediation in Khmer and English, which is a scientific study document showing the format. Mechanisms and methods of dispute resolution through mediation in Cambodia.
* Second, the Ministry of Justice will jointly disseminate with the Ministry of Women's Affairs a document on guidelines on gender-responsive family dispute mediation for officers practicing this dispute at the grassroots level.
* Third: The Ministry of Justice will also disseminate documents on guidelines, guidelines, codes of conduct, ethics and teaching methods related to dispute mediation to law enforcement officers at the local level.
* Fourth, the Ministry of Justice, in collaboration with relevant ministries, institutions and development partners, continues the mission of training to strengthen the capacity and skills of dispute mediation for officials who directly practice at the local level.
* Fifth, as a follow-up to the dissemination of the concept document on the establishment of a non-judicial dispute resolution mechanism in Cambodia through this local level mediation, the Ministry will develop a national policy on this mechanism and then Prepare to be a law on the resolution of disputes outside the judiciary in Cambodia as a whole.
