Based on this strategy, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has sought vaccines in all fields, both bilateral and multilateral mechanisms, with friendly countries and health organizations such as the World Health Organization. So far, Cambodia has received a total of more than 41 million doses of the vaccine. Cambodia has spent up to $ 200 million on the vaccine, with the help of friendly countries and through the Kovak Center.
With the rapid availability of vaccines, Cambodia has also accelerated the vaccination of its people. To date, Cambodia has vaccinated more than 14 million people. Of those, more than 13.6 million were injected in two doses, and more than 3.3 million were injected in the third or boosting dose.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Bat considers the closing of the February 20 community event as one of Cambodia's great achievements in the fight against Kovid 19. Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the Kovid 19 vaccine. For Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Kovid 19 vaccine has made a significant contribution to the fight against Kovid 19 and the lives of Cambodians.
Samdech Techo thanked friendly countries such as China, Japan, Britain, the United States, the Netherlands for providing vaccine assistance to Cambodia to help prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
