Tycoon Leng Pros Receives the Medal "As Stallion" for Contributing to National Achievement
(Phnom Penh): Oknha Leng Pros, CEO of "Navattra Giant" Company, was awarded the "Chea Touk Kar" by the King of Cambodia, a high-level award, in response to his efforts to build a national society.
Mr. HUN Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, presented this medal to Duke Leng Pros on December 25, 2021, yesterday at the Closing Ceremony of the 26th Special Bodyguard Training Course. 27th generation and inauguration of achievements in the bodyguard command training center.
The tycoon was very happy to receive this medal. He thanked the King of Cambodia for awarding the medal and thanked the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, for awarding the medal to the King.
Tycoon Leng Pros, as well as the younger tycoons, the tycoon of the "Leng" clan, was nicknamed by the general public as "Oknha Chet Dharm" or "Oknha Chet Thumar". In the family of farmers, the "Leng" family, who were born in Prey Veng province, did not have much opportunity to study and drifted to South Korea to work as laborers in that country, looking for money to support themselves and their families.
With the opportunity to build a better life, the "Leng" family has always carried out humanitarian activities to help the needy and the needy and always join the Royal Government in solving the nation's difficulties. The humanitarian gestures of the "Leng" family are highly appreciated and admired by the general public in Cambodia.
Oknha Leng Pros considered that contributing to the building and development of the country with the Royal Government is the most important work to make the nation grow and prosper.
