Spokesperson of the Ministry of Education: Candidates for the Baccalaureate exam with 19 Kovids are not allowed to take the exam, while candidates who do not take the exam will automatically fail (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Spokesman of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Mr. Ros Sovacha on On December 26, 2021, it was stated that candidates for the 2021 Baccalaureate examination (Baccalaureate) were found to be infected with the 19 virus and were not allowed to take the exam.
Mr. Ros Sovacha confirmed to Fresh News, "In the case of a positive candidate, Kovid 19 must be treated in accordance with medical rules and will not be allowed to take the exam to avoid contracting the disease in the examination center." At the same time, according to the technical mechanism last year, candidates who were absent from one subject or more due to individual reasons were automatically disqualified.
