Spokesperson of the Ministry of Education proposes 9 points to candidates preparing for the bankruptcy exam on December 27-28, 2021
1: Go to your respective examination centers tomorrow, December 26, 2021 from 9 am to check the name, room number, table number, heat meter and get a health sticker to confirm that there is normal heat
2: Prepare alcohol, wash your hands and take it to the examination center
3: Do not use wet hands (due to alcohol washing hands, etc.) to touch the exam worksheet, which may cause marks on the worksheet during the writing process.
4: Continue to implement individual plans to prepare for the bankruptcy exam in order to get results that are worth the effort
5: Determined to calm down in the way you like, such as through meditation.
6: Eat enough, get enough sleep, drink enough water.
7: Continue to participate in the implementation of the principles of law, justice, transparency and acceptable results
8: Participate in the implementation of health safety measures, especially the implementation of 3 protections in maintaining the safety of individuals and families
9: Increase caution when traveling on the road by continuing to respect traffic laws.
Underlined that in the academic year 2020-2021, a total of 114,183 candidates registered for the exam, 60,397 females. There are 25 candidates per room, except for the last room and the room with the candidates from the special education high school.
