Mr. Kong Vibol stated, "We have seen that in the past 10 years, tax revenue has been stable, with good growth, which the General Department of Taxation has collected more than planned every year from 2012 until now."
Mr. Kong Vibol said that in 2020 and 2021, in the context of Kovid-19 disease, it is expected that the tax revenue will decrease significantly, but on the contrary, the tax revenue in 2020 There was a 1.36 percent increase over the plan.
He pointed out that 2020 is the year of Kovid-19 invading the world as well as Cambodia, but the internal revenue of the General Department of Taxation remains stable and collects more revenue than planned.
National budget revenue collected by the General Department of Taxation for the past 10 years, from 2012 to 2021, has been stable and good growth:
* In 2012, the General Department of Taxation collected a total revenue of approximately $ 759 million, 3.12% more than planned
* In 2013, the General Department of Taxation collected a total revenue of about 901 million USD, 4.08% more than planned
* In 2016, the General Department of Taxation collected a total revenue of approximately $ 1.502 million, 5.70% more than planned
* In 2018, the General Department of Taxation collected a total revenue of approximately $ 2.197 million, exceeding the plan by 14.27%
* In 2019, the General Department of Taxation collected a total revenue of approximately $ 2.819 million, exceeding the plan by 23.20%
