(Phnom Penh): The Union of National Unions of Cambodia (CCTU) on the morning of December 25, 2021 organized its congress to elect new leaders for the seventh mandate, which was chaired by Mr. Prak Chanthoeun, Secretary of the Ministry of Labor. And Vocational Training Representative of Dr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, and as a result, Ms. Tep Kim Vanna was elected Chairman for this seventh mandate.
Mr. Prak Chanthoeun urged unions to respect the law. Because external work can be done, internal work can be done, but the aspect of law is not respected, it is not possible, we must all work hard to implement the law.
According to the report, there are 16 trade unions under the auspices of the National Confederation of Trade Unions of Cambodia, and CCTU has members from all sectors: garments, footwear and ports, beer, construction, salt fields, fisheries, covering 15 provinces and cities. There were 84,289 members, but the number declined during the 19 epidemic of Kovid because some went to work and could not return, and others died.
According to the report, due to the outbreak of Kovid 19, for almost two years, the confession did not work at all due to the division into red zone, yellow zone and yellow zone. Everyone stays at home until May 6, when some areas will be open for work.
Mr. Tun Sophorn, National Coordinator of the International ILO (ILO) in Cambodia, congratulated the Union of National Unions of Cambodia for electing the Presidential candidate for the seventh term. He said that most members of the National Union of Trade Unions of Cambodia are women in many factories, so we want more women leaders to address women's issues in the workplace as well as the union movement.
At the same time, he congratulated the achievements of CCTU in the past mandate. He said the CCTU has worked hard, especially over the past two years, to recover from the 19-crisis Kovid crisis, which has had a serious impact on Cambodia's economy as well as the global economy, especially the employment and employment of factory workers. Enterprise. At the same time, the representative of ILO also promised to help the training of the Union of National Unions of Cambodia.
Speaking at the ceremony, Mr. Prak Chanthoeun instructed the leaders in the National Union of Cambodia (CCTU) to be united and lively to progress and what to think is youth and femininity to Be a future leader.
The Secretary of State also instructed to strengthen local unions related to the roles and responsibilities of local unions, which must be trained to know all because it is an important issue of the union.
With this in mind, the Secretary of State sees a loophole for union work: discrimination. We need to monitor the actions of employers, whether their actions discriminate against the union or not.
"All we need to think about during this period is not to strike, but to negotiate and to study the facts of the law, whether it is discrimination or not and what is right," said a senior Labor official. Protest and mediate according to the procedure.
Meanwhile, Mr. Prak Chanthoeun added, "During the pre-election campaign, but dare to do something, the opposition will come in and seize the members, making us lose credit. "The formation of demonstrations and strikes, although mediated by law, is an opportunity for the opposition."
