Two killed in Houthi rebel attack in southern Saudi Arabia
Riyadh: A Saudi and a Yemeni were killed in a rocket attack by Houthi rebels on the southern city of Jazan on Friday. This is according to Saudi state media quoted by CGTN on Saturday, December 25, 2021.
Saudi state media made the report based on a statement from the Riyadh-led Arab League. The statement added that in addition to the dead, a rocket attack by a Yemeni-based Houthi rebel group also wounded seven people, including six Saudi nationals and one civilian. Twelve cars and two markets were damaged in Bangladesh.
