International Analysis: Rising Christmas Tree Demonstrates 2021 US Economic Chaos
Rising Christmas tree prices are a phenomenon that could indicate that the cost of living in the United States continues to rise. In November, US inflation hit a new 39-year high of 6.8 percent. Inflation has "taken" the salaries of all Americans and is still not enough. Many people fall into sluggishness as wages continue to rise but goods are becoming less affordable.
In the context of the spread of Kovid 19 disease, the gap between rich and poor in the United States has widened rapidly.
On the surface, the reasons why Americans find it difficult to celebrate Christmas are related to factors such as rising commodity prices and the spread of Kovid 19, but in reality it is due to the incompetence of American politicians. The fight against Kovid 19 and the implementation of irresponsible monetary policy are the inevitable results of putting political interests above the interests of the people.
In the United States, in the context of Kovid 19, the social order in which capital is the priority and the wealthy have the highest rights is becoming more prevalent, so Americans are more anxious and depressed. These self-serving Washington politicians should be responsible for this year's Christmas, which is difficult for ordinary Americans.
