(Central): Once again, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Health O Vandin and Chair of the National Commission for the 19th Kovid Vaccination explained the latest developments in scientists' findings on new mutations. Of the 19 types of Kovidic disease, the most contagious is omega-1.
In an interview with reporters during the visit of the 19-dose Kovid vaccination in Kandal province on December 24, 2021, Ms. O Vandin explained that the reason is that the omega virus is transmitted from one person to another. Because of this type, when it enters the human body, it stays in the throat and nose and does not fall into the lungs like other species.
The Cambodian health official also claimed that this location factor would cause the omni-city type to pass quickly from one person to another if individuals did not implement proper health measures such as wearing masks and keeping a safe distance.
According to Ms. O Vandin, it has been a month since the discovery of the first omega species in Africa and has spread to more than 100 countries, including Cambodia. Which is the case of import. For Cambodia, she claims that the situation is not serious for those infected.
However, Ms. O Vandin, as the chairperson of the committee for vaccination against Kovid 19 and closely monitors the new development of Kovid 19 omega, claims that in all of our transformation Can be prevented through the implementation of health rules, especially the rules "3 protection and 3 do not" combined with proper vaccination and so on.
