(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism and the four provincial administrations of Cambodia's coastal areas are committed to continuing to promote the implementation of tourism safety rules and minimum operating standards (SOP) procedures along the new normal path for tourism businesses to ensure the reception of tourists. Safe.
Mr. Ny Phally confirmed to Fresh News that after the report of the Department of Tourism of Sihanoukville, Koh Kong, Kampot and Kep provinces on the progress of the implementation of tourism safety rules and minimum operating standards (SOP) in the normal course. New for tourism business, the meeting discussed and exchanged ideas and experiences of each province under the coordination of the Under Secretary of State.
"At the same time, the four provincial administrations of Cambodia's coastal areas are committed to implementing tourism safety rules and minimum operating standards (SOP) procedures along the new normal trajectory for tourism businesses to ensure acceptance. "Tourists are safe and confident in attracting international tourists."
Meanwhile, the Undersecretary of State recommended four points:
1: To request the four coastal provincial administrations to continue to encourage small, medium and large businesses, as well as all tourist resorts to continue to implement tourism safety rules and SOP standards as well as health rules on a regular basis to participate in disease prevention and control. Kovid 19 efficient and safe tourist reception.
3. Consider the possibility of establishing a coordination mechanism or a regular consultation mechanism between the private sector and the public sector to support the development of tourism in the province.
4: Provide opportunities for students to complete research and volunteer work in the tourism sector through cooperation with universities and educational institutions.
