Check out the pictures! Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presides Over the Opening Ceremony of the "Samdech Techo Prime Minister's Award" Golf Tournament and Activities at Vattanac Golf Resort
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presides over the opening ceremony of the "5th Samdech Techo Prime Minister's Award" golf tournament on Saturday, December 25, 2021. Golf Vattanac Golf Resort.
Today's golf tournament is jointly organized by the Ministry of Tourism, the General Commission of the National Police, the Golf Federation of Cambodia and the Vattanac Golf Resort Golf Course. The competition was held to celebrate the 23rd anniversary of the Victory-Monument (29 December 1998-29 December 2021) of the end of the Cambodian Civil War and the successful implementation of Samdech's win-win politics. Techo Hun Sen, Founder Ek.
Take a look at the pictures and activities of the golf tournament: Mr. Kor Vandy and Mr. Seang Sok announced their support for the unanimous decision of the 43rd Central Committee Meeting to elect HE Hun Manet as the future Prime Minister.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kor Vandy and Mr. Seang Sok would like to send a message of full support for the unanimous decision of the 43rd Central Committee Meeting of the 5th Mandate of the Cambodian People's Party on December 24, 2021. Appointed HE Hun Manet as the future Prime Minister.
This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced the opening of the golf tournament "Samdech Techo Award 5th"
According to the information, the competition will be attended by national and international players, divided into two teams: the team competition with 80 participants and the individual competition with 27 participants with 8 participants. People are the national team.
The competition lasted all morning and in the afternoon, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will present awards to the athletes who participated in the competition and had a joint meal to strengthen the unity.
Please note that the golf tournament "Samdech Techo Prime Minister Award 4" was held in 2019. At that time, a total of 179 national and international players participated in the competition, including 33 international players and 23 female players.
