Cassava has a better market this year than last year, but yields fall due to heavy rains
(Banteay Meanchey): Eighty-five percent of the farmers living along the border are cassava growers and 15% are traders, especially farmers living in Matbai district, Banteay Meanchey province, who have complained about the decline in harvests due to this year. Heavy rains and flooding caused the tubers to rot, and prices were higher than last year.
According to traders who buy from farmers, this year's cassava yield is not different from last year, which is a decrease due to heavy rains and floods, causing the tubers to rot, but the price is higher. The market is better than last year, leaving farmers and laborers to remove potatoes without having to cross the border at risk of migration.
Farmers in Banteay Meanchey province also requested the head of government, relevant ministries and institutions to pay attention to help Cambodian farmers to have a market for this crop to reduce illegal migration.
