(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Kanthara, Undersecretary of State and Chairman of the Working Group on Education, Outreach and Prevention of Drug Use and Trafficking of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, on December 24, 2021, presided over a seminar to disseminate knowledge from Drugs and tobacco products to students at the Fine Arts High School.
The seminar was also attended by Major General Lim Tong Huot, Director of the Department of Legal Education and Rehabilitation of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, and representatives of the Center. National Health Promotion, Ministry of Health.
Mr. Huot Sithon, Deputy Principal of Fine Arts Secondary School, welcomed and stated the purpose of the workshop was to raise awareness and participation of students in the fight against drugs and tobacco products for community health and safety. .
Lt. Gen. Lim Tong Huot, on behalf of General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, thanked the leadership of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and informed that in the first nine months of 2021, Cambodia can control drug users and addicts. There were 13,736 students, of which 3.66 percent were students and 18- to 35-year-olds were still the most vulnerable.
