According to the Karen National Union (KNU), an indigenous armed force in Karen State, the Myanmar military has launched at least two airstrikes and fired artillery into an area under Its control near the border between Myanmar and Thailand on Thursday this week. But so far the Myanmar military has not commented.
Fighting between the Myanmar military and KNU forces erupted last week, and more than 4,200 people have fled into Thai territory since the conflict in Myanmar, according to the Thai Ministry of Foreign Affairs. But Myanmar civil society groups say more than 10,000 Myanmar people have fled the conflict.
