Japanese government provides nearly $ 370,000 grant for four projects in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan, through its Embassy in Cambodia, has provided a total of US $ 368,478 to four recipient units under the Humanitarian Security Assistance Program or Kusanoun Grants.
The signing ceremony was held on December 24, 2021 by Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia and representatives of the four recipients.
According to Mikami Masahiro, since 1991, in addition to large-scale loans and grants, the Japanese government has been implementing the Kusano program in Cambodia to directly assist local authorities and NGOs in implementing its projects. They. Kusano means "grass root" in Japanese.
In the last 30 years, the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia has contributed to more than 650 projects through the Kusano Foundation Grant. Another 587 vehicles were inspected and fined on December 24, 2021
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmets, no license plates, overtaking and sign offenses. In particular, the car violated the speed, violated the sign, no driver's license, no license plate, no phone belt.
