(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap Provincial Administration has instructed the Siem Reap Provincial Health Department to promote the name, location and services of clinics accredited by the Ministry of Health in the treatment of Kovid 19 so that tourists can know and receive clear information easily. In seeking treatment for Kovid 19.
The introduction was made during a meeting to review and address challenges at Siem Reap International Airport after the opening of the first international tourist on December 17, 2021, chaired by Mr. Pov Piseth, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap this morning. December 24, 2021.
The meeting was attended by the Department of Health, the Department of Tourism, the Siem Reap International Airport Authority, clinic owners and relevant units to implement a safe and confident reception of tourists related services, Rapid test and PCR test for incoming tourists. Siem Reap and back.
On that occasion, the Deputy Governor instructed the Siem Reap Provincial Health Department to "publish a proclamation of clinics accredited by the Ministry of Health to receive treatment for Kovid-19 to the public so that guests know and receive clear information easily. Finding a location for medical services.
Deputy Governor Pov Piseth instructed the Siem Reap Provincial Health Department to prepare a comprehensive dissemination document on the implementation of the SOP standard operating procedures set by the Ministry of Health.
At the same time, Mr. Pov Piseth also advised all clinic owners who have received permission from the Ministry of Health to stop charging more than the limit, making guests feel inferior and affect the national tourism sector.
He added that the Siem Reap Provincial Health Department must also prepare a public notice of the location for the PCR test and test pricing. General Khim Bunsong, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP)
