The forum aims to share the results, challenges, concerns and requests of non-communicable patients in the context of Kovid-19 and what policies and programs are in place to support those patients.
The forum was attended by the Deputy Director of the Department of Health Protection of the Ministry of Health, Dr. Muy Seang Horn, and the Director of the Non-Communicable Diseases Bureau of the Ministry of Health, development partners, and representatives of civil society organizations implementing non-communicable diseases in Cambodia. .
The results of this forum get the following three main points:
1: Promote and promote the salary of village health volunteers and the role of village, commune and sangkat officials 2: Establish a network of non-communicable patients to help educate the community 3: Facilitate the affordable price of drugs to Patients from 4 relevant ministries: Promote non-communicable diseases education and establish a community gymnasium.
Under the above recommendations, the Department of Health Protection will discuss with the management to support patients in leading to the prevention of non-communicable diseases and the health of the people in Cambodia.
