Ministry of Social Affairs Organizes National Forum on Employment and Occupation Environmentally to Promote Job and Employment Opportunities for People with Disabilities
(Phnom Penh): The National Forum on Employment and Occupational Environment for Persons with Disabilities will act as a joint mechanism for relevant institutions, including ministries, government institutions, organizations representing persons with disabilities, national and international NGOs, and the private sector to share experiences. And lessons learned, as well as building more relationships and collaborations at the national and international levels.
He said the forum will work to promote and seek support from various stakeholders, with a focus on promoting and expanding environmentally friendly employment opportunities for people with disabilities.
Speaking at the forum, Mr. Hach Hean also made some important recommendations, including:
1: Continue to promote the implementation of the Law on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities and other legal documents to turn the documents on paper into practical activities to help people with disabilities.
2: Continue to expand the National Forum "On Employment and Occupational Environment for People with Disabilities" to the sub-national level.
3. Continue to encourage ministries, public institutions and the private sector to accept people with disabilities to work at the rates set out in the sub-decree on the selection of people with disabilities to work, which is 2% for public institutions and 1% for the private sector.
