In response, Mr. Amphai Kindavong expressed his special thanks to Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon for receiving his hearing at this busy time and for the good cooperation and closeness of the leadership and officials of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. Foreign and international cooperation, which is an important basis for contributing to the success of his diplomatic mission in Cambodia.
On this occasion, the Ambassador expressed his deep gratitude to the Prime Minister for providing invaluable assistance to Laos, including the Kovid-19 vaccine budget and a series of medical equipment, especially on the occasion of his official visit. Lao Prime Minister Phorn Khamviphavan recently.
The two sides also raised sub-regional, regional and international issues of common concern. Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon thanked Laos for its support to Cambodia in the recent successful holding of the 13th Asia-Europe Summit and for Cambodia's role as chair of ASEAN in 2022.
Commentary: The tactic of using "Xinjiang cards" to prevent China will definitely fail
China's actions not only strongly defended sovereignty and national security as well as development interests, but also strongly defended the principle of non-interference in internal affairs and sovereignty equality. A clear attitude in opposition to hegemony and power politics.
With regard to the issue of Xinjiang, China adheres to the same attitude, that is, does not allow external forces to interfere, the so-called "prevention of China by using the Xinjiang issue as an excuse" will certainly fail. Missed. The United States needs to lift so-called sanctions on Chinese officials and stop interfering in China's Xinjiang affairs and internal affairs.
If the United States insists on doing so arbitrarily, China will act more accordingly as the situation develops. This equal retaliation shows that no matter how hard China speaks, no one can underestimate China's determination and strong will to uphold its legitimate rights and interests. .
