With the support of KOICA and Korea Productivity Center (KPC), the new business exchange program between Cambodian and Korean universities was successful.
(Phnom Penh): With the support of the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) in Cambodia and the Korea Productivity Center (KPC), the new business exchange program between Cambodian and Korean universities has been a resounding success.
Dae Hwan Bae, Project Manager of the Korea Productivity Center, said that with good relations between the two countries, the program is part of strengthening ties and cooperation for students to connect with each other.
Cambodian student Srey Neang expressed her pleasure and admiration for the Korea International Cooperation Agency in Cambodia and the Korea Productivity Center for setting up the program. Srey Neang said that the program not only helps them research technology, but also provides good communication with Korean students.
Please be informed that the research in planning for the new business exchange program between the University of Cambodia and the University of Korea was conducted online due to the Kovid 19 crisis, which made it difficult for students to discuss. Each. According to the project manager of the Korea Productivity Center, next year's and next programs will be held offline.
