SEOUL: South Korean Justice Ministry announced earlier that President Moon Jae-in has decided to grant a formal pardon to former President Park Geun-hye, who is serving a prison sentence for corruption. This was released by Yonhap News Agency on Friday morning, December 24, 2021.
In early January 2021, South Korea's Supreme Court overturned Park's sentence of 20 years in prison for corruption and gave her the first chance to end the legal process, which was seen as She may be pardoned.
Ahead of the announcement by the South Korean Ministry of Justice, a South Korean government official told Yonhap news agency on condition of anonymity, "I learned that former President Park Geun-hye's name was on the list. "That will be pardoned."
