Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) achieves new achievements in connecting 230 kV high voltage transmission network around Phnom Penh
He said that the launch of this transmission line is another historic achievement that was achieved in 2021 after more than three years of difficult construction of the east line from the 6th substation (Udong). Come to Substation 7 (Takhmao City) with a length of 88.5 km across 4 rivers.
With this new transmission line, Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) has also launched the 75-megawatt Khsach Kandal substation, located in San Long Village, Vihear Sour Commune, Khsach Kandal District, Kandal Province, which has increased the capacity of the electricity supply to be more stable and better quality. The source approached the people in the area.
The substation will supply consumers in Khsach Kandal district and some parts of the surrounding area, including Lvea Em district, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province, Srey Santhor district, Kang Meas district, Batheay district, Kampong Cham province, Sithor Kandal district and Pearang district, Prey Veng province.
The achievements of the new transmission line and substation not only provide additional supply capacity, it is also part of a network project around Phnom Penh that connects Udong, Ponhea Leu and Muk Kampoul districts and continues to connect Khsach Kandal, Lvea Em, Kien Svay and Takhmao City, Saang District, Kandal Stung District, Kong Pisey District, Ang Snoul District and Kambol District, together with a 400 MW oil / gas power plant invested by the Royal Government.
From now on, the electricity supply in Phnom Penh and Kandal will be more stable and sustainable due to mutual sources that help each other, even if there is a problem, we will be able to supply again.
Mr. Keo Rattanak stated, "This new transmission line and substation is a fruitful achievement from the good cooperation between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the People's Republic of China in the development of the electricity sector, contributing to the economic growth of Cambodia under the guide." "Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techea Hun Sen."
