Ministry of Labor: NagaWorld Labor Dispute Resolution for December 23, the two sides still do not agree
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has continued to issue a press release on the results of the Labor Dispute Resolution Meeting at NagaWorld Limited for December 23, 2021, with both parties still not agreeing to end the case. Dispute still.
According to the press release, on December 23, 2021, the Ministry will continue to coordinate and resolve labor disputes at NagaWorld Limited, with Ms. Chhim Sithor and Mr. Horm Sunrith representing the workers and Mr. Mike Ngai. As a representative of the company.
After the meeting, the two sides still did not agree to end the dispute because:
1: Company representatives will consider the formula for calculating the termination of employment contract for 85 workers who have agreed to accept the payment of termination contract in accordance with the law under the coordination of the Ministry, but the company refuses to accept workers Other are protesting to get back to work.
2: Workers' representatives demand a package settlement by requiring the company to accept the workers who are protesting to work first, then the other 85 workers agreed to accept the payment of severance pay in accordance with the law.
However, the Ministry of Labor also encourages union workers as well as employers to continue to cooperate with the Ministry and the competent authorities to end this dispute in a spirit of mutual understanding.
