(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has issued a notification to 944 workers from 8 factories in the garment, tourism and film industries (as attached in the appendix) who have been granted suspension of employment contracts. In line with the spirit of the third round of the Royal Government's package of measures.
The following is the announcement of the Ministry of Labor: Director General of CSX: At the end of this year, one company received a listing license while two companies are preparing
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hong So Hour, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the General Director of the Cambodia Securities Exchange (CSX), said that by the end of 2021, a number of companies have already received permission from the Cambodian regulator to list securities. The other two companies are already preparing and may be ready by early 2022.
JS Land Plc. Is a residential developer through the use of state-of-the-art technology for construction, approving the principle of public offering of securities.
JS Land Plc will be the second company to list on the Cambodia Securities Exchange.
Mr. Hong Sochua confirmed that as of today, there is a delay of companies that will come to register the sale of securities because some companies are busy closing the list of documents not yet ready, plus the preparation of applications. The listing of this securities is not ready yet. Others are awaiting approval and approval from relevant authorities, such as the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and the National Bank of Cambodia.
"For companies that are late in listing this year, they will rush to list in 2022," he said. "So in 2022, there will be more companies listed, both companies that have been working with the stock exchange now and many new companies."
He added that although the performance was lower than expected of the listed company, the stock market received high trading volume.
Please be informed that in 2020, the Cambodia Securities Exchange has received 5 companies to list and sell securities.
Court orders protection of 20 vehicles from Hak Chheangly and Kuy Rita
(Phnom Penh): The Bailiff of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on December 22, 2021 yesterday implemented the protection order No. 486 "M" DR dated 29 November 2021 to confiscate 20 vehicles. Co-debtors Hak Chheangly and his wife Kuoy Rita bought the car in installments between 2018 and 2019, but refused to pay the car for several years.
In addition to falsifying documents to get creditors to agree to sell the car in installments to the couple, they also forced their employees and apprentices to pretend to be the original car owners or garage owners with conspiracy. Former creditors' employees cheat creditors to agree to pay off several vehicles.
In addition, a number of vehicles were hid by the two co-debtors in various places to hide and evade the authorities in charge of enforcing the protection order as well as the creditors. .
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of December 24, 2021, tomorrow, the Cambodian People's Party, the ruling party for the first six terms, will open its 43rd Central Committee Meeting for the fifth term to decide on the party's candidacy for Prime Minister. This for the future, including some other agendas.
The 43rd Central Committee Meeting will be chaired by Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, and Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Honorary President of the Cambodian People's Party, with the participation of permanent members. The Central Committee, including representatives of local leaders in the capital and provinces, is working to help young Cambodians become start-ups who can solve problems using technology.
Mr. Srun Sovila, Director of the National Center for New Business Training of Cambodia, added that the purpose of the New Digital Business Training Program 2021 is to enable students and young entrepreneurs in Cambodia to study and develop new ideas to solve problems in Cambodia using Technology and to create new business models to be sustainable for its solutions.
Mr. Kien Tak, Deputy Rector, Mr. Chet Chealy, Representative of the Royal University of Phnom Penh, said that the Royal Government of Cambodia in recent years has been working to promote the establishment of ecosystems for new businesses. At the same time, the Royal University of Phnom Penh has been establishing a new National Business Training Center of Cambodia on the campus of the Royal University of Phnom Penh with the assistance of the Republic of Korea, represented by KOICA in Cambodia.
Mr. Kien Tak added, "Under the leadership of Rector Chet Chealy, we will have a new center, the Center for University and Enterprise Cooperation, which will be built on the three campuses of the Royal University of Phnom Penh."
Please be informed that the National New Business Training Center of Cambodia is also a project supported by the Government of Korea (KOICA representative) for the establishment of a new business training system between universities and industries in Cambodia with a total budget of nearly 8 million US dollars. Construction began on September 3, 2021, with completion scheduled for 2023.
