Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized this in his speech at the inauguration ceremony of the Administration Building, the Customs School Building and the Customs Museum Building of the General Department of Customs and Excise this morning, December 23, 2021.
In this ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded of the initiative of foreigners to sell the customs institution during 2004. For Samdech Techo Hun Sen, selling a customs office is tantamount to selling national sovereignty, leading to his outspoken opposition to the idea.
Samdech Techo said that if Samdech followed the instructions of foreigners, the customs revenue would fall to foreign hands up to 50 percent.
Samdech Techo considered that not selling customs institutions to foreigners or the private sector under the guidance of foreigners during that period was one of the most correct decisions for the national interest. According to Samdech Techo, this right decision was based on the concept of independence and national sovereignty.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen reiterated the concept of leadership in defending independence and national sovereignty: "Whatever we do, we must control and adhere to the concept of independence and national sovereignty, and we must not bow our heads in exchange for aid." "Or any tolerance from abroad."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen is a Cambodian leader who always defends the sovereignty and independence of the Cambodian nation very strongly and always opposes any foreign request to exchange on any issue that affects the sovereignty of the nation.
In fact, while the EU announced a tariff on about 20 percent of Cambodian goods imported into the EU, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also vehemently declared the protection of national democracy and agreed to comply with EU requirements. Cambodian goods.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister said that agreeing to do something at the request of foreigners not only loses national sovereignty, but it will also become a bad habit, that is, when foreigners do not like something, they always Warn them to do this or that to be oppressive and force them to do what they want.
