Commentary: Any attempt to obstruct the democratic development process of Hong Kong will fail!
BEIJING, Dec. 20 (Xinhua) - Following the release of the so-called Five Eyes "Joint Statement", the G7 also issued a so-called Joint Foreign Ministerial Declaration on December 20. Defamation of the just-concluded 7th legislature election of China's Hong Kong Special Administrative Region recently, alleging that Hong Kong's democratic factors are being "destroyed".
The US Department of State and the Treasury Department have also been inspired by the US State Department's submission of the so-called "latest Hong Kong Autonomous Law" report to the US Congress. The United States has re-imposed the so-called sanctions on five Chinese officials.
The so-called G7 foreign ministers' statements and the so-called US State Department reports have all been rumored to be new, nothing new. The G7 has attacked Hong Kong's new electoral regime for "restricting the choice of ballots", using "democracy" as an excuse to denigrate it.
In fact, the "crackdown on democracy" was a British act that had colonized Hong Kong for more than 150 years. According to a white paper entitled "Democratic Development of Hong Kong under the" One Country, Two Governments "regime, released by the Information Office of the State Council of China on December 20, Hong Kong Under British colonization, there was no democracy.
Hong Kong's distinctive democracy is now booming, and new policies and good governance are opening up. In the face of the ever-forward historical trend, all attempts to obstruct the development of Hong Kong's democracy are in vain and fail!
