1: Continue to promote the dissemination of information to all parties involved in the provisions of laws and regulations to increase the understanding and participation of all parties in the implementation of fiscal obligations and the implementation of laws and regulations in force to strengthen The rule of law builds a better fiscal culture.
2: Continue to effectively implement revenue collection strategies and public financial management reform programs through leadership development, capacity building in implementation, reform, strengthening ownership, reform, strengthening Ownership and care Empowerment of human resources with greater use of information and communication technology.
3. To continue and constantly improve the implementation of trade facilitation support mechanisms, such as automation, risk management system after customs clearance.
4. Participate in the effective and effective implementation of measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease and address the effects by consistently implementing the new normal life-saving strategy in the Kovid-19 environment to Economic recovery.
5: To continue to effectively strengthen the prevention of smuggling to contribute to increase revenue, competition for the promotion of fiscal compliance in Cambodia, on the other hand, to completely eliminate tax evasion, to strengthen the state, the law, to promote professional ethics in cooperation with Relevant sectors as well as the private sector.
The General Department of Customs and Excise is the main operator of the Royal Government in collecting taxes on all goods exported and imported into Cambodia. Currently, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia is managed by Dr. Kun Nhim.
