(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has announced that in 2021, the Royal Government will not increase the salaries of civil servants in the Armed Forces, and in 2022, it will not be possible to increase them. 19 The more the economic income increases, the Royal Government will increase the salary in 2023.
It should be informed that the suspension of the salary increase for civil servants and the armed forces for two consecutive years because Cambodia has suffered from the crisis of the spread of Kovid 19 since the end of 2019, which has affected the national economy. .
On the occasion of the inauguration of the Administration Building of the General Department of Customs and Excise on December 23, 2021, Samdech Techo Prime Minister requested the understanding and tolerance of civil servants and the Armed Forces for the inability to increase salaries in 2021 until 2022.
Samdech Techo stated that, however, the Royal Government has made efforts to maintain macroeconomic stability, curb inflation, maintain the purchasing power of the Cambodian Riel in order to keep the price of goods in the country from rising too high, which will seriously affect the lives of officials. Government and the Armed Forces. The meaning of the prince is "if not increase the salary, but do not let the price of goods go up too much."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also called on civil servants and the Armed Forces of all levels of administration to participate in tax collection to increase the national economy and lead to an increase in the salaries of all civil servants and the Armed Forces.
(Kampong Cham): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, this morning, December 23, 2021, confirmed that the Ministry of Interior does not equip the United States National Armed Forces with some national police forces. These units are old weapons left over from the war.
In an interview with reporters after the commemoration of the 16th accident in Cheung Prey district, Kampong Cham province, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also confirmed that in the case of the American gun is a pistol that the police bought. Private to use for work only.
Please be informed that the statement made by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng is not different from the statement made by Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, who said that the weapons of the United States that are now in Cambodia are the remaining old weapons. At the bottom of the warehouse since the Lon Nol era, the current Cambodian government has never bought the youngest weapon in the United States.
Speaking in an interview with reporters after the groundbreaking ceremony for the actual shooting range at the Phnom Chum Reak Reay Military Police Center in Kampong Chhnang province on Friday morning, December 17, 2021, Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh confirmed that the army is now gathering And US weapons inspection.
The Cambodian Minister of Defense added that until now, the US weapons left over from the war were in poor health, unusable, and even more catastrophic for use.
Please be reminded that on December 10, 2021, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, ordered all armed units to immediately review US weapons and military equipment and, if any, to be retained. Store in a warehouse or dispose of as needed.
The order comes after the United States, through its Office of Industry and Security, unilaterally announced further sanctions on the Cambodian government by restricting the sale of arms and military equipment to Cambodia for geopolitical reasons.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the United States for helping to confirm that Samdech's decision not to buy weapons from the United States was right for Cambodia's defense policy, and it was also a warning message to Cambodians who control the next generation of government. "If you want to be independent in the field of defense, do not use American weapons."
So far, neither the Ministry of Defense nor the Ministry of Interior has released a report that could confirm the number of US weapons in Cambodia.
