Former Thai Foreign Minister Kasit Piromya has recently spoken out against plans for a Cambodian head of government to visit Myanmar. Mr. Kasit Phirum said that the visit was trying to turn ASEAN's efforts against the coup leader of Myanmar in vain.
In his speech today, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia asked the critics, "What is the goal?" Are you reaching this goal of removing Myanmar from ASEAN? Samdech stated, "You answered directly to me what your goal is, but another person said, 'Mr. Hun Sen to Myanmar seems to recognize the administration that came out of the military coup, I just ask you, your country. Is the embassy detached from Myanmar? ”
He added that ASEAN must not have only nine countries, if ASEAN has only nine countries, ASEAN will fail. "I will strive to bring ASEAN 9 back to ASEAN 10. As I chair ASEAN, I would like to declare that as long as ASEAN 9 is not enough, ASEAN should not work like this." He added that all countries have retained their embassies in Myanmar, and Myanmar has also maintained its embassies in ASEAN.
"So I went as the Prime Minister of Cambodia as well as the chair of ASEAN, because it is too difficult to send a mission to the chair of ASEAN. Who are we going to talk to? ” He said that Myanmar needs to increase mutual trust.
Samdech further stated, "One of our problems is to bring ASEAN back to ASEAN unity, because ASEAN loses unity. If ASEAN is only 9, how can it be called ASEAN Central or ASEAN Solidarity?" "As the chair of ASEAN in 2022, we need to make ASEAN 10 again. It is not possible for ASEAN 9 to be a dangerous habit and it will break ASEAN at once. Secondly, we contribute to the implementation of the five-point consensus."
He said that although Myanmar has not yet reached its goal of holding elections in August 2023, the facilitation phase has its stages, such as the cessation of violence as the key to protecting human life. Samdech hopes that friends and ASEAN partners or observers of the political situation understand the work we need to do, "If not talk to the leader, who to talk to?"
