(Phnom Penh): The Working Group for the Management, Distribution and Supply of Strategic Medicines for Combating Kovid-19 has issued a notification on the distribution of Molnatris (Molnupira Vaccap 200 mg) from December 23. This year 2021 will continue at the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications. This is according to the announcement received by Fresh News.
In order to continue to help prevent the spread of Kovid-19 in a timely manner and build a truly strong community immunity against the Kovid-19 pandemic, the team imported Molatris (Mol). Nupiravapazul 200 mg) for mild to moderate Kovid-19 in adults.
This medicine will be distributed at the price of US $ 55 per dose (1 dose is equal to 1 can contains 40 tablets) from Thursday, December 23, 2021 to private hospitals, clinics, pharmacies, sub-pharmacies and the public under the following conditions: Under:
* Individuals have the right to order from 5 to 10 doses * Private hospitals, clinics, pharmacies and sub-pharmacies have the right to order from 10 to 200 doses (must have a business license) and can resell no more than $ 65 per dose * Private hospitals, clinics, pharmacies, sub-pharmacies and the public can re-order at least 2 weeks after the last order.
Private hospitals, clinics, pharmacies, sub-pharmacies and the public can order Molnatris directly at the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications at 13 Monivong Blvd., Srah Chak, Daun Penh, every working hour from Monday to Friday.
