Russia violates WTO commitments through import bans and policies
The remarks by the US Trade Representative were aimed at restricting the import of agricultural products and imposing a ban on Russian imports.
Reuters reports, citing an annual USTR report submitted to the US Congress on Russia's WTO subversion, in which USTR officials said Russia would launch a system in 2021. Keep track of the distribution of goods through the supply chain and maintain restrictions on the import of unscientific agricultural products.
A USTR official said in the report: "Over the past year, Russia has resumed its economic performance by deviating from WTO guidelines on non-discrimination, free trade and predictable transparency. And fair competition. ”
"Russia maintains restrictions along the border measures, imposes restrictions on imports in the country to curb trade and implements an industrial policy that is more likely to be driven by import-restriction guidelines and measures," the official said. "Various coercive measures in the country."
The USTR said the United States was concerned about Russia's actions and would "use all appropriate means to address this issue and maintain Russia's open market for US exports."
Minister of Commerce: Cambodia-Vietnam border trade agreement will improve the lives of border people
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, said that the agreement on border trade between Cambodia and Vietnam will be implemented in 2022. The minister expressed optimism that the agreement would improve the lives of people living along the border.
Negotiations to establish a border trade agreement between Cambodia and Vietnam have been concluded and a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) was signed between the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia and the Ministry of Industry and Trade of Vietnam on December 21, 2021 between Mr. Pan Sosak. Minister of Commerce of Cambodia and Mr. Tran Kok Khanh, Deputy Minister of Industry and Trade of Vietnam.
The signing ceremony was held at the Peace Palace under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc, Head of State of Vietnam.
Mr. Pan Sosak told Fresh News that the Cambodia-Vietnam border trade agreement, which will be signed and implemented in 2022, is to establish a legal framework and bilateral mechanisms to support trade activities. The karma that people live along the border has been done together for a long time.
"This agreement will promote the establishment of markets, rich trading systems, trade facilitation and promote legitimate trade activities, support services for cross-border trade, exchanges," he said. "Market information, problem-solving mechanisms that may occur eventually, etc."
According to Mr. Pan Sosak, after receiving the approval of the National Assembly of each country, the two countries will have provincial and national mechanisms to promote the implementation and resolution of disputes.
Minister Pan Sosak expressed optimism that the border trade agreement will improve the lives of people living along the border between the two countries. The agreement will also contribute to strengthening friendship, cooperation and comprehensive relations, establishing links for sustainable development, stability and long-term development for both sides, and creating favorable conditions for the two sides' businesses.
KUALA LUMPUR, Sept. 22 (Xinhua) - The Malaysian Health Authority on Wednesday reported 3,140 cases of Kovid-19 infection in the last 24 hours. This is according to a release by the Xinhua news agency.
Three District Governors in Kampong Chhnang Province After Tonle Sap Invasion
(Phnom Penh): Three district governors in Kampong Chhnang province, including Boribo, Kampong Leng and Choul Kiri districts, have been replaced by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Pursuant to the Royal Government Sub-Decree signed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on December 22, 2021, it was decided to terminate the position of Mr. Yim Sarin from Boribo District Governor, replaced by Mr. Cheng Chandona, and terminate the position of Mr. Hay Monorom from the District Governor. Chulkiri was replaced by Mr. Dov Kimsing and Mr. Sam Chanthorn was removed from the post of Kampong Leng District Governor and replaced by Mr. Yem Leakena.
In the sub-decree, it was decided to transfer the duties of Mr. Yim Sarin and Mr. Hay Monorom to work in Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration instead. Separately, the former governor of Kampong Leng district, Mr. Sam Chanthorn, who has reached retirement age, is currently serving as the chairman of the CPP committee in Kampong Leng district.
It is unknown at this time what he will do after leaving the post. What is noteworthy is that the exchange took place after the three districts were encroached upon and occupied several hectares of flooded forest land in the Tonle Sap Lake.
Pursat Women's Association donates US $ 3,500 to the Cambodian Red Cross to help build houses for poor Cambodian veterans in Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, would like to express his deep gratitude to the Pursat Women's Association for donating US $ 3,500 (three thousand five hundred US dollars) to the Cambodian Red Cross. To contribute to the construction of 628 houses for 628 poor Cambodian veterans in Bun Rany Sen Chey village, Damnak Troyeung, Prongel commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province.
Please note that each house has a size of 5 meters X 7 meters, metal components, concrete pillars, smart walls, galvanized roof and back of the house as a kitchen, which costs $ 3,500. A separate toilet costs $ 270. General Department of Taxation promotes the implementation of VAT on e-commerce transactions to more than 1,000 business owners
