(Phnom Penh): Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs and Chair of the National Committee for the Promotion of Social Morality, the Values of Women and the Khmer Family, stated that the promotion of the social ethics, values of women and the Khmer family cannot be implemented by any ministry or institution. A separate one.
This statement was made on the occasion of Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi's meeting to review the results of work to promote social morality, women's values and the Khmer family in 2020-2021 and the direction of 2022 at the Phnom Penh Hotel on December 22. 2021.
Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi stated that "Promoting social morality, the values of Cambodian women and families and the elimination of social inactivity is a complex social education work that cannot be carried out by any ministry or institution. "Separately."
In this regard, Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi would like to say that we need to work together to address the legislature, the executive, the judiciary, development partners, civil society, the private sector, as well as all people.
Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi added that with this, the work of social morality is a work that involves changing the attitudes as well as the mindset of the people and a work that can not be done in a hurry and achieve success in a short time. .
She stressed that this work requires time, combined with the common vision of society, as well as high commitment from all walks of life at all levels, by continuing to promote social morality, the values of women and the Khmer family, which are factors contributing to equity, environment, welfare, family and society. .
He emphasized that the purpose of this meeting was to review the progress, challenges and lessons learned from the implementation of the work to promote social morality, women's values and the Khmer family in 2020-2021 and to continue the work direction for 2022.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng and Leaders of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce Attend a Workshop on the Implementation of Value Added Tax on Electronic Business Transactions
(Phnom Penh): Neak Oknha Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, on the morning of December 22, 2021, participated in a seminar on the implementation of value added tax on e-commerce transactions through video. Zoom Online is chaired by Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and a Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Taxation.
The workshop was also attended by the Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, members of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, relevant officials of the General Department of Taxation, speakers and 800 online remote participants.
The purpose of this workshop is to introduce a mechanism for the implementation of value-added tax on digital goods and digital services e-commerce for use in the Kingdom of Cambodia and to be supplied by non-resident taxpayers who do not have a permanent institution in Cambodia. .
The scope of this workshop is applicable to the supply of digital goods or digital services electronically or to all e-commerce activities conducted by non-resident suppliers outside of Cambodia.
Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Inaugurates Administration Building of General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The 35-storey Administration Building of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia will be officially inaugurated on Thursday, December 23, 2021, under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The unit resumed operations on July 13, 1979 under the auspices of the Ministry of Commerce. However, it was transferred under the supervision of the Ministry of Economy and Finance through a sub-decree dated March 11, 1988. The Customs and Excise Office was established as the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia (ACC) through a sub-decree dated September 15, 2008.
* Propose policies related to international trade exchanges, draft regulations related to the collection of taxes and duties on all types of export-import duties. In particular, consider the construction and implementation of customs tariffs and procedures related to customs and excise work on all types of goods in accordance with each stage of national and international economic development.
* Participate in the preparation of the annual national budget to be included in the draft law on finance for each annual management, perform other duties as determined by the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia has the following missions: To be responsible for managing, inspecting and collecting taxes, duties and other fees on exported or imported goods in accordance with the provisions of the Customs Law and other relevant laws and regulations. And export-import, circulation and warehousing.
In particular, for the five years from 2014 to 2019, the growth rate of taxes and duties collected by the General Department of Customs and Excise was an average of 19.5% annually, making the revenue figure in 2019 almost doubled. Revenue collected in 2014.
