Cambodia is closer to exporting directly to the Chinese market as the risk assessment takes place in the first week of January 2022
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia's lentils are getting closer to exporting directly to China for the first time as the risk assessment will take place in the first week of January 2022. This is according to the press release on the progress of the negotiations to open the market of Cambodian longan to the People's Republic of China of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, obtained by Fresh News on December 22, 2021.
For more information on this process, the public can contact the General Department of Agriculture of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the national competent body responsible for negotiating the opening of agricultural markets (plants and plant products) to the country. Including China by calling 012 325 558 and 012 533 647.
Please be informed that in the past, Cambodian gourd was exported to China by companies of neighboring countries only due to hygienic conditions, which makes it impossible for Cambodia to export gourd directly to China. Myanmar: Minority Armed Forces Want International Help to Create 'No-Flight Zone' As Fighting Continues
Nay Pyi Taw: Myanmar's oldest ethnic armed group is urging the international community to help establish a "no-fly zone" near the Thai border after they warned Clashes with Myanmar military forces have been putting innocent people at risk of air strikes. This was released by Reuters on Wednesday evening, December 22, 2021.
Fighting has recently escalated between the Myanmar military and the Karen ethnic armed group (KNU), forcing thousands to flee to Thailand. According to Thai authorities, about 3,400 people have fled there recently, while thousands more are stranded on the border with Myanmar.
Last November, the UN Security Council in a rare statement, unanimously approved by all 15 members, expressed concern over the violence in Myanmar and called on the Myanmar military government. Act with the utmost patience.
