Ministry of Labor Announces Outcome of NagaWorld Labor Dispute Resolution Meeting
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on the evening of December 22, 2021, announced the results of the meeting to resolve labor disputes at NagaWorld Limited today.
In accordance with the spirit of the meeting at Phnom Penh Capital Hall on December 21, 2021, the meeting agreed to continue to resolve the demands of 360 employees of NagaWorld Limited who have not yet agreed to accept payment. Terminate the employment contract in each case.
In this regard, in order to continue to resolve this dispute in accordance with the laws and procedures in force, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has issued invitations to all 360 workers and their representatives to resolve from 9:00 am. December 22, 2021 at the Ministry.
A statement from the Ministry of Labor stated that as of 4 pm, a worker came to attend and informed the Ministry that it agreed to accept the solution from the company and was ready to inform the company tomorrow, and this morning the Ministry met With the representatives of the workers to check the calculation of compensation of the previous employer.
The Ministry claims that it continues to wait for workers who agree to accept the conditions agreed at the previous meeting at Phnom Penh Capital Hall and continue to meet with workers' representatives to discuss various work.
The Ministry of Labor also called on workers and trade unions, as well as employers, to cooperate with the ministry and the competent authorities to end the dispute rather than strike, which affects the interests of all parties involved.
The Ministry affirms that it continues to protect the legitimate interests of workers and employers and continues to strive to resolve labor disputes for workers every day from 9:00 am in accordance with their duties and responsibilities. Until the dispute is resolved in accordance with the laws in force. The United States finally approves injections to prevent HIV for the first time!
Ms. Chea Serey: SMEs play an important role in supporting economic growth and improving people's livelihoods
Ms. Chea Serey made the remarks at the 8th Annual Macroeconomic Conference on "Challenges and Policies for the Development of Small and Medium Enterprises in Cambodia" organized by the National Bank of Cambodia on December 22, 2021.
According to Chea Serey, small and medium enterprises account for about 99 percent of the total enterprises and account for nearly 60 percent of GDP and more than 70 percent of employment.
However, she said that previous studies have shown that SMEs in Cambodia face many business challenges as obstacles to sustainable development. These challenges include: Lack of management skills and skilled labor, Lack of sources of capital and access to official finance, Lack of information on local and export markets, competition from large enterprises, and imports of goods from Foreigners and so on.
Regarding the challenges of the SME sector, Mr. Lim Oun, Director General of the Bank for Small and Medium Enterprises in Cambodia, presented three key conditions for small and medium enterprises to implement to facilitate access to finance from banking and microfinance institutions. .
He said SMEs still find it difficult to apply for loans from microfinance institutions and banks to save their businesses, and most of the SMEs that do not receive this financing do not register their businesses.
He said that some small and medium enterprises have the ability to expand their business, have the ability to repay, but the problem of not being able to get a loan due to lack of collateral for this issue, please encourage the use of corporate credit guarantee. (CEC) that will meet the needs and problems of this mortgage.
He added that recently, the Cambodian Credit Guarantee Corporation has been active and good, working with various commercial banks to provide services to customers who wish to borrow from partner banking institutions can accept this service.
The building was first built temporarily for visitors to the World's Fair in 1889 and to celebrate the 100th anniversary of the French Revolution. The Eiffel Tower has three levels where you can buy tickets to see the view from the top by taking the stairs and the elevator. Inside the building there are post offices, museums, souvenir shops and shops.
During the construction, there was a lot of criticism of the shape of the tower as a work of art, built by just crossing the iron up and down, without any scientific principles.
Later, in 1909, the Eiffel Tower was used as a radio transmission center and continues to this day. It is considered a symbol of Paris and a major tourist destination in France. US warns of less time for resumption of Iran nuclear talks
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - US negotiator Rob Malley said on Tuesday that there were only a few weeks left to salvage a nuclear deal with Iran if Tehran resumed its nuclear activities. Body in the current momentum. This was released by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, December 22, 2021.
"It depends on the momentum of their nuclear program," Malley, the US special envoy for Iran, told CNN. If they slow down or stop, we will have more time. "But if they continue at the current moment, we will have only a few weeks left, no more to restore the deal."
An agreement called the JCPOA, first reached in 2015, eased sanctions on Iran in exchange for restricting Tehran's nuclear program, which has been placed under strict UN scrutiny. But former US President Donald Trump has decided to re-impose sanctions, prompting Iran to begin abolishing the agreement in 2019.
