(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that some Western countries are repeatedly calling for "democracy" and "human rights" and have spent all their energy Body on preventing countries that do not follow their example.
This statement was made by Dr. Kin Phea at the International Conference on "China's Role in the 21st Century and China's Relations with ASEAN" on the morning of December 22, 2021.
On that occasion, Cambodian international relations experts said that the West has always tried to hide its failures and internal turmoil by shifting all blame to other countries such as China and Cambodia.
"What kind of political procedures and rules are there in the political system and the laws of the state, and are those political systems and laws really enforced?" "Are the rules and procedures for the exercise of power democratic and, more importantly, the exercise of power under the control and restraint of the people?" This is an additional question by Dr. Kith Phea.
A senior official of the Royal Academy of Cambodia underlined: "Cambodia is fed up with the war, Cambodia is fed up with the superpowers, let us go, so we have to find a strong position in this competitive landscape, we can not just play the role ahead of them. That no. ”
"Of course, great power sings sweetly on peace, democracy, human rights. We do not deny this is a delicacy of the people, but sometimes the song is broken if we do not prepare." This is the additional confirmation of Dr. Yong Pov.
