Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement is a Good Opportunity for Cambodia
China's agreement to buy agricultural products directly from Cambodia and the signing of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement, which will enter into force in early 2022, is a good opportunity for Cambodia because the Chinese market is a big market. With a population of over 1.4 billion, China is also one of the world's largest importers of agricultural products. Stepping into the Chinese market is a great opportunity for the Cambodian government, the private sector and farmers.
At the same time, meeting the requirements to export goods directly to China will also provide good preparations for Cambodia to take advantage of some other free trade agreements that will enter into force in the near future. Face, too.
In conclusion, we can not expect that China's permission for Cambodian agricultural products to enter the Chinese market and the entry into force of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement will allow Cambodian agricultural products to flow into the Chinese market spontaneously. Smoothly, all stakeholders must work together to address the challenges to allow Cambodia to take full advantage of this opportunity.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth: Although the events of February 20 have ended, be careful to ensure the openness of the country and the economy
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, presided over the launching ceremony of the "Strategic Framework and Program for Restoration and Promotion of Economic Growth" on December 22, 2021. "Cambodia to live with Kovid-19 on a new normal path for 2021-2023."
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth said, "This important document is the basis and a roadmap for the implementation of the Royal Government's specific strategies and actions in the near and medium term, aimed at restoring and promoting growth. "Cambodia's economy is returning to its growth potential, and in other words, to strengthen resilience for sustainable socio-economic development and the environment in the long run."
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth said that during the past two years of the Kovid-19 crisis, we can all clearly see the negative consequences of this crisis on the socio-economic situation in Cambodia. In addition to threatening and taking the lives of the people, the crisis has exposed some of the fragile points of Cambodia's economic base that are vulnerable to external factors.
Indeed, the disruption of supply and production chains, as well as the decline in demand for Cambodian products after the introduction of health and administrative measures by countries around the world is a testament to that. Shows that the stability of the sector, which is the key to Cambodia's economic growth, is closely related to regional and global economic trends.
In fact, Cambodia's agricultural sector has been able to maintain a steady and strong growth and has helped absorb some of the suspended workforce from other sectors. This shows that agriculture is still a strong sector of economic growth that the Royal Government must continue to pay attention to further development and industrialization to achieve the growth potential of this sector.
(Phnom Penh): The Inter-Ministerial Commission for Leading, Monitoring and Evaluating the Implementation of the National Employment Policy 2015-2025 Shows Progress and Achievements Achieved in 2020 After Joint Approval at the First Meeting 6 this morning, December 22, 2021.
Key developments in policy implementation in 2020 include:
Maintain macroeconomic stability despite disruption due to the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
* Approved 195 new qualified investment projects and 43 production expansion projects that can create about 151,000 jobs.
* Develop plans and strategies for attracting targeted investment.
* Introduced tax incentives and tax incentives to facilitate priority areas affected by the Kovid-19 outbreak.
* Modernized reform of business registration, payment of public services and registration of fully automated registration system through the Information Technology Nursery (CamDx).
* Launched an action plan to modernize the technical and vocational education and training system 2019-2023.
* Collected and disseminated labor recruitment information from 184,808 sources.
* Prepared a report on labor market updates.
Provides career and career counseling services to 6,238 job seekers.
* Reformed the labor inspection system and set up a joint data management system related to the labor sector.
* Increased minimum wage on a regular basis for workers in the textile, garment and footwear industries.
* Studied in expanding the labor market abroad, especially in developed countries with good working conditions and high wages, as well as strengthening the mechanism to protect Cambodian workers abroad through the Deputy Attorney General in charge of labor at the Cambodian Embassy and the Consular Officer of the Embassy. Cambodia is also in the target countries.
