(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, emphasized that the close relationship between China and ASEAN has contributed significantly to the rights and interests of the country's development, increasing mutual understanding and trust, including Promoting peace and stability in the region.
Dr. Kin Phea made the remarks at the International Conference on "China's Role in the 21st Century and China's Relations with ASEAN" on the morning of December 22, 2021.
According to Dr. Kin Phea, despite the 199 outbreak of Kovid, ASEAN is still China's largest trading partner and still maintains the momentum of growth. During Kovid 19, China played a key role in fighting regional and global epidemics and accelerating economic recovery.
