(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan provided about 10 vehicles worth $ 245,215 to the Ministry of Environment. Garbage collection vehicles will be deployed in 10 provinces in Cambodia to improve waste collection services.
The signing ceremony for the garbage truck was held last week between Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia and Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment. Garbage collection vehicles in Cambodia's provinces are under a grant scheme for a small-scale humanitarian security project of the Japanese government called "Kusanoni Grant".
With the development of the economy, Cambodia has been struggling with the increase in waste due to the lack of facilities for proper garbage collection. The provision of garbage collection vehicles will contribute to the protection of public health and the natural environment, which will improve the quality of life of more than 530,000 people in the ten target provinces.
Mr. Say Sam Al is optimistic that in the next five years, Cambodia will definitely become a new face with a better environment. The Minister thanked the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia for this important support and is always ready to cooperate with the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia and further support to the Ministry of Environment.
