(Phnom Penh): Undersecretary of State for the Ministry of Economy and Finance Kong Mary said that digitalization was important for businesses in Cambodia during the Kovid-19 crisis, which was key to supporting economic development, accelerating economic growth and building resilience. Cambodia after the Kovid 19 outbreak.
The senior official made the remarks at the launch of Meta's report on "Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises and the Use of Digital Functions during the Kovid-19 Outbreak" at the Hyatt Hotel in Hyderabad. December 21, 2021.
"The digitalization of businesses is key to supporting economic development, accelerating economic growth and building resilience in the aftermath of an epidemic," he said. The Ministry will continue to work closely with Meta and its programs and other stakeholders to support this important mission to fully achieve Cambodia's digital transformation in the coming years.
Nearly half of all small and medium-sized enterprises (MSMEs) in Cambodia use digital functionality for their business activities, while most Cambodian online businesses see functionality, according to a new report released by Meta. These were important values in running their business during the Kovid-19 crisis.
The report, which is available both online and in print, also found that micro, small and medium enterprises in Cambodia have increased their use of digital functions by about 10 percent to operate their businesses during an epidemic. Kovid-19, with 36 per cent of businesses surveyed reporting the use of digital functions for pre-Kovid businesses, compared with 45 per cent a year ago.
The survey is part of a comprehensive study of small and medium enterprises (MSMEs) using new survey data from global business leaders in South America, South Asia and the Middle East. Southeast Asia.
