Former Malaysian Prime Minister Mahathir Modi will be released from hospital in a few days.
Mahathir, now 96, who also had a heart condition, was admitted to hospital last Thursday for a thorough medical examination. The hospital, as well as Mahathir's spokesman, did not specify why he was taken to hospital.
Mahathir became the longest-serving Malaysian prime minister, serving 22 years from 1981 to 2003. He returned to power in 2018 after leading a coalition of opposition political parties to a historic victory that made him the world's oldest head of government.
