The new administrative building of the National Assembly, which is currently holding the groundbreaking ceremony, will be built on an area of 27 meters wide and 49 meters long, 12 stories high, starting from the first floor below. But under the 12-storey building, two more car parks have been built that can accommodate an additional 260 vehicles.
