Russia on Monday said it urgently needed a response from the United States over its security assurances, and Moscow has again warned against military action unless it sees fit. Political activities that help alleviate security concerns. This was released by Reuters on Tuesday, December 21, 2021.
Russia has released a proposal for security guarantees that it wants to negotiate, including the promise of a security crackdown on Western nations last week near the Ukrainian-Ukrainian border. NATO will abandon all military action in Eastern Europe and in Ukraine.
Washington has said some points in Russia's proposal are "unacceptable" but stressed that the United States will respond this week with clearer information on the form of possible talks.
