More than 350,000 poor people and vulnerable children have access to clean water from the World Vision Water and Sanitation Project
(Phnom Penh): In 2021, more than 300,000 poor people and more than 50,000 vulnerable students and children will have access to clean water from the World Vision Water and Sanitation Project.
World Vision is implementing this water and sanitation project in 24 target districts in Kratie, Battambang, Kampong Speu, Kampong Thom, Kampong Chhnang, Preah Vihear, Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap and some areas in Phnom Penh.
World Vision's goal is to ensure that children grow up healthy and that their families have access to safe drinking water.
By 2025, World Vision wants to achieve two goals:
* First, 500,000 people will have access to clean drinking water and sanitation equipment. * Second, more than 100,000 school children will have access to safe drinking water and sanitation equipment.
During this Christmas, Olympia Shopping Mall organized a charity fair called "Christmas Fair Contributes to Changing the Lives of Cambodian Children" to raise funds for the construction of a water well for the benefit of nearly 400 primary school students in Kampong Chhnang Province.
We hope that the participation of all of you will contribute to the development of every child and ensure that people across the country, especially vulnerable children, have access to clean water and avoid diseases caused by scarcity. Clean water.
