Pros car owner sues Tabui for 3 offenses, demanding $ 100,000 in compensation for refusing to pay more than $ 2,000 for repairs, and the proceeds from the lawsuit will be donated to Kantha Bopha Hospital
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khi Hong alias Tabui was sued by the owner of a bus to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on 3 counts and demanded $ 100,000 in damages. The complaint was filed with the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on Monday, December 20, 2021. This is according to a complaint received by Fresh News today.
Immediately after the incident, the two sides reached an agreement, with the drunken Tabui side promising to pay for the car repair to the victim. But the next day, when the victim showed $ 2,250 to repair the car, Tabui refused to take responsibility, accusing it of being overpriced and posting on Facebook accusing the car owner of profiteering.
The fact that Ta Bui refused to take responsibility for the car repair fee and posted the accusation on the part of the car on Facebook also made the car party angry and filed a lawsuit in court.
According to the complaint, Huy Maing, a lawyer representing the victim, was taken to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to describe some of the activities prior to the incident. The complaint details:
According to the complaint, the victim tried to drive away from the perpetrator but could not escape until the scene, where the victim decided to stop the car and run away from the car for fear of danger. To death, suddenly, the perpetrator drove the car and hit the victim's car from behind in a rage. After the collision, the perpetrator opened the window and shouted insults and threatened to kill the victim again.
The complaint states that after the action, the perpetrator drove away from the scene, when the victim chased the car until it stopped the offender car on the Boulevard of the Russian Federation. Railway fence. At that time, the perpetrator got out of the car drunk, soft hands, soft feet, talking without knowing right from wrong.
The victim decided to sue Mr. Khi Hong, also known as Ta Bui, for three offenses: driving while intoxicated, driving while intoxicated and defamation.
The victim sued for $ 100,000 in damages. According to the victims, the money from this lawsuit will be donated to Kantha Bopha Hospital.
Mr. Nguyen Suon Fuc's visit to Cambodia at the invitation of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
According to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, during the state visit, Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc will pay homage to His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni at the Tev Vinich Hall and pay homage to His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej. Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, the Queen Mother of Cambodia, is the most revered at the Kantha Bopha Palace in the Royal Palace.
In addition, Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc will have a separate meeting with Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. After the working meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, some important documents will be signed.
The President of Vietnam will preside with Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin at the groundbreaking ceremony for the new administration building at the National Assembly.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs considers that Nguyen Suon Fuc's state visit to Cambodia will continue to strengthen and deepen bilateral relations in the spirit of good neighborliness, traditional friendship, comprehensive cooperation and peace. Long-term stability between the two countries for the mutual benefit of the people of the two countries.
Nguyen Suon Phuc was elected President of the National Assembly to replace Nguyen Phu Trong on Monday, April 5, 2021. Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc served as Prime Minister from 2016 to 2021.
It should be noted that Cambodia and Vietnam were connected on June 24, 1967, but this relationship was severed in March 1970. In January 1979, after Cambodia was liberated from the Pol Pot genocidal regime, relations between Cambodia and Vietnam re-established. In March 2005, the two countries' relations were upgraded to "traditional good-neighborly relations with strong, long-lasting and comprehensive cooperation in all fields."
Through this good relationship, the leaders of Cambodia and Vietnam often exchanged trips. Nguyen Suon Phuc also visited Cambodia in April 2017 when he was Prime Minister of Vietnam.
Based on this good cooperation, Cambodia and Vietnam have always supported each other on various difficulties. Especially during the 19 epidemic of Kovid, both countries supported each other in the fight against Kovid 19. Vietnam has provided about $ 320,000, plus a series of medical equipment to Cambodia. Separately, Cambodia also provided a total budget of about $ 350,000, as well as many other medical equipment to Vietnam.
On October 29, 2021, Cambodia also provided the Vietnamese government with 200,000 doses of 19 types of Kovidin syphilis vaccine to Vietnam.
In terms of investment, from 1994 to September 2021, Vietnamese investment in Cambodia was 88 projects with a total capital of approximately $ 2.56 billion. For the first 10 months of 2021, Vietnamese investment in Cambodia amounted to about 89.4 million US dollars. Cambodia implements new 400,000 tonnes rice export quota provided by Chinese friends
(Phnom Penh): The new export quota of 400,000 tons of rice provided by the Chinese friend will start from December 2021, with a period of 17 months.
Oknha Hun Lak, Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Rice Federation, told Fresh News that a new 400,000-tonne quota agreement was signed in November 2021, and exports will be implemented from December onwards. Set a specific period of 17 months. At the same time, both Cambodia and China have agreed to expand the quota to 500,000 tons.
The leader of the Rice Federation continued, "The quota of Chinese rice import quotas from Cambodia has helped boost the development of Cambodia's rice sector." "From 2014 to 2021, the Chinese friend has already provided six quotas."
China has become an important market for Cambodia's rice exports. In recent years, China has been the number one buyer of rice from Cambodia.
