At a seminar last weekend on the development of the garment and textile sector, executives of companies in the industry said that two months after the resumption of operations, their main concern now is the lack of manpower. Labor costs, raw material costs, and Kovid-19 disease prevention costs.
Logistics costs have risen sharply since the outbreak. Companies are now worried that labor shortages will delay production and distribution, and to ensure timely delivery of goods, they may have to ship high-cost products by air.
She said only one-fifth of customers agreed to include part of the cost of Kovid-19 prevention in the unit price.
