International Analysis: Joe Biden, from president with tidal support, becomes president without tidal support
SINGAPORE: Joe Biden defeated Donald Trump in the 2020 US presidential election by a landslide, when he began his presidency in early January 2021. His share is up to 57 percent.
But now Biden's approval rating has plummeted to just 43 percent, and 71 percent of Americans think their country is on the wrong track. What is the reason for Mr. Biden, who received the support of the tsunami, to fall in popularity like a dam?
* Biden's Economic Management
Another major issue that has made Biden unpopular is the management and handling of economic issues. The economy is considered to be one of the main factors that can determine the fate of the US president in the election. During the election campaign, most Americans thought Donald Trump was better able to handle economic issues than Biden.
It should be noted that Mr. Joe Biden has already stated his intention to run for another presidential term in 2024. But some experts say it is difficult for Biden to win again as his foreign policy, especially the defeat in Afghanistan, continues to haunt him and the image of America as a world leader.
