It should be noted that after the groundbreaking ceremony, the Governor of Kampong Cham Province and his team inspected the construction site of another road, which is a project of the Ministry of Rural Development, from Pak Nam Commune, Koh Sotin District to Prek Sandek Commune, bordering Prey Veng Province. Foreign Ministry issues official statement on Vietnamese President's two-day state visit to Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The new President of Vietnam Nguyen Xuan Phuc will pay a two-day state visit to Cambodia from December 21-22, 2021, according to a statement issued by the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs. This afternoon, December 20, 2021.
The President of Vietnam will arrive in Cambodia on Tuesday morning, December 21, 2021 at the invitation of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
During the state visit, Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc will pay homage to His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia at Tevavinich and pay homage to Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother. The Khmer nation is the highest place of worship at the Kantha Bopha Palace in the Royal Palace.
The President will preside over Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin at the groundbreaking ceremony for the new administrative building in the National Assembly and with Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen at the signing ceremony of a number of important documents.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs considers that the state visit of Mr. Nguyen Suon Fuc to the Kingdom of Cambodia will continue to further strengthen and deepen the bilateral relations in the spirit of good neighborliness, traditional friendship, and comprehensive cooperation. And long-term peace and stability between the two countries for the mutual benefit of the people of the two countries.
Deputy Prime Minister Men Sam An thanked the benefactors for their contribution to humanitarian work in Svay Rieng province.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of December 20, 2021, Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, received a generous donation from philanthropists with 8 tons of rice and 250 cases of noodles to help the people. Shortage in Svay Rieng province.
Through Ms. Hun Sinath, who brought the gifts directly, Ms. Men Sam An also promised in front of the donors that they would give these gifts to the needy people directly without disappointing the donors. .
On that occasion, Ms. Men Sam An also expressed her deep gratitude to the benefactors who donated their wealth to join the Royal Government, especially to help humanitarian work, as well as to help people who are experiencing difficulties in Svay Rieng.
Investment in the construction sector in the first 11 months of 2021 is more than 5 billion dollars
(Phnom Penh): Investment in the construction sector in the first 11 months of 2021 is worth more than 5 billion dollars, while throughout November, construction projects increased by more than 300 projects. This is according to Mr. Lao Tip Seiha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction.
Investment in the construction sector from January to November amounted to 5,210,359,509 US dollars, an increase of more than 300 million US dollars, while from January to October, investment in this sector was approximately 4,876,804,899 US dollars.
Proposed projects include commercial buildings, market buildings, hotels, residential buildings, condominiums, flats, multi-functional buildings, industrial plants.
Phan Phalla, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Economy and Finance, recently said that the Kovid 19 crisis has not significantly affected the real estate sector in 2021, as the sector is still doing well. The real estate sector is one of three sectors that will drive Cambodia's economic growth in 2021.
"The real estate sector has seen better growth this year compared to the same period in 2020," he said. "Obviously, for this year, despite the 19 Kovid crisis, the real estate sector is still active, with many housing estates continuing to flow and everywhere."
From 2005 to the first 11 months of 2021, the construction of high-rise buildings from 5 floors up to more than 2,375 buildings, of which more than 666 high-rise buildings in Sihanoukville.
90 members elected in Hong Kong parliamentary elections
Of the 90 members of the Hong Kong Parliament, 40 are elected by the Election Commission, while 30 are nominated by special interest groups and 20 are elected by the people themselves.
This is the first Hong Kong parliamentary election after China improved the electoral system in Hong Kong under the principle of "patriots rule Hong Kong." Drugs cracked down in Kampong Speu
(Kampong Speu): The competent authorities of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes cracked down on drug trafficking, arrested a Cambodian man and confiscated more than 1 kg of drugs in Kampong Speu Province.
This operation took place on December 18, 2021 at 17:30, the specialized force of the Anti-Drug Department (A4) led by Major General Kheng Sarath, Deputy Director of the Anti-Drug Department, attended the Provincial Police. Kampong Speu, with the coordination of Ms. Chat Sorasmey, Prosecutor of Kampong Speu Provincial Prosecutor's Office, investigated and cracked down on Sovankiri village, Khtom Kraing commune, Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province.
The results of the arrest of a suspect named Men Vichekar, male, 19 years old, Cambodian, and the evidence seized methamphetamine (ICE) weighing 1385.49 grams.
At present, the suspects and the seized exhibits have been sent to the Kampong Speu Provincial Court to continue the procedure.
